rary of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aSphygmomanometers12aBlood Pressure Determinationxinstrumentation 2aAddress2 aHomœopathic Medical Society of the State of New York.tTransactions.2 aNew York Society for Medico-Scientific Investigation,eformer owner.  aAUTH02276cgm a22004814a 101322944DNLM20260227152238.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u071207s2007    mdu067|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14118  a(OCoLC)192041978  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2671 aShamamian, Peter.10aEndothelial lineage cells in cancer :ba potential target for green tea derived catechins /cPeter Shamamian.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNCI OCCAM monthly lecture series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Feb. 12, 2008).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 7 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 10, 2007.3 a(CIT): The NCI's Office of Cancer Complementary and Alternative Medicine (OCCAM) invites you to view its monthly lecture series.  With the goal of informing the National Cancer Institute (NCI) community about the variety of ongoing research in cancer and complementary and alternative medicine (CAM), NCI's Office of Cancer Complementary and Alternative Medicine (OCCAM) has created a monthly lecture series on cancer CAM. These hour long lectures, occurring from 10 a.m. - 11 a.m. on the second Wednesday of each month, will feature a fifty minute presentation on a cancer CAM topic and allow ten minutes for questions.   For more information, visit  http://www.cancer.gov/cam/news/monthly-lecture-series.html.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxdrug therapy22aCamellia sinensisxchemistry22aCatechi