ppropriate to seek or waive consent for studies when pediatric donors reach the age of majority. Confusion about ethical and legal obligations and the complicated logistics of re-contacting pediatric donors and/or their families have plagued pediatric investigators despite the potential for advancing scientific knowledge, diagnostic capability, and therapeutic practice.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aInformed Consentxethics22aBiological Specimen Banksxethics22aChild22aHuman Experimentationxethics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bBiospecimen Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17193  aAUTH00957cam a22002897i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118245012100151250001400272264005400286300003100340336002600371337002800397338002700425490003400452650001700486650002200503651001000525655002400535710006500559830003400624999000900658101592501DNLM20260205120427.0961230s1956    cc a   j      000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdad20260205dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1803 no.1800aZhuo ma que qu /cFen nian yue du xiao cong shu bian ji wei yuan hui bian zhu ; Zhang Zhifan, Wang Tong deng hui tu.  aDi 1 ban. 1aShanghai :bShao nian er tong chu ban she,c1956.  a19 pages :billustrations.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aFen nian yue du xiao cong shu12aRural Health22aSocial Conditions 2aChina 2aJuvenile Literature2 aFen nian yue du xiao cong shu bian ji wei yuan hui,eeditor. 0aFen nian yue du xiao cong shu  aAUTH01387cas a2200457   0417466DNLM20260227090911.0cr||||||||||||740618c19609999ja mr         0    0jpno   a0009-918Xl0009-918X  aRISHD  a(DNLM)R49780000(s)z(DNLM)C26040000(s)  a(OCoLC)04301256  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Japan00aW1bRI2167R10aRinsho Shinkeigaku2dnlm00aRinshō shinkeigaku =bClinical neurology.30aClinical neurology  aTo