- The curability of epilepsy and the proportion of such cases. Factors that determine prognosis -- The colony of small homes community plan of providing state care for epileptics. Notes on location, size, physical features, water, sewage, industries, education, classification of colonists, size of homes, cost to construct and maintain, & c. -- The situation in Alabama.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202505082pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202505085DNLM12aEpilepsy22aHousing22aIndependent Living22aPersons with Disabilities 2aUnited States1 aLetchworth, William Pryor,d1823-1910,ededicatee.  aAUTH01819cgm a22004694a 101268228DNLM20260227150214.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2003    mdu049 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11552  a(OCoLC)71233026  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWK 5151 aWray, Susan.10aFrom nose to brain :bthe road to reproduction /cSusan Wray.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed July 12, 2006).  aStreaming video (48 min., 51 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded July 1, 2003.3 a(CIT): 2003 Summer Lecture Series for Students  Research at the Frontier   Susan Wray, Ph.D.  Chief, Cellular and Developmental Neurobiology Section  National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke  For more information, visit the Office of Intramural Training and Education.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aGonadotropin-Releasing Hormone22aBrainxembryology22aCell Movement22aNeuronsxcytology22aNeurosecretion22aOlfactory Pathwaysxembr