 prevent and treat post-acute sequelae of SARS-CoV-2 (PASC), including what is commonly called Long COVID or long-haul COVID. This Listening Session will help the RECOVER initiative to hear from and better understand affected communities" experiences, needs, and priorities, and will set the stage for hosting listening sessions in the future.  Dr. Amy Patterson, NIH, Dr. Walter Koroshetz, NIH, Dr. Lenora Johnson, NIH, Dr. Andrea Lerner, NIH and Alissa Gallagher, NIH.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed January 27, 2022).22aNIH RECOVER (Initiative)12aCOVID-19xcomplications22aCOVID-19xdiagnosis22aCOVID-19 Drug Treatment22aHealth Services Accessibility22aBiomedical Research22aSocioeconomic Factors 2aUnited States 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNIH RECOVER (Initiative),esponsoring body,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=42174  aAUTH01841cas a2200553 a 8708560DNLM20260227091022.0cr|cn#||||||||870723c19829999oncqr p       0    0eng    acn 83030647   a0714-9808l0714-9808  zCJAGE  a(DNLM)SR0057180(s)  a(OCoLC)09586298  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aengafre  9Canada00aW1bCA624P10aCan J Aging2dnlm 0aCanadian journal on aging00aCanadian journal on aging =bLa revue canadienne du vieillissement.13aCJA/RCVfMar. 1986?-31aRevue canadienne du vieillissement30aCJA30aRCV  aMaple, Ont. :bCanadian Association on Gerontology,c[1982-3 3<2004- > :aCambridge, UK :bCambridge Press  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1/2-  aFrench parallel title on cover precedes the English title, spring 1994-1 aMEDLINEbv23n1, spring 2004-0 aPubMedbv23n1, spring 2004-1 aIndex medicus  aSupplements accompany some numbers.  aAlso issued online.  aArticles chiefly in English, some in Fren