the impact of TSD on military and veteran families and caregivers across deployment, homecoming, and reintegration. The conference will examine the needs of families and caregivers in support of military and veterans with TSD, factors related to family functioning and reintegration, and effective approaches that facilitate treatment of trauma disorders and services to families and caregivers, paying particular attention to gender and health disparities. Next steps will be developed for addressing research concerns identified at the conference.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aBrain Injuriesxpsychology12aStress Disorders, Post-Traumaticxpsychology22aCaregiversxpsychology22aFamily Relations22aFamilyxpsychology22aMilitary Personnelxpsychology22aVeteransxpsychology 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15502  aAUTH01347cas a22004334a 101178411DNLM20260227090924.0m        d        cr|cn ||||||||030513c20039999enkuu pss     0    0eng    a  2003243272  a1478-7954l1478-7954  a(OCoLC)52384322  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9England10aW110aPopul Health Metr2dnlm00aPopulation health metrics.  aLondon :bBioMed Central,c[2003]-  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, issue 1 (2003)-  aTitle from home page (viewed May 21, 2003).  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 1, issue 6 (2003) (viewed May 21, 2003).1 aMEDLINEbis v14, 2016-0 aPubMedbv1n1, 2003-0 aPMC  aArticles added on a continuous basis.  Each article constitutes a new issue.  aMode of access: Internet.12aHealth Status Indicators22aBiometry22aHealth Status 2aPeriodical40uhttps://pophealthmetrics.biomedcentral.com/40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101178411  aAUTH02196cas a2200565 a 9806357DNLM20260224111546.0cr|cn ||||||||980423c19989999ne  x p       0||| 0eng    asn 98047222   a1387-1307l1387-1307  a