cience research studies.  Session Topics will include: The rational for including male and female subjects in studies; the impact of including or not including sex as a basic biological variable; practical methods to integrate the biological variable "sex" into research projects; and how to cultivate a culture of "Sex Matters" across multiple disciplines.  The workshop will include presentations from Dr. Lawrence Tabak, Deputy Director, NIH and Dr. Lawrence Cahill, Professor, University of California, Irvine.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed Nov. 25, 2014.12aBiomedical Research12aSex Factors22aWomen's Health 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Research on Women's Health,esponsoring body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18686  aAUTH01652cas a2200481   7807107DNLM20260227090956.0cr|cn#||||||||780907c19789999nyu x p       0    0eng    a0161-4754l0161-4754  zJMPTD  a(DNLM)J28120000(s)  a(OCoLC)03957827  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bJO748F10aJ Manipulative Physiol Ther2dnlm 0aJournal of manipulative and physiological theraputics00aJournal of manipulative and physiological therapeutics.13aJMPT  aLombard, Ill.,bNational College of Chiropractic.2 31999- :aSt. Louis, MO :bMosby, Inc.31aNew York, NY :bElsevier Inc.  av.bill.  aNine no. a year,b1990-  aQuarterly,b1978-1986  aBimonthly,b1987-1989  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-    Mar. 1978-1 aMEDLINEb1982-1 aPubMedb1982-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 18, no. 1 (JAN 1995)c19950518fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paperxFurther review is required to determine exactly when acid-free paper was first used for this title 2aChiropractic 2aPeriodical2 aNational College of Chiropractic.0 x1532-65864 uhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-manipulative-and-