76DNLM20260227164909.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u241002s2024    mdu639|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:35225  a(DNLM)CIT:35227  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWQ 1052 aGlobal Implementation Science Approaches to Improve Maternal Heart, Lung, Blood, and Sleep Health Outcomes (Workshop)d(2024 :cOnline)jauthor.10aGlobal implementation science approaches to improve maternal heart, lung, blood, and sleep health outcomes. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (10 hr., 39 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded September 16 & 17, 2024.3 a(CIT): Workshop Objectives: Explore the maternal health crises in the US in the context of health disparities and HLBS disorders that impact maternal mortality and morbidity. Use global successes including in high-income countries (HICs) and low- and middle-income countries (LMICs) to determine how contextually adapt evidence-based practices to improve maternal health in vulnerable populations both in the US and abroad. Explore challenges and opportunities for advancing implementation research, training, and capacity-building for maternal health with a focus on HLBS disorders that impact pregnant women and mothers in the U.S. as well as LMICs. Discuss the importance of engaging the community in maternal health research and programs to improve the health of mothers in the perinatal and postpartum period. Facilitate reciprocal learning and sharing of insights between global and domestic settings to foster innovative solutions and co-learning opportunities that enhance maternal HLBS health outcomes. Identify knowledge gaps and critical unmet needs and uncover opportunities for improving maternal HLBS health outcomes using implementation science both domestically and globally.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed February 23, 2026).12aMaternal Health22aImplementation Science22aHealth Status Disparities22aEvidence-Based Medicine22aOutcome and Process Assessment, Health Care 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5514540uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=55146  aAUTH01634cgm a22004934a 101267954DNLM20260227145913.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2001    mdu071 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11105  a(OCoLC)70326846  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 5901 aSchinke, Steven Paul.10aSmoke signals :bboy and woman bear /cSteve Schinke.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2001]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed June 30, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 10 min., 52 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Sep. 6, 2001.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aHealth Education22aAdolescent22aComputer-Assisted Instruction22aDiet22aIndians, North American22aProblem Solving22aRisk Reduction Behavior22aSmoking Cessation22aTobacco Use Disorderxprevention & control 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11105  aAUTH01187cas a22004094a 101083101DNLM20260227090908.0cr|cn ||||||||001106c20019999moutr p       0    0eng    a   00213059 0 a1532-3382l1532-3382  a(OCoLC)45288621  aNSDcNSDdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9United States00aW1bJO644CVQ10aJ Evid Based Dent Pract2dnlm04aThe journal of evidence-based dental practice.3 aJournal of evidence based dental practice  aS