from screen banner (viewed Apr. 18, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 3 min., 5 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 23, 2000.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aSpinal Cordxembryology22aCell Differentiation22aGene Expression Regulation, Developmental22aHomeodomain Proteins22aMotor Neurons22aTranscription, Genetic 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10904  aAUTH02414cgm a2200469 a 101578535DNLM20260227154107.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120215s2012    mdu304|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17101  a(OCoLC)785706133  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 26.52 aBioinformatics & Computational Biosciences Festivald(2012 :cBethesda, Md.)10aBioinformatics in the cloud :b2012 Bioinformatics & Computational Biosciences Festival.1 a2012 Bioinformatics & Computational Biosciences Festival  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 4 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Feb. 2, 2012.3 a(CIT): The NIAID Office of Cyber Infrastructure and Computational Biology (OCICB) welcomes all NIH researchers to its 2012 Bioinformatics and Computational Biosciences Festival. The theme of this year's festival is Bioinformatics in the Cloud. The primary goal of the festival is to start a discussion about cloud computing at NIAID and to educate NIH researchers on the value of cloud computing as it relates to bioinformatics. This full day festival will feature presentations by subject matter experts from government agencies, academia, and the IT data management industry. Presentations will touch on issues such as: How might NIAID comply with federal regulations? Which cloud options in the scientific arena could be exercised? How might cross-Institute collaborations benefit from the use of cloud and its economies of scale?.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aComputational Biology22aFederal Government22aGovernment Agencies22aInformation Dissemination22aInformation Storage and Retrieval22aInterinstitutional Relations 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17101  aAUTH01848cas a2200517 a 9318425DNLM20260227091016.0cr#un#||||||||931118c19819999ja  x p       0||| 0jpn    a0389-5564l0389-5564  a(DNLM)SR0065676(s)  a(OCoLC)10316681  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 ajpnaeng  9Japan00aW1bGE13387 0aGeka to taisha, eiyō00aGeka to taisha, eiyō :bNihon Geka Taisha Eiyō Gakkai, Kanzen Jōmyaku Eiyō Kenkyūkai kikanshi = The Japanese journal of surgical metabolism and nutrition.30aJapanese journal of surgical metabolism and nutrition30aSurgical metabolism and nutrition  aTōkyō :bNihon Geka Taisha Eiyō Gakkai,c1981-3 aTokyo :bNihon Geka Taisha Eiyo Gakkai  av. :bill.  aFive no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 15, no. 1 (1981-nen 2-gatsu)-  aQuarterly.  aTitle from cover.  aAlso issued online  aText chiefly in Japanese with some in English; summaries in English.  aContinues: Jutsugo Taisha Kenkyūkai shi.22aNihon Geka Taisha Eiyō Gakkai.22aKanzen Jōmyaku Eiyō Kenkyūkai (Japan) 2aMetabolism 2aNutritional Physiological Phenomena 2aPostoperative Complicationsxmetabolism 2aPeriodical2 aNihon Geka Taisha Eiyō Gakkai.2 aKanzen Jōmyaku Eiyō Kenkyūkai (Japan)0 x2187-515410tJutsugo Taisha Kenkyūkai shi4 uhttps://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/browse/jssmn/  aAUTH01203cas a22004334a 101254060DNLM20260227090920.0cr|cn ||||||||050729c20069999sz br p       0    0eng    a  