aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government.  aOpen-captioned.12aProgeriaxcomplications12aProgeriaxgenetics22aAging22aCardiovascular Diseasesxcomplications 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13190  aAUTH02554cgm a22004334a 101507159DNLM20260227153704.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090605s2009    mdu111 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15052  a(OCoLC)423570828  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aBF 637.N661 aGoldin-Meadow, Susan.10aAdministrative strategies - body language :blet me hear your body talk! /cSTEP - Staff Training in Extramural Programs.30aBody language :blet me hear your body talk  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed June 26, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 50 min., 8 sec. : sd., col.).  aAccess restricted to HHS.5DNLM  aRecorded Apr. 23, 2009.3 a(CIT): STEP - Staff Training in Extramural Programs  Overview You may be surprised to learn how loudly you speak without words. Understanding body language in the workplace isn"t just a game -- it"s a career necessity. When you are speaking with others, can you assess their interest levels, determine if they are responding truthfully, recognize when they are in disagreement, or identify their emotional responses? More to the point, are they reading your body language and adjusting the conversation accordingly? Facial expressions, postures, gestures, touch, and use of personal space are all under-appreciated aspects of how we communicate. Come and explore the world of body talk! Learn how to read others and select your own body language. This training is recommended for ESA credit.  Speakers: Dr. Susan Goldin-Meadow, University of Chicago</li> <li>Dr. Curtis LeBaron, Brigham Young University, Dr. John Stern, Washington University St. Louis. Organizing Committee Blaine Moore (Chair), Marina Broitman, Chris Hatch, Kelli Marciel, Lisa Moeller, Eduardo Montalvo, Dick Okita  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aKinesics22aInterpersonal Relations 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bStaff Training-Extramural Programs Committee.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15052  aAUTH01692cgm a22004814a 101294865DNLM20260227151559.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu066|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13314  a(OCoLC)84716045  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWF 6581 aBunn, Paul A.10aEGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitor for lung cancer :bpatient selection and methods to overcome primary resistance /cPaul A. Bunn Jr.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 12, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 6 min. : sd., col.).  aAccess restricted to HHS and NIH only.5DNLM  aRecorded June 27, 2006.3 a(CIT): Center for Cancer Research - National Cancer Institute Grand Rounds.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aLung Neoplasmsxdrug therapy12aLung Neoplasmsxgenetics22aDrug Resistance, Neoplasm22aErbB Receptorsxantagonists & inhibitors22aErbB Receptorsxgenetics22aPatient Selection22aProtein Kinase Inhibitorsxtherapeutic use 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13314  aAUTH01493cas a2200481   8000151DNLM20260227090950.0cr|cn#||||||||791220c19799999pauqr p       0    0eng    a   83642039 zsc 80000292 zsn 79000463  a0194-7648l0194-7648  zJLMDB  a(DNLM)J27510000(s)  a(OCoLC)04997813  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  ansdp  9United States00aW1b