019]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (58 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aRecorded March 27, 2019.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 14, 2020).12aCerebral Palsyxrehabilitation22aExoskeleton Device22aRobotics.22aWalking22aChild 2aWebcast 2aLecture1 aBulea, Thomas C.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aClinical Center grand rounds40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=31598  aAUTH02484cgm a2200421 i 101635873DNLM20260227154644.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u140627s2014    mdu053|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18479  a(OCoLC)884541052  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWB 8901 aNahin, Richard L.eauthor.14aThe blind men and the elephant :bsurvey perspectives of complementary health approaches /cRichard L. Nahin. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (53 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aAt head of title: National Center for Complementary and Alternative Medicine (NCCAM).  aAccess restricted to HHS only.5DNLM  aRecorded June 9, 2014.3 a(CIT): This program provides overviews of the current state of research and practice involving complementary health therapies, and explores perspectives on the emerging discipline of integrative medicine. Richard Nahin, Ph.D., M.P.H, is NCCAM's Senior Advisor for Scientific Coordination and Outreach. Dr. Nahin's talk will discuss the use of complementary health approaches. Trying to get a complete picture of the use of complementary health approaches is analogous to the story of the blind men and the elephant.  Looking at only one aspect of use does not give you the true picture.  This lecture illustrates this point by giving examples from a variety of data, including surveys of the public and health professional, marketing/sales data, data from the NCCAM Clearinghouse, data from professional associations, insurance data, Google trends data, and structured interviews.  Selected complementary health approaches will be examined with trends over time highlighted.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed July 3, 2014.12aComplementary Therapies 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aNational Center for Complementary and Alternative Medicine (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18479  aAUTH01886cas a2200481 i 101682214DNLM20260227090926.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||160209c20149999su || poo     0    0eng    a  2016243450  a947075010  a2352-2429l2352-2410  a(OCoLC)927018728  z(OCoLC)947075010  aLUNbengerdad20260227cLUNdAU@dOCLCFdCUSdDNLM  apcc  9Saudi Arabia00aW100aJournal of dermatology & dermatologic surgery.1 aJournal of dermatology and dermatologic surgery1 aJDDS 1a[Riyadh, Saudi Arabia] :bKing Saud University; production and hosting by Elsevier B.V. on behalf of King Saud University,c[2014]-  a1 online resource  aSemiannual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 18, Issues 1/2 (January/July 2014).  aNumbering from content page.  aDescription based on: Volume 18, Issues 1/2 (January/July 2014); title from cover image (publisher's Web site viewed Nov. 16, 2016).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 20, Issue 2 (July 2016) (viewed Nov. 16, 2016).12aDermatologic Surgical Procedures.12aSkin Diseases 2aPeriodical2 aSaudi Society of Dermatology and Dermatologic Surgery,eissuing body.2 aJāmiʻat al-Malik Saʻūd,epublisher.0 x2352-241000tJournal of the Saudi Society for Dermatology and Dermato