uerrerio. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2019]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (49 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aRecorded October 30, 2019.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 9, 2020).12aLoeys-Dietz Syndromexcomplications22aLoeys-Dietz Syndromexgenetics22aEosinophilic Esophagitisxetiology 2aWebcast 2aLecture1 aGuerrerio, Pamela,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aClinical Center grand rounds40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=34959  aAUTH00787cam a22002537i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118245010900151250001400260264005300274300001400327336002100341337002500362338002300387650003600410650002100446651001000467710004700477999000900524101607409DNLM20260209100400.0130502s1970    cc            000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdad20260209dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1773 no.1500aChuan ran xing gan yan de fang zhi /cZhongguo ren min jie fang jun 109 yi yuan, Hong qiao yi yuan bian.  aDi 1 ban. 1aShanghai :bShanghai ren min chu ban she,c1970.  a22 pages.  atext2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier12aHepatitisxprevention & control22aHealth Education 2aChina2 aZhongguo ren min jie fang jun 109 yi yuan.  aAUTH03542nam a2200421 i 9918986632506676DNLM20260227075816.0231025t20252025njua     b    001 0 eng    a  2023548056  a9780826139160q(paperback)  a0826139167q(paperback)  z9780826139177q(ebook)  a(OCoLC)1405843816  aYDXbengerdacYDXdBDXdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCLdIBIdOCLCOdDLCdPZFdIG#  apcc  9United States 4aRT73.7b.O47 202500aWY 1804a610.73qOCoLC223/eng/202311201 aOermann, Marilyn H.,eauthor.10aEvaluation and testing in nursing education /cMarilyn H. Oermann, PhD, RN, ANEF, FAAN, Kathleen B. Gaberson, PhD, RN, CNOR, CNE, ANEF, Jennie C. De Gagne, PhD, DNP, RN, NPD-BC, CNE, ANEF, FAAN.  aSeventh edition. 1aPrinceton, New Jersey :bSpringer Publishing,c[2025] 4c©2025  axiii, 384 pages :billustrations ;c26 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.1 aPart 1: Concepts of assessment -- Assessment and the educational process -- Qualities of effective assessment procedures: Validity, reliability, and usability -- Part 2: Testing and other assessment methods -- Planning for testing -- True/false and matching -- Multiple-choice and multiple-response -- Short-answer (fill-in-the-blank) and essay -- Assessment of higher level learning and clinical judgment -- Test construction and preparation for students for Next Generation NCLEX and Certification examinations -- Assessment of written assignments -- Part 3: Test construction and analysis -- Assembling, administering, and scoring tests -- Testing and evaluation in online courses -- Test and item analysis: Interpreting test results -- Part 4: Clinical evaluation -- Clinical evaluation -- Clinical evaluation methods -- Simulation and objective structured clinical examination for assessment -- Part 5: Issues related to testing and evaluation in nursing education -- Social, ethical, and legal issues -- Grading -- Program evaluation and accreditation.  aThe resource presents an expanded discussion on assessment of higher-level learning and clinical judgment, new content on assessment of competencies, examples of new item types in all chapters, updated information on online testing, more in-depth explanations of how to analyze and score NGN items with examples, and new content on evaluating students in online nursing programs. Also unique to this edition is practical advice on developing test blueprints and creating all types of test components including NCLEX-type items and the Next Generation NCLEX. The text continues to present fundamental measurement and evaluation concepts to aid current and future nurse educators in designing, critiquing, and employing pertinent test and evaluation tools along with guidance for evaluating instructor and program effectiveness. It also examines key social, ethical, and legal issues associated with testing and evaluation, including prevention of cheating and designing academic policies for testing, grading, and progression.12aEducation, Nursing22aEducational Measurementxmethods22aTeaching1 aGaberson, Kathleen B.,eauthor.1 aDe Gagne, Jennie C.,eauthor.  aAUTH01688cas a2200457 i 9918419176206676DNLM20260227090918.0m     o  d        cr#|||||||||||210711c20209999gw || poo     |    0eng    a  2022229150  a1273685115a1298433101  a2719-4523l2719-4523  a(OCoLC)1262670582z(OCoLC)1273685115z(OCoLC)1298433101  aVT2bengerdad20260227cVT2dOCLCFdUEJdDNLM  apcc  9Germany00aW110aRheumatol Immunol Res2dnlm00aRheumatology and immunology research. 1a[Berlin, Germany] :bDe Gruyter Open Access,c[2020]-  a1 online resource  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1, issue 1 (December 2020).0 aPubMedbv1n1, Dec. 2020-0 aPMC  aVolume 1 complete with one issue.  aSearch interface in English and German.0 aVolume 1, issue 1 (December 2020); title from the journal home page (publisher's website, viewed October 25, 2022).1 aVolume 3, issue 3 (October 2022) (viewed October 25, 2022).12aRheumatic Diseases22aImmune System Phenomena 2aPeriodical2 aNational Clinical Research Center for Dermatological and Rheumatologic Diseases of China,eissuing body.40uhttps://www.degruyter.com/journal/key/rir/html40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=9918419176206676  aAUTH01885cgm a2200457 a 101595178DNLM20260227154337.0m        z f      