 of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (10 hr., 32 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 18 & 19, 2024.3 a(CIT): The NEI OCT Symposium directly supports the NIH mission by facilitating a scientific exchange of the OCT technology and its more recent advances. This meeting will bring together ~300 participants with the expertise needed to address the specific goals below:<p><ul><li>Participants will talk about development of OCT technology and its most recent advances</li><li>Biological and clinical applications of OCT and its modifications</li></ul></p>.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed June 27, 2025).12aTomography, Optical Coherencexmethods22aDiagnostic Techniques, Ophthalmologicalxinstrumentation22aEye Diseasesxdiagnostic imaging22aEyexdiagnostic imaging 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Eye Institute,eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5430040uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=54317  aAUTH00751cam a22002537a 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032020001800073020001500091040002100106044001200127060001100139245009800150250001300248260005100261300004200312336002600354337002800380338002700408650002200435700003100457999000900488101285109DNLM20260206080130.0060728s2006    gw a     b    001 0 ger    a9783437240904  a3437240900  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Germany00aQT 26100aSportverletzungen :bDiagnose, Management und Begleitmassnahmen /cMartin Engelhardt (Hrsg.).  a1. Aufl.  aMünchen :bElsevier, Urban & Fischer,c2006.  axiv, 834 p., xvi p. of plates :bill.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aAthletic Injuries1 aEngelhardt, Martin,d1960-  aAUTH01299cas a2200421 a 101222433DNLM20260227090915.0cr|cn ||||||||040623c20049999enkbr p       0    0eng    a  2004243477  a1745-039Xl1477-2817y0003-942X  a(OCoLC)55800628  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9England00aW1bAR266J10aArch Anim Nutr2dnlm00aArchives of animal nutrition.  aAbingdon, Oxfordshire, U.K. :bTaylor & Francis  av. :bill.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with: Vol. 58, no. 1 (Feb. 2004).  aDescription based on: Vol. 58, no. 3 (June 2004); title from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv58n1, Feb. 2004-0 aPubMedbv58n1, Feb. 2004-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.12aAnimal Nutritional Physiological Phenomena22aAnimal Feed 2aPeriodical0 x1477-281700tArchiv für Tierernährungx0003-942Xw(DLC)sn 83003984w(OCoLC)14820264 uhttps://www.tandfonline.com/loi/gaan20  aAUTH02347cgm a2200385 a 101512277DNLM20260227153116.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090801s2009    mdu268|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15232  a(OCoLC)432239842  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWS 350.8.P42 aInteragency Autism Coordinating Committee (U.S.)10aInteragency Autism Coordinating Committee /cIACC.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (4 hr., 28 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded July 15, 2009.3 a(CIT): The Interagency Autism Coordinating Committee (IACC) coordinates all efforts within the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) concerning autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Through its inclusion of both Federal and public members, the IACC helps to ensure that a wide range of ideas and perspectives are represented and discussed in a public forum.  The IACC mission is to: <li> Facilitate the efficient and effective exchange of information on ASD activities among the member agencies <li> Coordinate ASD-related activities <li> Increase public understanding of the member agencies' activities, programs, policies, and research by providing a public forum for discussions related to ASD research, screening, education, and interventions </li> IACC meetings are open to the public and include presentations and discussions about member activities and projects of the IACC. The meetings also include scientific presentations from investigators in the field of ASD research. A portion of each meeting is reserved for public comment. A summary of each meeting is posted on the meetings & events page of the IACC website.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aChild Development Disorders, Pervasive 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15232  aAUTH01630cas a2200445 i 101666399DNLM20260227090917.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||150819c20159999ne || poo     |    0eng    a  2015247819  a2405-5263l2405-5255  a(OCoLC)926108512  aDNLMbengerdad20260227cDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9Netherlands00aW110aOsteoporos Sarcopenia2dnlm00aOsteoporosis and sarcopenia. 1a[Amsterdam] :bThe Korean Society of Osteoporosis ; production and hosting by Elsevier B.V.,c[2015]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1, Issue 1 (September 2015).0 aPubMedbv2n1, Mar. 2016-0 aPMC  aNumbering from content page.  aDescription based on: Volume 1, Issue 1 (September 2015); title from issue table of contents page (ScienceDirect website, viewed October 23, 2015).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 1, Issue 2 (December 2015) (viewed Mar. 11, 2016).12aOsteoporosis12aSarcopenia 2aPeriodical2 aAsian Federation of Osteoporosis Societies,esponsoring body.2 aTaehan Koltakongjŭng Hakhoe,eissuing body.0 x2405-525540uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/2405525540uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101666399  aAUTH01