romoting implementation science research and potential dissemination of impactful food security research interventions.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed May 22, 2023).12aFood Insecurity22aMalnutrition22aGlobal Health 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aFogarty International Center,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=46301  aAUTH02250cgm a2200541 i 9918573157206676DNLM20260227163317.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230302s2023    mdu453|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32974  a(DNLM)CIT:32975  a(DNLM)CIT:32979  a(DNLM)CIT:32980  a(OCoLC)1417059609  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 704.62 aAnnual NIH HEAL Initiative Investigator Meetingn(4th :d2023 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aAnnual NIH HEAL Initiative Investigator Meeting 2023 (day 1 & 2) /cNIH HEAL Initiative. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (4 streaming video files (7 hr., 33 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 21 & 22, 2023.3 a(CIT): The NIH HEAL Initiative(r) will bring together HEAL funded researchers, federal officials, people with lived experience, and other stakeholders to share research findings, explore trends and shared interests, and identify opportunities to advance the goals of the initiative.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed December 27, 2023).12aPain Management22aAnalgesics, Opioidxadverse effects22aNeonatal Abstinence Syndrome22aDrug Overdosexprevention & control22aInformation Dissemination22aCommunity Participation 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNIH HEAL Initiative,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps