onthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Oct. 2010)-  aAlso issued online.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 3, no. 1 (Feb. 2012).12aAnimal Technicians22aAnimal Diseases 2aPeriodical4 uhttp://www.magonlinelibrary.com/loi/vetn  aAUTH01155cas a2200361   7902974DNLM20260227091005.0cr|cn#||||||||790329c19789999dk  x         0||| 0eng    a0106-2301l0106-2301  a(DNLM)S08060000(s)z(DNLM)S36750000(s)  a(OCoLC)04547219  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Denmark00aW1bSC154N04aThe Scandinavian psychoanalytic review.13aSPsaR  aOslo,bUniversitetsforlaget ; New York, distributed in the U. S. by Columbia Univ. Press.3 aCopenhagen :bMunksgaard International Publishers  av.bill.  aTwo no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-    1978-  aPublished under the auspices of the psychoanalytic societies in Sweden, Norway, Denmark, and Finland.  aAlso issued online. 2aPsychoanalysis 2aPeriodical0 x1600-08034 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/toc/rspr20/current  aAUTH02521cgm a22004334a 101531541DNLM20260227153416.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100519s2010    mdu048|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15781  a(OCoLC)642278276  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQW 5731 aHanada, Ken-ichi.13aAn MHC-independent macromolecular ligand for a human tumor-reactive [alpha-beta] T-cell receptor /cKen-ichi Hanada.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (48 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 31, 2010.3 a(CIT): Dr. Ken-ichi Hanada received his MD from the Tokyo Medical and Dental University and completed a residency in Internal Medicine at that University Hospital. He then completed his PhD and post graduate work in the Department of Biochemistry at the University of Tokyo.  He was involved in the identification of the murine hematopoetic stem cell during post-graduate work and as a research member of the Japanese Foundation for Cancer Research.  In 1997 he arrived as an Exchange Scientist in the Surgery Branch, NCI. As a Research Fellow and then a Staff Scientist, he has been involved in studying the cellular immune response to human renal cancer.  In 2004, he published the first description of vertebrate post-translational protein splicing in Nature, when he identified the spliced epitope from a renal cancer antigen recognized by a T-cell.  Now pursuing new T-cell reactivities which can recognize renal cancer, he has elucidated the molecular basis for an unprecedented ligand which can trigger a human alpha-beta T-cell receptor.  The Immunology Interest Group.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aReceptors, Antigen, T-Cell, alpha-betaximmunology22aMajor Histocompatibility Complexximmunology22aMultiprotein Complexesximmunology22aNeoplasmsximmunology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bImmunology Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15781  aAUTH01410cas a2200481 a 9606930DNLM20260227091016.0cr|cn ||||||||960516c19969999sz  x p       0    0eng    a1420-3030l1420-3030  aANEOFO  a(DNLM)SR0085558(s)  a(OCoLC)34703585  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Switzerland00aW1bAU201GM10aAudiol Neurootol2dnlm00aAudiology & neuro-otology.3 aAudiology and neuro-otology1 iIssues for v. 10, no. 3- have title:aAudiology & neurotology3 aAudiology and neurotology  aBasel ;aNew York :bKarger,cc1996-  av. :bill.  aSix no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Jan.-Feb. 1996)-   = 96/1/1-1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan.-Feb. 1996-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan.-Feb. 1996-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online. 2aAudiology 2aHearing