medical scientists, and medical practitioners. Her lecture is the keynote address of Viral Networks: An Advanced Workshop in Digital Humanities and Medical History, which brings together scholars from various fields of medical history whose innovative research shows promise through the use of methods, tools, and data from the digital humanities.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed March 20, 2018).12aPandemics22aClinical Laboratory Techniques22aHemorrhagic Fever, Ebolaxepidemiology22aInfluenza A Virus, H1N1 Subtype22aInformation Dissemination22aPopulation Surveillance22aZika Virus Infectionxepidemiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aMacPhail, Theresa,d1972-espeaker.2 aNational Library of Medicine (U.S.).bHistory of Medicine Division,esponsoring body.2 aViral Networks : An Advanced Workshop in Digital Humanities and Medical Historyd(2018 :cBethesda, Md.) 0aHistory of Medicine seminar40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?23678  aAUTH01410cas a2200469 a 9506663DNLM20260227091013.0cr|cn ||||||||950420c19959999gw mr p       0    0eng    a   95648296 zsn 95035271  a0948-6143l0948-6143y0301-5564  aHCBIFP  a(DNLM)SR0083808(s)  a(OCoLC)32074894  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Germany00aW1bHI74810aHistochem Cell Biol2dnlm00aHistochemistry and cell biology.18aHistochemistry  aBerlin :bSpringer,  av. :bill.  aMonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 1995.  aDescription based on: Vol. 103, no. 2 (Feb. 1995); title from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv103n1, Jan. 1995-0 aPubMedbv103n1, Jan. 1995-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aOfficial journal of the Society for Histochemistry. 2aCell Biology 2aHistocytochemistry 2aPeriodical2 aSociety for Histochemistry.0 x1432-119X00tHistochemistryx0301-5564w(DLC)   74642853w(OCoLC)17930144 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/418  aAUTH