a(CIT): Please join Dr. Collins in welcoming Senator Barbara Mikulski, Chair of the Senate Appropriations Committee, to the NIH campus in Masur Auditorium, Building 10.  Senator Mikulski, together with her counterpart in the House, Representative Hal Rogers, led the bipartisan compromise that provides support for NIH and the rest of the government for FY14.  She will share the latest news on the Federal Budget and what it means for NIH employees.  As you know, Senator Mikulski is a staunch supporter of biomedical research and a champion for federal workers.  After her remarks, she will take questions from reporters who will be seated in the front row.  aDescription based on version viewed March 19, 2014.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aBiomedical Researchxeconomics22aAnniversaries and Special Events22aBudgets22aPolitics22aUnited States Government Agenciesxeconomics 2aUnited States 2aAddress 2aWebcast1 aCollins, Francis S.,eauthor.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18293  aAUTH01962cas a2200529 a 9000927DNLM20260227091012.0cr||||||||||||900104c19899999enk|| p       0    0eng    asn 89024086   a0792-4259l0792-4259y0168-8170  aIRDEE2  a(DNLM)SR0066157(s)  a(OCoLC)19737364  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aengafre  9England00aW1bIN993VD10aInvertebr Reprod Dev2dnlm 0aInvertebrate reproduction & development00aInvertebrate reproduction & development.30aInvertebrate reproduction and development  aRehovot, Israel :bBalaban : Distributed by International Science Services,cc1989-2 aRehovot :bBalaban in Collaboration with the International Society of Invertebrate Reproduction313<2011-> :aColchester, UK :bTaylor & Francis in association with the International Society of Invertebrate Reproduction & Development  av. :bill.  aSix no. a year  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 