ical2 aSociety for the Psychological Study of Social Issues.0 x1540-456040uhttps://spssi.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/15404560  aAUTH00994cam a22003017i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002100073040003500094044001000129060003200139100003300171245011000204250001400314264005200328300003000380336002100410336003300431337002500464338002300489500005300512650001500565651001000580655001900590700007400609999000900683101606586DNLM20260205121425.0130422s1956    cc a          000 0 chi    a(OCoLC)893183181  aDNLMbengerdad20260205dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1768 no.91 aLin, Qi,d1931-2010eauthor.10aBing jia /cgen ju Lin Qi "Qing le bing jia de ren" yuan zhu ; Guo Yan gai bian ; Guo Yan, Xing Fang hui.  aDi 1 ban. 1aBeijing :bZhao hua mei shu chu ban she,c1956.  a23 pages :billustrations  atext2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier  aAdaptation of: Qing le bing jia de ren / Lin Qi.12aSick Leave 2aChina 2aPictorial Work1 iAdaptation of (work):aLin, Qi,d1931-2010.tQing le bing jia de ren.  aAUTH02426cgm a22004454a 101480532DNLM20260227152624.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080801s2008    mdu056|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14594  a(OCoLC)244264628  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWI 1401 aPowrie, Fionaq(Fiona Margaret)10aImmune regulation in the intestine /cFiona Powrie.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series  aTitle from title screen (viewed Aug. 8, 2008).  aStreaming video (56 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 25, 2008.3 a(CIT): The gastrointestinal tract in humans is colonised by a large number and diverse array of commensal bacteria many of which are beneficial to the host.  Most of reside peacefully with our gut residents however a breakdown in intestinal homeostasis can result in inflammatory diseases of the intestine including inflammatory bowel disease, celiacs disease and allergy.  In this talk I will review recent work from my own laboratory and others that indicate the intestinal homeostasis is a delicate balance between pro-inflammatory effector responses and immune suppressive regulatory T cells.  Analysis of cytokines that drive intestinal inflammation identified IL23 as a master regulator that orchestrates intestinal inflammation via effects on innate cells and T cells. Recent genome wide-association studies have identified polymorphisms in the IL23R as linked to susceptibility to IBD validating IL23 mediated pathways as potential therapeutic targets in IBD.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGastrointestinal Diseasesximmunology22aGastrointestinal Tractximmunology22aGastrointestinal Tractxmicrobiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14594  aAUTH01307cas a22004454a 101094211DNLM20260227090922.0cr|cn#||||||||010423c20019999ne  x p       0    0eng    a  2001243324  a1568-0096l1568-0096  a(OCoLC)48132748  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aeng  alcd  9Netherlands00aW1bCU70910aCurr Cancer Drug Targets2dnlm00aCurrent cancer drug targets.  aHilversum, The Netherlands ;aBoca Raton, FL :bBentham Science Publishers,cc2001-  av.  aEleven issues a year,b2019-  aFrequency varies,b2001-2018  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (May 2001)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, May 2001-0 aPubMedbv1n1, May 2001-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso available online.12aDrug Delivery Systems22aDrug Design22aNeoplasmsxdrug therapy 2aPeriodical0 x1873-55764 uhttp://www.eurekaselect.com/584/journal/current-cance