 8).  aFor marching band and voice.  a32 pages printed on one side, with 2 parts on each page.1 aNatafalusy, Alex.1 aUnited States.bArmy.bMedical Regiment, 1st.  aAUTH02435cgm a2200469 i 9918592675306676DNLM20260227163600.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230429s2023    mdu617|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33100  a(OCoLC)1457225336  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.55.C52 aWorkshop on Inclusive Participation in Clinical Researchd(2023 :cOnline)jauthor.10aWorkshop on inclusive participation in clinical research (day 1 & 2) /cNIMHD, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (9 hr., 77 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 30 & 31, 2023.3 a(CIT): The purpose of this workshop is to improve implementation of evidence-based best practices for inclusive participation in clinical research. This workshop will discuss evidence-based best practices to increase inclusive participation in clinical research, how to implement these practices, challenges to overcome, and lessons learned. Workshop topics are organized by stage in the research process: before the study, during the study, and after the study. Day two will include a special session that will feature representatives from the different entities involved in supporting and conducting clinical research (academia, pharma, community-based organizations, and federal agencies).  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed August 26, 2024).22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aClinical Studies as Topic22aClinical Trial Protocols as Topic22aEvidence-Based Practice22aPatient Selectionxethics22aDiversity, Equity, Inclusion22aHealth Inequities 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Inst