zaz|u210206s2021    mdu172|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31518  a(OCoLC)1248768048  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWS 12500aBreastmilk Ecology: Genesis of Infant Nutrition (BEGIN) meeting series.pWorking group 2,pHuman milk composition /cNICHD, NIH.1 aHuman milk composition 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (2 hr., 52 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded January 29, 2021.3 a(CIT): A deeper understanding of the biology of human milk is essential to address ongoing and emerging questions about infant feeding practices. Human milk is a complex biological system, a matrix of many interacting parts, that is more than the sum of those parts. Its production needs to be studied as an ecology that consists of inputs from the mother, her breastfeeding baby, and their respective environments. The Breastmilk Ecology: Genesis of Infant Nutrition (BEGIN) meeting series is designed to examine this ecology, its functional implications for both mother and infant. The goal is to support the research community"s efforts to ensure safe, efficacious, and context-specific infant feeding practices in the United States and globally.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed April 26, 2021).22aBEGIN (Collaborative Group)12aMilk, Humanxchemistry22aNutritive Value22aInfant Health22aMother-Child Relations22aEcological and Environmental Phenomena22aInfant Nutritional Physiological Phenomena 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aEunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=40152  aAUTH01218cas a2200397 i 101583855DNLM20260227090911.0cr||||||||||||120509c20119999ii || p       |    0eng    a  2013243575  a2230-9748l2230-9748  a(OCoLC)861490407  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9India00aW1bJO736300aJournal of laryngology & voice.1 aJournal of laryngology and voice 1aMumbai :bMedknow Publications and Media Pvt. Ltd.  aSemiannual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with 2011.  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Vol 2, issue 1 (Jan/Jun 2012); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol 2, issue 1 (Jan/Jun 2012).12aLaryngeal Diseases22aVoice22aVoice Disorders 2aPeriodical2 aLaryngology and Voice Association,eissuing body.0 x2231-26924 uhttps://journals.lww.com/jolv/pages/default.aspx  aAUTH01641nam a2200397 i 101754547DNLM20260223082834.0190919r19111911nyu           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5658 no.151 aSolomon, Meyer,cM.D.,eauthor.12aA hurried bird's eye view of the problem of the modern care of the insane /cMeyer Solomon. 1a[New York] :bA.R. Elliott Publishing Company,c[1911?] 4c©1911  a16 pages ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCover title.  a"Reprinted from the New York Medical Journal incorporating the Philadelphia medical journal and the Medical news, April 1, 1911."  a"Copyright, 1911, by A.R. Elliott Publishing Company."--Page 1.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  cGift;aAmerican Heritage Center, University of Wyoming;d1998.5DNLM  aWill digitizec202103022pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202103025DNLM22aGovernment Hospital for the Insane (U.S.)12aPersons with Psychiatric Disorders22aHospitals, Federal22aHospitals, Psychiatric22aMental Disordersxtherapy1 aGlueck, Bernard,d1884-1972,eformer owner.5DNLM0 aNew York medical journal.  aAUTH01396cgm a22004094a