o NIH. She will deliver remarks and answer questions from NIH staff.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed February 27, 2015.22aUnited States.bDepartment of Health and Human Services22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aAcademies and Institutes12aBiomedical Research22aUnited States Government Agencies22aPublic Health 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18817  aAUTH01468cas a22004814a 101201068DNLM20260224111559.0cr||||||||||||031217c20049999oncfr p       0    0eng    a  2004243663  a1612-1783l1612-1783  a(OCoLC)56530392  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9Canada00aW1bCO4272M10aCommun Med2dnlm00aCommunication & medicine.3 aCommunication and medicine  aBerlin ;aNew York :bM. de Gruyter,cc2004-2 32008-2024 :aLondon :bEquinox3132025- :aToronto :bUniversity of Toronto Press  av. :bill.  aThree no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (2004)-  aTitle from cover.  aPlace of publication varies.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, 2004-1 aPubMedbv1n1, 2004-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3v.1, no. 1 (May 2004)c20060630fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper that meets the full ANSI standard for Permanent Paper12aCommunication22aDelivery of Health Care22aEthics 2aPeriodical0 x1613-36254 uhttps://utppublishing.com/loi/cam  aAUTH02483cgm a22004574a 101303655DNLM20260227151954.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070403s2007    mdu068|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13710  a(OCoLC)123962867  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 55.91 aMorimoto, Richard I.,d1952-10aProtein misfolding in aging and neurodegenerative disease /cRichard I. Morimoto.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aFlorence S. Mahoney lecture on aging  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 16, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 8 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 21, 2007.3 a(CIT): Aging and stress, stress and aging - a pair of ominous human conditions that affect the quality of life.  When events go awry, molecular events take place that, over time, can lead to or enhance the risk of neurodegenerative disease.  At the root of problem is a fundamental process common to all cells, protein folding. When proteins misbehave and misfold, however, they can adopt altered states that cause diseases of protein conformation including the neurodegenerative Huntington's disease, Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis, Alzheimer's, Parkinson's and Creutzfeld-Jacob.  For each, a hallmark of the disease is the appearance of misfolded and mutant proteins (Huntingtin, superoxide dismutase, amyloid beta peptide, alpha-synuclein) and associated toxicity. How these proteotoxic species form, the processes that determine their persistence or clearance, and the molecular basis of their toxicity are critical to understanding disease mechanism. WALS.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aProtein Folding22aAgingxphysiology22aNeurodegenerative Diseasesxphysiopathology22aProtein Conformation 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pFlorence Mahoney lecture on aging40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13710  aAUTH01523cas a2200457 a 101312593DNLM20260227090909.0cr|cn#||||||||060504c20079999enkqr p       0    0eng    a  20062146110 a1931-7611l1931-7611  a(OCoLC)68192141  aNSDcNSDdNSDdNOCdCGUdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9England14aBF692b.J6400aW1bJO858B10aInt J Sex Health2dnlm00aInternational journal of sexual health :bofficial journal of the World Association for Sexual Health.  aBinghamton, N.Y. :bHaworth Press,cc2007-3 32008- :a