search and development  aAuckland ;aPhiladelphia :bAdis International,cc1999-3 aAuckland :bAdis, Springer International  av. :bill.  a4 issues a year,b2010-  aMonthly,b1999  aBimonthly,b2000-2008  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 1999)-  aTitle from cover.  aPrint issues ceased with v. 9, no. 6 (2008)1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan. 1999-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan. 1999-0 aPMC1 aIndex medicus  aNone published 2000-2001.  aPublication suspended from 2008-2009.  aAlso issued online.12aDrug Therapy22aDrug Evaluation22aDrug Industry22aDrugs, Investigational22aResearch 2aPeriodical0 x1179-69014 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=1008836474 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/40268  aAUTH01464cas a2200457 a 9100095DNLM20260227091027.0cr|cn ||||||||901206c19909999caumr p       0    0eng    a1044-7431l1044-7431  aMOCNED  a(DNLM)SR0066405(s)  a(OCoLC)19879705  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bMO195B10aMol Cell Neurosci2dnlm 0aMolecular and cellular neurosciences00aMolecular and cellular neurosciences.1 iTitle varies slightly:aMolecular and cellular neurosciencef1995-1 iAt head of title:aMCNf1995-  aSan Diego :bAcademic Press,cc1990-  av. :bill.  aMonthly  aBimonthlyb1990-1995  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Aug. 1990)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv5n1, 1994-1 aPubMedbv5n1, 1994-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 1, no. 1 (AUG 1990)c19950516fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper that meets the full ANSI standard for Permanent Paper 2aNeurosciences 2aPeriodical0 x1095-93274 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/10447431  aAUTH05091cgm a22004934a 101310976DNLM20260227152025.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070703s2007    mdu056 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13892  a(OCoLC)165047546  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2021 aSood, Anil,cM.D.10aNeuroendocrine influences on cancer metastasis /cAnil Sood.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCenter for Cancer Research, National Cancer Institute grand rounds  aTitle from title screen (viewed July 11, 2007).  aStreaming video (55 min., 55 sec. : sd., col.).  aNIH access only.5DNLM  aRecorded June 12, 2007.3 a(CIT): Center for Cancer Research - National Cancer Institute Grand Rounds    Dr. Sood received a B.S. degree from Davidson College in 1986 and M.D. degree from the University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill in 1991. He completed his residency in Obstetrics/Gynecology at Shands Teaching Hospital, University of Florida in 1995 and a fellowship in gynecologic oncology at the University of Iowa Hospitals & Clinics in 1998. He was an assistant professor of Gynecologic Oncology at the University of Iowa from 1998 to 2002. Dr. Sood joined  the department of Gynecologic Oncology at the M.D. Anderson Cancer Center in 2002 and is a physician scientist and Director of Ovarian Cancer Research. He has a joint appointment in the Department of Cancer Biology and maintains a research laboratory where his research focuses on mechanisms of cancer invasion and metastasis in ovarian cancer. Specifically, his research is focused in three main areas: 1) effect of neuroendocrine stress hormones on ovarian cancer growth and progression; 2) development of novel anti-vascular therapeutic approaches, and 3) development of new strategies for in vivo siRNA delivery. Dr. Sood has published numerous peer-reviewed articles and has authored and co-authored several book chapters. His research is funded by the National Cancer Institute and the Department of Defense. Dr. Sood has received major recognition for his research accomplishments including the Hunter Award from the American Gynecological and Obstetrical Society, the James Nolan Research Award and the Gynecologic Cancer Foundation/Margaret Greenfield/Carmel Cohen, MD Excellence in Ovarian Cancer Research Award. Moreover, he has been invited to give multiple presentations at national and international forums. Dr. Sood currently serves on the editorial board for several journals and is a reviewer for many others. He has served on study sections for the National Institutes of Health and the V.A. Merit Review Grants. He is a Fellow in the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists and a Fellow in the American College of Surgeons. He has served and holds membership in several national organizations including the American Association for Cancer Research, American Society of Clinical Oncology, International Gynecologic Cancer Society, Society of Gynecologic Oncologists, Psycho-Neuro-Immunology Research Society, and the Western Association of Gynecologic Oncologists. He is a member of the Gynecologic Oncology Group's Committee on Experimental Medicine.  Dr. Sood is actively involved in teaching graduate students and clinical fellows. He is a member of The University of Texas Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences and teaches classes related to cancer cell signaling pathways. He was the recipient of M. D. Anderson's Outstanding Educator Award in 2003 and the Educator of the Month Award in 2005.    Anil K. Sood, M.D.  Professor, Departments of Gynecologic Oncology and Cancer Biology  Director, Ovarian Cancer Research  Department of Gynecologic Oncology  The University of Texas   M. D. Anderson Cancer Center  Houston, TX   The primary educational objective of these seminars is to provide new information, ideas, and discussion about timely areas of research with impact on the field of oncology.  A secondary educational objective is to elicit participation by individuals from all divisions of the intramural NCI, and thus facilitate more interactions among investigators and groups in the NCI.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasm Metastasisxphysiopathology22aNeovascularization, Pathologicxphysiopathology22aNeurosecretion22aRNA Interference22aStress, Psychologicalxcomplications22aStress, Psychologicalxphysiopathology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aCCR grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13892  aAUTH01460cas a2200481 a 8809466DNLM20260224111548.0cr|cnu||||||||880825c19889999cc br p       0||| 0eng    a0952-5238l0952-5238  aVNEUEY  a(DNLM)SR0061201(s)  a(OCoLC)17700144  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9China00aW1bVI911E10aVis Neurosci2dnlm00aVisual neuroscience.  aNew York, NY, USA :bCambridge University Press,cc1988-3 aJiangsu, China :bMaximum Academic Press  av. :bill.  aBimonthly  aQuarterly,b1988  aMonthly,b1989-1992  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1-  aTitle from cover.  aPrint issues ceased with v. 29 (2011).1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, 1988-1 aPubMedbv1n1, 1988-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso available online.  3Vol. 1, no. 1 (1988)c19920910fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aNeurosciences 2aVision, Ocular 2aPeriodical0 x1469-87144 uhttps://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/visual-neuroscience4 uhttps://www.maxapress.com/vns/journal%5Finformation  aAUTH02187cgs a2200517 i 101773517DNLM20260227090919.0m     o  c        sqr p o     0   a0cr#|||||||||||190501c20199999vau---        o   vleng    a  20192012500 a2643-5217l2643-521721  a(OCoLC)1099573873  aDLCcDLCbengerdad20260227dDLCdDNLM  apccansdp  9United States10aISSN RECORD00aW110a617.4822310aNeurosurg Focus Video2dnlm0 aNeurosurg. focus, Video 0aNeurosurgical focus. Video00aNeurosurgical focus: Video. 1aCharlottesville, Virginia :bAmerican Association of Neurological Surgeons,c[2019]