ärz 1969)-  aTitle from cover.  aPublished: Heidelberg : Hüthig, 1995?- .1 aMEDLINEbv1n2,Jun. 1969-v23n4, 19911 aPubMedbv1n2,Jun. 1969-v23n4, 19911 aIndex to dental literaturex0019-3992bv1n2,Jun. 1969-v23n4, 1991  aAlso issued online. 2aJaw Abnormalities 2aOrthodontics 2aPeriodical4 uhttps://www.thieme-connect.de/products/ejournals/journal/10.1055/s-00000026  aAUTH02234cgm a22004694a 101528447DNLM20260227153716.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100406s2010    mdu082|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15747  a(OCoLC)648077709  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 1201 aNicholson, Jeremy K.14aThe human microbiome-host metabolic axis in health and disease /cJeremy Nicholson.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aStars in nutrition and cancer1 aNCI stars in nutrition lecture series  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (1 hr., 22 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 16, 2010.3 a(CIT): NCI Stars in Nutrition Lecture Series    This lecture will explore: gene-environment interactions; molecular epidemiology of disease risk factors and biomarker discovery; measuring and modeling metabolic profiles and microbial mammalian co-metabolism; and personalized healthcare.   This lecture series features extraordinary contributors or "stars" in the field of cancer and nutrition research. Speakers highlight the important role that nutrition plays in modifying cancer development. The lectures aim to facilitate interdisciplinary interactions among basic scientists, clinicians, and behavioral and social scientists. Lectures typically occur each fall and spring.   For more information, visit  http://prevention.cancer.gov.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aMetabolomicsxmethods22aChemistry Techniques, Analytical22aMetagenomexphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.) 0aStars in nutrition & cancer 0aNCI stars in nutrition lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15747  aAUTH01325cas a2200445   0117605DNLM20260227090917.0cr|cn#||||||||671102c19679999xxuar         0||| 0eng    a   67029891   a0066-4197l0066-4197  aARVGB  a(DNLM)A54105000(s)  a(OCoLC)01481501  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bAN771N10aAnnu Rev Genet2dnlm00aAnnual review of genetics.  aPalo Alto, Calif.,bAnnual Reviews, inc.3 aPalo Alto Ca :bAnnual Reviews  av.billus.  aAnnual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       1967-  aEditor: 1967-       H. L. Roman.1 aMEDLINEbv4, 1970-1 aPubMedbv4, 1970-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 11 (DECEMBER 1977)c19890816fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper that meets the full ANSI standard for Permanent Paper 2aGenetics 2aPeriodical1 aRoman, Herschel L.0 x1545-29484 uhttp://www.annualreviews.org/loi/genet  aAUTH01264cgm a22004094a 101528403DNLM20260227153331.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100406s2010    mdu068|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15676  a(OCoLC)643440768  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 26.51 aPalsson, Bernhard.10aSystems biology :bfrom genome annotation to in silico models /cBernhard Palsson.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (1 hr., 8 min. : sd., col.).  aAccess restricted to NIH only.5DNLM  aRecorded Mar. 5, 2010.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aSystems Biology22aGenomics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15676  aAUTH02225cgm a2200433 a 101510690DNLM20260227152955.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090710s2009    mdu060|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15149  a(OCoLC)732773888  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWH 2001 aShlomchik, Mark.10aB's, T's, tolls, and DCs in systemic autoimmunity /cMark Shlomchik ; Immunology Interest Group.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner.  aRecorded June 3, 2009.3 a(CIT): Mark Shlomchik is an outstanding B cell expert with a primary focus on autoimmunity.  Mark was first in reporting an antibody-independent role of B cells in autoimmune disease.  Stemming from his in-depth analysis of an anti-rheumatoid factor transgenic mouse model, he described the prevalence of somatic hypermutated antibody responses in the absence of germinal centers.  He has studied the various stages of B cell development, including the germinal center reaction, plasma cells and memory B cells using a variety of approaches: flow cytometry and expression analysis of specific populations, analysis of antibody sequences and cell imaging.  Most recently, he has found divergent roles for TLR9 and TLR7 in the lupus autoimmune disease, and has reported on the use of B cell depletion therapy in treatment for diabetes.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aB-Lymphocytesximmunology22aAutoimmunity22aT-Lymphocytesximmunology22aToll-Like Receptorsximmunology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bImmunology Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15149  aAUTH01264cas a2200397 a 101527959DNLM20260227090918.0cr||||||||||||090311c20119999ctuqr p       |    0eng    a  20092023610 a1947-5764l1947-5764  a(OCoLC)314127891  aNSDcNSDdNSDdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW