ode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aFatty Acids, Essentialxchemistry22aFatty Acids, Essentialxmetabolism 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?9954  aAUTH01969cgm a2200397 a 101559819DNLM20260227153944.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u110503s2011    mdu762 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16558  a(DNLM)CIT:16557  a(OCoLC)729826538  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 32500aPluripotent stem cells in translation :bearly decisions /cNIH and FDA.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2011]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file : sd., col., 12 hr., 42 min.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed May 26, 2011).  aRecorded Mar. 21-22, 2011.3 a(CIT): The National Institutes of Health and the Food and Drug Administration are collaborating on a series of workshops on moving pluripotent stem cell therapies into the clinic. The first two day workshop, "Pluripotent Cells in Translation: Early Decisions," is scheduled for March 21 and 22 at Lister Hill Auditorium on the NIH campus in Bethesda, Maryland. The first day will cover pluripotency and its challenges, sources of pluripotent cells, and stem cell banks; the second day will cover making pluripotent stem cells into a product, product characterization, and emerging technologies. The meeting has participation from industry, academic and clinical scientists, the FDA, and the NIH.  aOpen-captioned.12aPluripotent Stem Cells 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1655840uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16557  aAUTH01431cas a2200481   760010