 nurses /cby George M. Price. 1aPhiladelphia ;aNew York :bLea & Febiger,c1913.  aviii, 1 unnumbered page, pages 18-236 ;c20 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aNurses' text book series  aIncludes index.0 aChapter I. Introduction to the study of hygiene -- Chapter II. The hygiene of habitation -- Chapter III. The hygiene of foods and food supply -- Chapter IV. The hygiene of schools and of school children -- Chapter V. The hygiene of occupations -- Chapter VI. The hygiene of municipalities -- Chapter VII. Personal hygiene.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011062pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20260217lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aHygiene12aSanitation 2aNurses Instruction 0aNurses text book series  aAUTH03184ngm a2200445 i 9918916890506676DNLM20260227164836.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u241002s2024    mdu091|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:35185  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 84.300aAdvancing health equity through community-engaged research /cNakela L. Cook. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 31 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aHealth equity research outreach (HERO) lecture series  aRecorded August 27, 2024.3 a(CIT): About the Session: PCORI Executive Director Dr. Nakela Cook, will discuss the Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute’s approach to the funding of health research, highlighting its commitment to advancing health equity through the meaningful engagement of patients and communities throughout the research process. She will share lessons learned from PCORI’s approach to patient and community engagement, as captured in its recently refreshed engagement rubric - the Foundational Expectations for Partnerships in Research. She will also touch on PCORI’s focus on the implementation of study results in ways that reach the patients and communities they are intended to benefit. Through these examples, Dr. Cook will highlight the shared purpose of PCORI and NHLBI’s Center for Translation Research and Implementation Science (CTRIS). The lecture will be followed by a panel discussion on advancing health equity through community-engaged research. The panel includes Dr. Cook (PCORI), Dr. Liz Cohn (CUNY) who will be talking about the soon-to-be released third edition of the seminal text on "Principles of Community Engagement", as well as the Lead Principal Investigators of the Community Engagement Alliance Consultative Resource (CEACR), Dr. Mylynda Massart (UPitt) and Al Richmond (Community Campus Partnerships for Health) who will share lessons learned around meaningful community engagement in research. The panel discussion will conclude with a Q&A session moderated by Dr. Maliha Ilias from NHLBI  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed February 9, 2026).22aCenter for Translation Research and Implementation Science.22aPatient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute (U.S.)12aCommunity-Based Participatory Research22aHealth Equity 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aCook, Nakela,espeaker.2 aCenter for Translation Research and Implementation Science,esponsoring body. 0aHealth equity research outreach (HERO) quarterly lecture series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=55096  aAUTH01405cas a2200457 a 101528176DNLM20260227090924.0cr||||||||||||091214c20109999nyubr p       |   a0eng    a  20092081760 a2152-4971l2152-497121  a(OCoLC)488695930  aDLCcDLCdGUAdDLCdDNLM  apccansdp  9United States00aQH442.2b.C55900aW1bCL933D10a66021410aCell Reprogram2dnlm0 aCel