6)  aWashington :bExecutive Committee of the Convention of American Instructors of the Deaf3 aSilver Spring Md :bConference Of Educational Administration Serving The Deaf And: Convention Of American Instructors Of The Deaf  av.billus., ports.  aFive no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 31, no. 4-       Oct. 1886-  aIncludes a directory of American Instructors of the Deaf, Jan. 1902-1 aMEDLINEbv10n5, Nov. 1965-0 aPubMedbv10n5, Nov. 1965-0 aOLDMEDLINE1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aMicrofilm.mv.31(1886)-80(1935) + Index v.1(1847)-80(1944).b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d1994.e17 microfilm reels : negative ; 35 mm.  aOfficial organ of the Convention of American Instructors of the Deaf, Sept. 1911-       and of the Conference of Executives of American Schools for the Deaf, 1932-  aIssued Oct. 1886-June 1895 by the Convention of American Instructors of the Deaf; Oct. 1895-       by the Conference of Executives of American Schools for the Deaf (Oct. 1895-Sept. 1930, called Conference of Superintendents and Principals of American Schools for the Deaf).  aVols. 1-50, 1847-1905.  1 v. (Includes index for vols. 1-31 of American annals of the deaf and dumb)  Subsequent indexes issued every ten years.  3Vol. 132, no. 1 (1987)c19900913fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paperxFurther review is required to determine exactly when acid-free paper was first used for this title 2aDeafness 2aPeriodical2 aConference of Executives of American Schools for the Deaf.2 aConference of Superintendents and Principals of American Schools for the Deaf.2 aConvention of American Instructors of the Deaf.00tAmerican annals of the deaf and dumbx0093-1284w(OCoLC)34721974 uhttp://muse.jhu.edu/journals/american%5Fannals%5Fof%5Fthe%5Fdeaf  aAUTH02361cgmaa22004574a 101180549DNLM20260227144252.0vf|cbahouvf|cjahou030530s2003    mdu060 ||    f   