e era, we increasingly rely on strong collaboration between basic and clinical scientists to develop novel approaches for treatment of human disease. The intramural program of the NCI is one of the largest centers for cancer research in the world, with over 300 Principal Investigators, and has a major role in development and implementation of many of new technologies, such as genomics and proteomics.  For more information, visit http://ccr.cancer.gov/careers/traco.asp.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aLung Neoplasmsxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aCenter for Cancer Research (National Cancer Institute (U.S.)) 0aTRACO seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14015  aAUTH01597cas a2200445 i 101676795DNLM20260227090910.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||160211c20169999ne || poo     0    0eng    a  2017243298  a989756029a990742792a993933918  a2452-0748l2452-0748  a(OCoLC)962744583  z(OCoLC)989756029z(OCoLC)990742792z(OCoLC)993933918  aCNCGMbengerdad20260227cCNCGMdVT2dOCLCQdOCLCFdUABdUX1dCUSdOCLdLNDdDNLM  apcc  9Netherlands14aTA418.9.N3500aW110aNanoImpact2dnlm 0aNanoImpactb(Amsterdam)00aNanoImpact. 1a[Amsterdam] :bElsevier B.V.,c[2016]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1 (January 2016).  a"An international journal of nanosafety research."1 aMEDLINEbv21, Jan. 2021-0 aPubMedbv21, Jan. 2021- ; Selected citations only before this date  aDescription based on: Volume 1 (January 2016); title from journal table of contents page (ScienceDirect website, viewed September 26, 2017).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 7 (July 2017) (viewed September 26, 2017).12aNanostructures22aSafety Management 2aPeriodical40uhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/nanoimpact  aAUTH01541cas a2200481 a 101525337DNLM20260224111603.0m        d        cr |||||||||||090603c201