all diseases affecting horses participating in racing and competition. Not only does this text discuss the physiological responses of each body system to exercise, but it covers nutritional support, the prevention of exercise-induced disorders and lameness, and modification of training regimens. New to this edition are topics such as drug effects on performance and the use of cloud-based technologies for monitoring performance, as well as new content on exercise physiology, welfare, conditioning, farriery, behavior, and vision." --cProvided by publisher.12aHorsesxphysiology12aVeterinary Sports Medicine22aHorse Diseases22aHorsesxsurgery22aExercise Testxveterinary1 aHinchcliff, Kenneth W.q(Kenneth William),d1956-eeditor.4edt1 aKaneps, Andris J.,eeditor.4edt1 aGeor, Raymond J.,eeditor.4edt1 aErck-Westergren, Emmanuelle van,eeditor.  ihas work:aEquine sports medicine and surgery (Text)4https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/ontology/hasWork  aAUTH01356nam a2200385 i 9918986597706676DNLM20260226110532.0t|240419s2024    paua     bf   001 0 eng    aGBC4368412bnb  a9781451116519qhardback  a14511165198 aCIPO000077316  a(OCoLC)1457980449  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCO  apcc  9United States00aWR 3904a616.50422230 aGenodermatoses (Spitz)10aSpitz's genodermatoses :ba full color clinical guide to genetic skin disorders /c[edited by] Jennifer L. Hand, Joel L. Spitz, Jackson Glenn Turbeville.  aThird edition. 1aPhiladelphia :bLippincott Williams & Wilkins,c2024.  a464 pages :billustrations (colour) ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aPreceded by Genodermatoses : a clinical guide to genetic skin disorders / [edited by] Joel L. Spitz ; illustrations by Vaune J. Hatch. 2nd. ed. c2005.12aSkin Diseasesxgenetics 2aHandbook1 aSpitz, Joel L.,eeditor.1 aHand, Jennifer L.,eeditor.1 aTurbeville, Jackson Glenn,eeditor.  aAUTH02163cgm a2200481 i 9