utes;  (2) reorganize the offices within the Office of the Director, NIH including adding, removing, or transferring the functions of such offices or establishing or terminating such offices; and  (3) reorganize, divisions, centers, or other administrative units within an NIH national research institute or national center including adding, removing, or transferring the functions of such units, or establishing or terminating such units. </ul>  The purpose of the Scientific Management Review Board (also referred to as SMRB or Board) is to advise appropriate HHS and NIH officials on the use of these organizational authorities and identify the reasons underlying the recommendations.   For more information, if available http://smrb.od.nih.gov/.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aAcademies and Institutesxorganization & administration12aBiomedical Researchxorganization & administration22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1506040uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15063  aAUTH01397cgm a22004214a 101267872DNLM20260227145857.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2002    mdu073 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10886  a(OCoLC)67281737  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 3141 aWestbrook, Gary.10aSynaptic integration in the olfactory bulb /cGary Westbrook.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2002]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 5, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 12 min., 59 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 15, 2002.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aOlfactory Bulb22aNeural Inhibition22aSynapses 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10886  aAUTH01199cam a2200361 i 9918845379806676DNLM20260212070707.0240701s2022    ag       b    000 0 spa    ź9789874781123  a(OCoLC)1521297274  aDNLMbengerdad20260212dDNLM  apcc  9Argentina00aWZ 70 DA71 aPalomo, Alejandroc(Professor of history),eauthor.13aLa medicina como profesión en Buenos Aires (1780-1830) :bdel protomedicato a la universidad /cAlejandro Palomo.  a1a edición. 1aCiudad Autónoma de Buenos Aires :bHygea Ediciones,c[2022]  axvi, 264 pages ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aSeries históricas  aIncludes bibliographical references.12aPhysiciansxhistory22aEducation, Medicalxhistory22aPublic Healthxhistory22aHistory, 18th Century22aHistory, 19th Century 2aArgentina 0aSéries históricas (Buenos Aires, Argentina)  aAUTH02437nam a2200433 i 9918862788106676DNLM20260206100209.0231209s2023    gw ac    b    000 0 ger    a9783849819323q(paperback)  a3849819329q(paperback)3 a9783849819323  a(OCoLC)1412786208  aOHXbengerdacOHXdOCLCQdZCUdOCLCOdNOC  apcc  9Germany 4aPN56.P9bW54 202300aWM 49 7aPN2lcco 7aRC2lcco04a150qOCoLC00a"Wie fremd ich der Welt geworden bin" :bUmrisse eines Projekts zum Thema "Literatur und Psychiatrie" /cGesa Allerheiligen, Walter Gödden, Lisa Inckmann, Michael Kienecker (Hrsg.) 1aBielefeld :bAisthesis Verlag,c2023  a312 pages :billustrations (chiefly color), portraits ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aVeröffentlichungen der Literaturkommission für Westfalen ;vBand 106  aIncludes bibliographical references  a"Das Projekt outside-inside-outside zum Thema Literatur und Psychiatrie wurde 2021 bis 2023 gemeinsam von der LWL-Literaturkommission, dem Kunsthaus Kannen und dem Lektora Verlag durchgeführt. Wie das Projekt selbst, ist dieses Buch stark interdisziplinär und abwechslungsreich angelegt - wissenschaftlich, poetisch, lyrisch. Dieses reich bebilderte Lesebuch beleuchtet die zahlreichen Facetten des Themas und vereint neben Fundstücken aus Literatur und Film auch Expertise aus Medizin und Therapie. Werkstattbeschreibungen von Konzerten und Theaterstücken sowie persönliche Einblicke ergänzen die Anthologie zu einem bunten Kaleidoskop unterschiedlichster Formen und Genres. In Zeiten des öffentlichen Diskurses um mentale Gesundheit bietet es einen differenzierten Kompass mit weiterführenden Hinweisen auf engagierte Initiativen und hilfreiche Anlaufstellen."--Publisher's website12aPsychiatry in Literature22aMedicine in the Arts22aMental Disorders1 aAllerheiligen, Gesa,eeditor.1 aGödden, Walter,eeditor.1 aInckmann, Lisa,d1957-eeditor.1 aKienecker, Michael,eeditor. 0aVeröffentlichungen der Literaturkommission für Westfalen ;vBd. 106.  aAUTH01917cgm a22004214a 101267801DNLM20260227152554.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2001    mdu120 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10688  a(OCoLC)1019844495  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWJ 14600aIncontinence in women :ba women's health seminar /cNIH Office of Research on Women's Health.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2001]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 6, 2006).  aStreaming video (2 hr., 0 min. : sd., col.).  aSpeakers, Jeanette S. Brown, et al.  aRecorded Mar. 1, 2001.3 a(CIT): Overview: Etiology and Epidemiology Jeanette S. Brown, M.D. University of California, SF Diagnosis of Incontinence: Techniques and Procedures O. Lenaine Westney, M.D. The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston   What We Know About Surgery for Stress Incontinence Veronica Mallett, M.D. Oakwood Hospital (Dearborn, MI)   Beha