Alzheimer's disease.The 2021 Summit will build on the foundation laid through the work of the 2012, 2015, and 2018 summit participants. Over the course of the Summit, a global audience of researchers and the public will have an opportunity to contribute individually to the discussions through multiple open forum sessions.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed December 10, 2021).12aAlzheimer Disease22aPrecision Medicine22aBiomedical Research 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute on Aging,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4176640uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4176540uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4176740uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41768  aAUTH01838nam a2200457 a 101745088DNLM20260220152311.0130911s1912    mau           000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)857853004  aMLNbengcMLNdOCLCOdOCLCFdOCLCQdHMSdOL$dOCLCAdOCLdDNLM  an-us---  9United States14aHV3006b.F362 191200aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5658 no.1314a610.73682211 aFernald, Walter E.,d1859-1924.10aCare of the feeble-minded /cby Walter E. Fernald.  a3rd ed.  aBoston :bPress of Geo. H. Ellis,c1912.  a10 pages ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCover title.  a"Reprinted from the National Bulletin of Charities and Correction, 1904."  a"Read at the National Conference of Charities and Correction at Portland, Me., June 20, 1904."--Footnote, page 1.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  cGift;aAmerican Heritage Center, University of Wyoming;d1998.5DNLM  aWill digitizec202102242pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202102245DNLM12aChildren with Disabilities12aInstitutionalization22aPersons with Intellectual Disabilities22aPersons with Psychiatric Disorders22aSocial Responsibility 2