, 2004.3 a(CIT): "Demystifying Medicine" is a weekly course, primarily for Ph.D. students, post-doctoral fellows, and staff at the National Institutes of Health. Physicians and other students are also welcome to participate. The course is led by Dr. Win Arias, Professor of Physiology and Medicine at Tufts School of Medicine in Boston and NIH Adjunct Investigator and Special Assistant in the Office of Intramural Research.  For more information, visit Demystifying medicine.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aColorectal Neoplasmsxtherapy22aAngiogenesis Inhibitorsxtherapeutic use22aGenes, Neoplasm22aNeoplasm Metastasisxphysiopathology22aNeoplasm Metastasisxprevention & control 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)02aPositive and negative regulators of metastasis.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11979  aAUTH02138cgm a2200505 i 101682297DNLM20260227155714.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u160503s2016    mdu059|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19581  a(OCoLC)951503509  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 51500aHealthy volunteer human influenza challenge model :ba key piece of the universal vaccine puzzle /cMatthew J. Memoli. Development and pre-clinical evaluation of a virus-like particle (VLP) universal influenza vaccine / Jeffery K. Taubenberger.1 aDevelopment and pre-clinical evaluation of a virus-like particle (VLP) universal influenza vaccine 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (59 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aRecorded March 30, 2016.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title fr