itiative 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (2 hr., 32 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 2 & 3, 2021.3 a(CIT): The Multi-Disciplinary Working Group serves as a fact-finding body of experts external to NIH to provide input to guide Helping to End Addiction Long-term SM Initiative, or NIH HEAL Initiative SM, research. The working group assists the NIH Institute and Center (IC) Advisory Councils to help ensure that NIH HEAL Initiative research meets the bold, trans-NIH goals for the initiative. Its meetings serve as a forum to engage partners in the private sector and research community, provide a transparent venue for stakeholders and members of the public, and help facilitate exchange of scientific information among NIH HEAL Initiative projects.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed December 20, 2021).22aNIH HEAL Initiative.12aBiomedical Research12aInterdisciplinary Research22aHealth Information Management22aPain Management22aOpioid Epidemic 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNIH HEAL Initiative.bMulti-Disciplinary Working Group,ehost institution.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of the Director,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4155040uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41552  aAUTH01365cgm a22003974a 101267573DNLM20260227145251.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2001    mdu074 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10389  a(OCoLC)65195204  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 301 aGarrett, Laurie.10aBeyond betrayal of trust :bthe geopolitics of getting from lab to global clinic /cLaurie Garrett.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Insti