tish Nutrition Foundation.0 x1467-301000aBritish Nutrition Foundation.tBulletinx0307-3548w(DLC)sn 80008224w(OCoLC)17719254 uhttp://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1467-3010  aAUTH01438cas a2200457 a 8911629DNLM20260227091020.0cr|cnu||||||||890622c19889999maubr p       0    0eng    a0894-0959l0894-0959  a(DNLM)SR0063294(s)  a(OCoLC)15794263  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bSE487NH10aSemin Dial2dnlm 0aSeminars in dialysis00aSeminars in dialysis.  a[Baltimore, MD :bWaverly Press,c1988-3 aCambridge Ma :bBlackwell Science  av. :bill., ports.  aBimonthly  aQuarterlyb1988-1992  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 1988)-  aTitle from cover.  aPlace of publication varies.1 aMEDLINEbv13n1, Jan.-Feb. 2000-1 aPubMedbv13n1, Jan.-Feb. 2000-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3v. 6, no. 1 (Jan. 1993)c20000404fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper that meets the full ANSI standard for Permanent Paper 2aDialysis 2aRenal Dialysis 2aPeriodical0 x1525-139X4 uhttp://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1525-139X  aAUTH02280cgm a2200409 i 101660638DNLM20260227155211.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u150602s2015    mdu070|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19008  a(OCoLC)914328272  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 3371 aCisek, Paul,eauthor.10aNeural mechanisms of real-time decisions /cPaul Cisek. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2015]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 10 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNeuroscience seminar series  aRecorded May 18, 2015.3 a(CIT): Neuroscience Seminar Series  Dr. Cisek is interested in how the brain controls behavior. Many scientists approach this very large question by starting with perception and asking how the brain builds an internal representation of the world, and how it then uses this representation to guide action. In contrast, he studies behavior by starting with a concrete task such as a voluntary movement and asking what parameters of the task the brain must specify and control, and what information from the environment it may employ toward that specification. The goal here is an understanding of brain mechanisms for mediating interaction with the world, not necessarily of mechanisms for representing the world. A research program based on such an approach begins with questions concerning motor control and gradually works its way toward the perceptual systems which guide that control. One could say he is going backwards through the brain.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 15, 2015).12aDecision Makingxphysiology22aBrainxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast 0aNIH neuroscience seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19008  aAUTH01271cas a2200421 a 9112162DNLM20260227091029.0cr|cn ||||||||910912c19889999gw  x p       0    0ger    a0932-8114l0932-8114  a(DNLM)SR0062603(s)  a(OCoLC)18485470  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 agerbeng  9Germany00aW1bZE593G0 aZeitschrift für Sexualforschung (Stuttgart, Germany)10aZ Sex Forsch2dnlm10aZeitschrift für Sexualforschung.  aStuttgart :bEnke,cc1988-  av. :bill.  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 a1. Jahrg., Heft 1 (März 1988)-  aFour no. a year.  aTitle from cover.0 aMEDLINEbSelected citations only0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aArticles in German; summaries in English and German. 2aSex 2aSexual Behavior 2aPeriodical4 uhttps://www.thieme-connect.de/products/ejournals/journal/10.1055/s-00000103  aAUTH01919cas a2200517   9425218DN