lted: Vol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 2009).1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan. 2009-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan. 2009-0 aPMC  aAlso issued online.12aImmunotherapy 2aPeriodical 2aReview0 x1750-74484 uhttps://www.tandfonline.com/journals/iimy204 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101485158  aAUTH02778cgm a2200457 i 101674304DNLM20260227155300.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u151224s2015    mdu063|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19379  a(OCoLC)934742936  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWV 2701 aCunningham, Lisa,eauthor.10aPreventing or reversing hearing loss /cLisa Cunningham ; National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2015]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 3 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBeyond the lab, understanding communication disorders  aRecorded December 10, 2015.3 a(CIT): Learn how research conducted by the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders (NIDCD) is preserving hearing after exposure to life-saving drugs that can cause deafness.    Over half a million Americans experience hearing loss every year from ototoxic drugs--drugs that can damage hair cells in the inner ear. These include some antibiotics and the chemotherapy drug cisplatin. These drugs are beneficial in treating infections or cancer, but they also have the potential side effect of causing hearing loss because the drugs are toxic to hair cells in the inner ear. NIDCD intramural scientists are studying various strategies to preserve hearing without interfering with the therapeutic benefits of these drugs. Designed for  administrative and support staff as well as scientists, the Beyond the Lab, Understanding Communication Disorders speaker series gives the NIH community an opportunity to learn about the NIDCD's research and research advances.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed January 7, 2016).22aNational Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders (U.S.)12aHearing Lossxchemically induced22aAnti-Bacterial Agentsxadverse effects22aCisplatinxadverse effects22aHearing Lossxprevention & control 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders (U.S.),esponsoring body. 0aBeyond the lab, understanding communication disorders speaker series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19379  aAUTH01187cas a2200373   0117710DNLM20260227090916.0cr|cn ||||||||671102c19309999at qr         0||| 0eng    a0029-8077l0003-8121  a(DNLM)O02060000(s)  a(OCoLC)50368489  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Australia00aW1bOC60810aOceania2dnlm00aOceania; a journal devoted to the study of the native peoples of Australia,bNew Guinea, and the Islands of the Pacific.  aSydney :bUniversity of Sydney313<2000- > :aSydney :bpublished by Wiley on behalf of Oceania Publications  av.billus.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       Apr. 1930-0 aMEDLINEbSelected citations only0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online. 2aEthnology 2aPeriodical0 x1834-44614 uhttp://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1834-4461  aAUTH01155cas a2200397 a 8916517DNLM20260227091024.0cr|cn ||||||||891012c19879999enkqr p       0    0eng    a0890-4065l0890-4065  a(DNLM)SR0060331(s)  a(OCoLC)14221706  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9England00aW1bJO534BM10aJ Aging Stud2dnlm 0aJournal of aging studies00aJournal of aging studies.30aAging studies  aGreenwich, Conn. :bJAI Press,cc1987-3 3<2003-> :aOxford :bPergamon  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no