50421s2005    mdu061       f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:3448  a(OCoLC)60414178  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aQT 3600aBiotechnology and nanotechnology :btwo overlapping health revolutions /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2005]  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (61 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (61 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aWALS, the NIH cultural lecture  aSpeaker, Ray Kurzweil.  aPresented March 30, 2005.  aAlso available online.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aBiotechnology12aNanotechnology22aBiomedical Engineeringxtrends22aGenetic Engineering22aInformation Science22aLife Expectancy1 aKurzweil, Ray.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pNIH director's cultural lecture4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=3448  aAUTH02733cgm a2200565 i 101713963DNLM20260227155754.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u170930s2017    mdu110|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:23462  a(OCoLC)1005931677  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQZ 2062 aNIH Research Festivald(2017 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aNIH Research Festival.pPlenary session III, "the Cancer Moonshot" /cDinah Singer, Aimée R. Kreimer, Brigitte C. Widemann, and Maria Isabel Achatz.1 aPlenary session III, "the Cancer Moonshot"1 aCancer Moonshot 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2017]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 50 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aDr. Widemann is last speaker.  aRecorded September 15, 2017.3 a(CIT): The Cancer Moonshot was launched in 2016 with the stated goal of achieving in five years what would otherwise take a decade of cancer research. To identify those areas of cancer research that were poised for acceleration, a Blue Ribbon Panel was convened with representatives from across the cancer continuum. The panel developed a series of recommendations designed to accelerate our understanding of cancer. This session will review those recommendations, describe the extramural programs that are being established, and highlight three of the intramural programs that are being launched as part of the Cancer Moonshot.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 4, 2017).22aCancer Moonshot (Initiative)12aBiomedical Research12aNeoplasms22aGenetic Predisposition to Disease22aGovernment Programs22aInformation Dissemination22aPapillomavirus Vaccinesxtherapeutic use22aRare Diseasesxtherapy 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aSinger, Dinah Schiffer,d1948-espeaker.1 aKreimer, Aimée R.q(Aimée Rebecca),espeaker.1 aWidemann, Brigitte,espeaker.1 aAchatz, Maria Isabel,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?23462  aAUTH00690cam a22002297i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118100003000151245006400181250001400245264004900259300004100308336002600349337002800375338002700403650002100430999000900451101610566DNLM20260209114427.0900808s1987    cc ac         000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdad20260209dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1772 no.101 aWang, Yabolahan,eauthor.10aRen lei chang qing jian mei bao dian /cWang Yabolahan zhu.  aDi 1 ban. 1aBeijing :bRen min ti yu chu ban she,c1987.  a60 pages :billustrations, portrait.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aPhysical Fitness  aAUTH02276cam a2200409 i 61951180RDNLM20260225114555.0hd|bfa012baap820821s1906    nyuaf    b    000 0 eng    a   06017879   a(OCoLC)5761617  aDNLMbengerdad20260211dDNLM  9United States00aQWAbE33g 19061 aEhrlich, Paul,d1854-1915,eauthor,eeditor.10aCollected studies on immunity /cby Professor Paul Ehrlich and by his collaborators ; with several new contributions, including a chapter written expressly for this edition by Professor Ehrlich ; translated by Dr. Charles Bolduan ; [edited by Paul Ehrlich].  aFirst edition. 1aNew York :bJ. Wiley & Sons,c1906.  axi, 586 pages, 1 unnumbered leaves of plates :billustrations, portrait ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aContains English translation of Gesammelte Arbeiten zur Immunitätsforschung.  a"Attention is called to the fact that the important work done since the publication of the German edition has been included by the addition of three chapters, two by Ehrlich and Sachs and one, written expressly for this translation by, Prof. Ehrlich. The subject is thus brought up to about March, 1906"--P. iii.  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 8626 no. 25DNLM  aPublisher's catalog bound together in 18 pages at back.  aContains bibliographical references.  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d1998.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011232pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20260212lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aImmune System Phenomena 2aCollected Work1 aBolduan, Charles,d1873-1950,etranslator.1 iContainer of (work)::aEhrlich, Paul,d1854-1915.tGesammelte Arbeiten zur Immunitätsforschung.lEnglish  aAUTH