 zhi,c[between 1949-1956]  a8 pages :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aSmallpoxxprevention & control22aSmallpox Vaccinextherapeutic use 2aPictorial Work1 aShanghai (China).bWei sheng ju,eissuing body.  aAUTH01447cgm a2200433 i 101629980DNLM20260227154733.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u140408s2014    mdu092|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18362  a(OCoLC)880404090  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 1081 aSmith, Carolyn Beebe,eauthor.10aDemystifying medicine 2014.pSleep :bperchance to dream /cCarolyn Beebe Smith, Susan Harbison.1 aSleep :bperchance to dream 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 32 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded Apr. 1, 2014.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed Apr. 25, 2014.12aSleep22aDrosophilaxgenetics22aSleep Wake Disorders 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aHarbison, Susan,eauthor.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18362  aAUTH02439cgm a22004574a 101289758DNLM20260227151635.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061011s2006    mdu096 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13357  a(OCoLC)84714275  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWT 301 aFogel, Robert William.10aChronic disease and disability from 19th to 21st centuries :binterview with Drs. Robert Fogel and Dora Costa.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Dec. 15, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 35 min., 36 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Sept. 12, 2006.3 a(CIT): Dr. Robert Fogel of the University of Chicago Graduate School of Business, the Nobel Lauerate in Economics whose work has revolutionized thinking about the history of health in the US, will appear with colleague Dr. Dora Costa of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology to discuss findings with their NIA Program Project grant on the aging process of Union Army veterans   This ambitious project links vast amounts of information for a sample of Union Army veterans to allow researchers to study their aging process and compare it to that of later cohorts.  Drs. Fogel and Costa will present their surprising findings from this study, which reveal a picture of humans today that is vastly different from 100 years ago.  They will examine what their research suggests for current and future aging populations - cohorts that today are longer-lived, healthier, more affluent and more urban than their predecessors - and what these trends imply for health, long-term care and social security systems.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aChronic Diseasexepidemiology22aAging22aCohort Studies22aHealth Status22aVeterans 2aUnited Statesxepidemiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13357  aAUTH01356cgm a22004334a 101524393DNLM20260227153304.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100213s2010    mdu037|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15559  a(OCoLC)551341864  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWI 1491 aKim, Su Young.10aUtilizing results from the NIH GIST clinics to plan for the future /cSu Young Kim.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aPediatric GIST Clinic invitational lecture ;v4th  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (37 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jan. 20, 2010.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGastrointestinal Stromal Tumors22aAdolescent22aChild22aTreatment Outcome 2aLecture 2aWebcast 0aPediatric GIST Clinic invitational lecture ;v4th.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15559  aAUTH02052cas a2200565 a 8904605DNLM20260227091013.0cr|cnu||||||||890302c19899999paumr p       0    0eng    a   89643636 zsn 88002245  a1040-2446l1040-2446  aACMEEO  a(DNLM)SR0065053(s)  a(OCoLC)18356569  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  ansdp  9United States00aW1bAC33NH10aAcad Med2dnlm 0aAcademic medicine00aAcademic medicine :bjournal of the Association of American Medical Colleges.  a[Philadelphia, Pa. :bHanley & Belfus,cc1989-3 aPhiladelphia, PA :bPublished for the Association of American Medical Colleges by Lippincott Williams & Wilkins  av. :bill.  aMonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 64, no. 1 (Jan. 1989)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv64n1,Jan. 1989-0 aPubMedbv64n1,Jan. 1989-1 aAbridged index medicus1 aIndex medicus  aSupplements accompany some issues.  aAlso issued online.  aVols. for 1990- include supplement with title: Research in medical education.  3(1995)c19950524lNot printed on acid-free paper1 3v.64,no.1, Jan. 1989-aWill not microfilmc200502232pda5DNLM 2aEducation, Medical 2aPeriodical2 aAssociation of American Medical Colleges.02aResearch in medical education.0 x1938-808X00tJournal of medical educationx0022-2577w(DLC)sn 81003337w(OCoLC)69886704 uhttp://www.academicmedicine.org/4 uhttps://ovidsp.ovid.com/ovidweb.cgi?T=JS&NEWS=n&CSC=Y&PAGE=toc&D=yrovft&AN=00001888-000000000-000004 uhttps://academic.oup.com/academicmedicine  aAUTH01417cas a2200493 a 8918131DNLM20260227091017.0cr|cnu||||||||891130c19899999enkqr p       0||| 0eng    asn 90031254   a0954-0261l0954-0261  aIRPSE2  a(DNLM)SR0064354(s)  