).  aRecorded Mar. 12, 2003.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aBrainximmunology22aBrainxdrug effects22aStress, Physiological 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute on Drug Abuse.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?9928  aAUTH02608cgm a22004814a 101531571DNLM20260227153405.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100519s2010    mdu789 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15839  a(DNLM)CIT:15855  a(DNLM)CIT:15859  a(OCoLC)669122032  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWT 1552 aNIH State-of-the-Science Conferenced(2010 Apr. :cNational Institutes of Health)10aNIH State-of-the-Science conference :bpreventing Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline /csponsored by the National Institute on Aging, Office of Medical Applications of Research.1 aPreventing Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (13 hr., 9 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 26-28, 2010.3 a(CIT): For many older adults, cognitive health and performance remain stable, with only a gradual and slight decline in short-term memory and reaction times. Others, however, progress into a more serious state of cognitive impairment or into various forms of dementia, including Alzheimer's disease. In addition to investigating the causes and potential treatments for Alzheimer"s and other dementias, researchers are focused on finding ways to prevent cognitive decline. Many preventive measures for cognitive decline and for preventing Alzheimer"s have been suggested, but their value in delaying the onset and/or reducing the severity of decline or disease is unclear. Be part of pivotal discussions that will help answer critical questions related to preventing Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.  http://consensus.nih.gov/2010/alz.htm.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aAlzheimer Diseasexcomplications12aAlzheimer Diseasexprevention & control22aCognition Disordersxetiology22aCognition Disordersxprevention & control 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1583940uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1585540uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15859  aAUTH02181cgmaa22005054a 101202666DNLM20260227144811.0vf|czahmuvd|cvaizucr|cna||||||||vf|cjahouhd|bfa012baap040109s2003    mdu069       f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:2587  a(OCoLC)54818880  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aWV 274bVC no.27 200300aCochlear implants :bpast, present, and future /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  a1 videocassette of 1 (DVCPRO) (69 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/4 in.3master.  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (69 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videodisc of 1 (DVD) (69 min.) :bsd., col. ;c4 3/4 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aThe NIH director's Wednesday afternoon lectures. NIH director's sixth astute clinician lecture  aSpeaker, Richard T. Miyamoto.  aPresented Nov. 5, 2003.  aAlso available online.  aVideocassette (Betacam SP)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2011.e1 videocassette (69 min.) : sd., col. ; 1/2 in.  aVideodisc (DVD)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2018.e1 videodisc (69 min.) : sd., col. ; 4 3/4 in.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aCochlear Implantation22aChild22aInfant22aLanguage Dev