tifying medicinepGenetic screening :bfinding Mendelian disease genes /cLes Biesecker and Julie Sapp.30aGenetic screening  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 20, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 50 min., 18 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 11, 2008.3 a(CIT): The course includes presentation of patients, pathology, diagnosis and therapy in the context of major disease problems and current research.  Primarily directed toward Ph.D. students, fellows, and staff, it is also of interest to medical students and clinicians.  The course is designed to help bridge the gap between advances in biology and their application to major human diseases.  Each session includes clinical and basic science components which are presented by NIH staff and outside invitees.  For more information, visit  http://www1.od.nih.gov/oir/DemystifyingMed.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGenetic Diseases, Inborn22aGenetic Counseling22aOligonucleotide Array Sequence Analysis. 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14355  aAUTH01644cgm a2200469 i 101645881DNLM20260227154727.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u141108s2014    mdu049       fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18664  a(OCoLC)898752329  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQZ 2001 aAlani, Rhoda M.eauthor.10aPromise and progress :bmelanoma therapy for 2014 and beyond /cRhoda M. Alani.1 aMelanoma therapy for 2014 and beyond 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (49 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds, contemporary clinical medi