 1975); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Cilt 15, sayı 3 (Aralık 2004).  aVols. 1-8 (1974-1997) cover 3 years each.  aAlso issued online.  aTurkish and English.12aPhysical Therapy Modalities22aRehabilitation 2aPeriodical2 aTürkiye Fizyoterapistler Derneği.4 uhttps://dergipark.org.tr/en/pub/tjpr  aAUTH01469cam a22003617a 101277599DNLM20260204124739.0060525s1890    ilua          000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)181358913  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1285 no.102 aSharp & Smith.bElastic Goods Department10aSharp & Smith, manufacturers of superior elastic stockings and abdominal supporters.3 aSharp and Smith, manufacturers of superior elastic stockings and abdominal supporters  a[Chicago :bSharp & Smith,c1894?]  a[18] p. :bill. ;c16 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"Three highest awards at World's Fair."  a"Heel in elastic stocking patented April 12, 1887."  aIncludes [7] perforated leaves for taking measurements.  aNLM copy: the first perforated leaf has been partially removed.5DNLM  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  cGift;aJane B. Lossing.5DNLM  aWill digitizec202012032pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202012035DNLM12aManufactured Materials22aEquipment and Supplies22aTrusses  aAUTH01943cgm a22004334a 101289646DNLM20260227151614.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061011s2006    mdu058 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13181  a(OCoLC)85885224  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQS 6771 aNussenzweig, Michel.10aSwitching on chromosome translocations /cMichel Nussenzweig.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Dec. 18, 2006).  aStreaming video (57 min., 21 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 19, 2006.3 a(CIT): Dr. Nussenzweig pursues a combination of biochemical, molecular and genetic approaches to define the checkpoints that regulate B-cell development, antibody production and B-cell tolerance. A second area of interest is in dendritic cells. His research interests range from the earliest phases of the B-cell pathway, including the commitment to becoming a B-cell through the completion of maturation. His ongoing work includes a focus on mechanisms of V(D)J recombination, somatic mutation, isotype switching, allelic exclusion and tolerance.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aTranslocation, Genetic22aImmunoglobulin Class Switching 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13181  aAUTH02389cgm a2200493 i 9918573160706676DNLM20260227163243.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230302s2023    mdu058|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32935  a(OCoLC)1393201538  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQU 248 AC200aCommunity-engaged approaches for preventing and controlling obesity among U.S. Latinos/Hispanics /cGuadalupe Ayala. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (58 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Wednesday afternoon lecture  aRecorded February 8, 2023.3 a(CIT): WALS  Dr. Ayala will describe a program of research in a rural community to address the issues of obesity and diabetes in the US Latino/Hispanic community. This program of research was an outgrowth of early collaborations between a research team and representatives from a Federally Qualified Health Center seeking to improve the health of the community. The partnership began with an outward-facing research agenda to one that involved significant policy and system changes within the healthcare settings. Using examples from three research projects, Dr. Ayala will describe changes to their research approach and health outcomes achieved.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed July 26, 2023).12aObesityxprevention & control12aObesityxethnology22aDiabetes Mellitusxprevention & control22aHispanic or Latino22aRural Population22aCommunity Health Services22aHealth Services Research 2aCaliforniaxethnology 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aAyala, Guadalupe X.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=46060  aAUTH01189cas a2200409 a 8910839DNLM20260227091023.0cr|cn ||||||||890615c19899999enk x p       0||| 0eng    a0933-4807l0933-4807  aPTRDEO  a(DNLM)SR0064415(s)  a(OCoLC)18083986  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9England00aW1bPT7310aPteridines2dnlm00aPteridines.  aBerlin ; New York :bWalter de Gruyter,cc1989-3 aPortsmouth, Eng :bInternational Society Of Pteridinology  av. :bill.  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 1989)-  aImprint varies.  aVols. 2 and 3 are complete in three issues.  aPrint ceased with v.17, no.4 (2006).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online. 2aPteridines 2aPeriodical0 x2195-47204 uhttps://www.degruyter.com/view/j/pteridines  aAUTH02578cgm a2200433 i 101735323DNLM20260227155835.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u181003s2018    mdu065|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:26073  a(OCoLC)1060577629  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 26.504aThe best way to predict the future is to create it-- but is it already too late? /cAlan Curtis Kay. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2018]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 5 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aLindberg-King lecture ;v3  aRecorded September 26, 2018.3 a(CIT): Computer science pioneer Alan Curtis Kay, Ph.D., will deliver this year's Lindberg-King Lecture in the Lister Hill Auditorium. His talk is titled, "The Best Way to Predict the Future is to Create It. But Is It Already Too Late?" A child prodigy, Dr. Kay was an original member of the seminal Xerox-PARC group, and for his myriad innovations in computer science was awarded computer science"s highest honor: the Turing Prize. He has been elected a Fellow of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, the National Academy of Engineering, and the Royal Society of Arts. He is the president of the Viewpoints Research Institute and an adjunct professor of computer science at the University of California, Los Angeles.  The Lindberg-King Lecture honors former NLM Director Donald A.B. Lindberg, M.D., and former NLM Deputy Director of Research, and Education Donald West King, M.D. The event is co-sponsored by the NLM, Friends of the National Library of Medicine, and the American Medical Informatics Association.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 16, 2018).12aMedical Informaticsxtrends22aDiffusion of Innovation22aMedical Informaticsxeducation 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aKay, Alanq(Alan Curtis),d1940-espeaker.2 aNational Library of Medicine (U.S.),esponsoring body. 0aDonald A. B. Lindberg and Donald West King lecturev3.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?26073  aAUTH01458cgm a22004454a 101268353DNLM20260227150524.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2004    mdu070 