 2aLecture 2aWebcast12aNath, Avindra.tProgressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy.12aMajor, Eugene O.tBiological and molecular link between Natalizumab therapy and risk of progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aClinical Center grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18864  aAUTH02647cgm a22004334a 101510699DNLM20260227153029.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090710s2009    mdu257|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15162  a(OCoLC)708543522  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 3202 aNational Advisory Child Health and Human Development Council (U.S.).bMeetingn(138th :d2009 :cBethesda, Md.)10aNational Advisory Child Health and Human Development Council Meeting :bJune 11, 2009 /cEunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (NICHD).  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 17, 2011).  aStreaming video (4 hr., 17 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 11, 2009.3 a(CIT): The NICHD Advisory Council has two specific functions:  (1) to advise the NICHD on policy and procedures affecting the extramural research programs and (2) to provide the second level of review for grant applications requesting Institute funding support. The Council meets for one day three times a year in January, June, and September.    The morning session is Open to the Public and is devoted to bringing Council members up-to-date with a Report of the Director, NICHD, a report by the Council Subcommittee on Planning and Policy, a review of one of the extramural program areas, discussion and review of proposed concepts for NICHD initiatives, the annual review of the Board of Scientific Counselors reports on intramural research programs, and new business items identified by the Council membership and Institute staff. The afternoon session is closed to the Public for the confidential Review of Applications.   For more information, visit  http://www.nichd.nih.gov/about/overview/advisory/nachhd/virtual-meeting-200905.cfm.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aNational Institute of Child Health and Human Development (U.S.)12aChild Welfare22aBiomedical Researchxorganization & administration22aHuman Development22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15162  aAUTH01234cas a2200373 i 101778016DNLM20260219100329.0210414c20209999fr || p       |    0fre    a  2026223509  a2743-155Xy0003-3049l2743-155X  a(OCoLC)1572697763  aDNLMbengerdad20260219cDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9France00aW1bAN22104aLes Pathologies vasculaires.1 aLPV 1aParis :bÉditions Eska  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with: Volume 72, numéro 1 (2020)  aOfficial organ of the Société française d'angéiologie and the Union internationale d'angéiologie.0 aVolume 72, numéro 1 (2020) ; title from cover.1 aVolume 74, numéro 1 (2022)12aBlood Vesselsxpathology12aVascular Diseases 2aPeriodical2 aSociété française d'angéiologie,eissuing body.2 aInternational Union of Angiology,eissuing body.00tAngéiologiex0003-3049w(OCoLC)2257509  aAUTH02022cas a2200565 a 8501420DNLM20260227091017.0cr|cn ||||||||850214c19849999nyuqr p       0||| 0eng    a   86641251 zsc 85002319zsn 82002222  a0731-8898l0731-8898  aJEPOEC  a(DNLM)SR0052441(s)  a(OCoLC)08266212  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bJO644BFD10aJ Environ Pathol Toxicol Oncol2dnlm 0aJournal of environmental pathology, toxicology and oncology00aJournal of environmental pathology, toxicology and oncology :bofficial organ of the International Society for Environmental Toxicol