06676DNLM20260220080953.0250207s2019    bo a     bs   000 0 spa    a9789917000785  aDNLMbengerdad20260219dDNLM  apcc  9Bolivia00aWA 900 DB61 aGálvez Murillo, Alberto de la,eauthor.10aMortalidad perinatal, neonatal y bajo peso al nacer en Bolivia /cAlberto De La Galvez Murillo C.  aPrimera edición. 1a[La Paz] :bCIDES-UMSA :c2019.  a91 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aCIDES 35 años  aIncludes bibliographical references.12aPerinatal Mortality22aInfant Mortality22aInfant, Low Birth Weight22aInfant Deathxprevention & control 2aBolivia 2aStatistics2 aObservatorio de Mortalidad Materna y Neonatal,eissuing body. 0aColección 35 aniversario (La Paz, Bolivia)  aAUTH02199cgm a2200397 i 101595172DNLM20260227154342.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u121102s2012    mdu395|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17588  a(OCoLC)821155360  aDNLMcDNLMerdadDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWS 10000aBridging the terminology gap in pediatrics :bdeveloping an action plan to support the continuum from clinic to research /cNICHS, PEDSnet, and AHRQ. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (6 hr., 35 min.) :bcolor, sound)  atwo-dimensional moving image2rdacontent  acomputer2rdamedia  aonline resource2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded September 21, 2012.3 a(CIT): This will bring together leaders from government, academia, industry, and professional organizations in the field of Pediatrics to organize a governance structure and prioritization mechanism across multiple pediatric terminology efforts. This effort is aimed at harmonizing and bridging the continuum from research to health care delivery in pediatrics.  Proposed topics of discussion include: Rationale for a standardized pediatric terminology; Defining use cases suitable to guide this effort; Mapping out a framework for governance and implementation of pediatric terminology; The anticipated outcomes are: A consensus governance model; An initial set of procedures for structuring that model; An action plan for implementing terminologies; A set of next steps to formalize the governance process.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed December 12, 2012.12aPediatrics22aTerminology as Topic 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aEunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17588  aAUTH01564nam a2200445 i 9918987879306676DNLM20260225094815.0240319s2024    flua     b    001 0 eng    a  2023290821  a9780367697624q(hardcover)  a0367697629  a9780367697631q(paperback)  a0367697637  z9781003143130q(ebook)  a(OCoLC)1427567631  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdOCLCQdIG#  apcc  9United States00aRS380b.P76 202400aQV 241/QV3804a615.1/9qOCoLC223/eng/2024041700aProcess validation in manufacturing of biopharmaceuticals /cedited by Anurag Singh Rathore, Hal Baseman, and Scott Rudge.  aFourth edition. 1aBoca Raton :bCRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024.  axvii, 394 pages :billustrations ;c27 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBiotechnology and bioprocessing series ;vv. 35  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.12aBiological Productsxpharmacology22aTechnology, Pharmaceuticalxmethods22aDrug Approval22aQuality Control1 aRathore, Anurag S.q(Anurag Singh),d1973-eeditor.1 aBaseman, Harold,d1956-eeditor.1 aRudge, Scott R.,eeditor. 0aBiotechnology and bioprocessing series ;vv. 35.  aAUTH01453cas a2200505 a 9004522DNLM20260227091012.0cr|cnu||||||||900329c19909999nyumr p       0||| 0eng    a1044-5498l1044-5498  aDCEBE8  a(DNLM)SR0066240(s)  a(OCoLC)19827838  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1