4 uhttps://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/browse/naika  aAUTH02729cgm a2200481 i 9918503180306676DNLM20260227162722.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u221105s2022    mdu583|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32653  a(DNLM)CIT:32657  a(OCoLC)1401899521  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWS 1072 aBuilding a Diverse Community for Down Syndrome Research (Workshop)d(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aINCLUDE Building a Diverse Community for Down Syndrome Research /cNIH, INCLUDE Project.1 aBuilding a Diverse Community for Down Syndrome Research 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (9 hr., 43 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded September 20 & 21, 2022.3 a(CIT): Join the National Institutes of Health (NIH) and the INCLUDE Project Team on September 20 and 21, 2022 as we host a virtual workshop to inform our efforts to enhance diversity and inclusion in Down syndrome research. The INCLUDE project was launched in 2018 to address health concerns and quality-of-life needs for people with Down syndrome. The goals of INCLUDE are to: -Understand health conditions that are common in people with Down syndrome -Improve collaboration on Down syndrome research -Increase the number of people studying Down syndrome -Involve more people with Down syndrome and their families--especially those from different backgrounds--in research This virtual workshop follows the listening sessions that we hosted in May 2022. Participants will include self-advocates, members of the Down syndrome community including governmental and agency partners, healthcare and service providers, researchers, and experts in diversity and inclusion.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed September 18, 2023).12aDown Syndrome22aBiomedical Researchxmethods22aDiversity, Equity, Inclusion22aVulnerable Populations 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aINCLUDE Project,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4623540uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=46237  aAUTH02299cgm a2200493 i 9918819969706676DNLM20260227164637.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u240501s2024    mdu900|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33892  a(DNLM)CIT:33905  a(OCoLC)1523180302  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 5032 aNIH HIV & Women Scientific Workshop: Centering the Health of Women in HIV Researchd(2024 :cOnline)jauthor.10aNIH HIV & Women Scientific Workshop: Centering the Health of Women in HIV Research :bMarch 21-22, 2024 /cOffice of Research on Women's Health, NIH.1 aNIH HIV and Women Scientific Workshop: Centering the Health of Women in HIV Research10aHIV & women scientific workshop (day 1 & 2) 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (15 hr., 0 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 21 & 22, 2024.3 a(CIT): This 2-day scientific workshop will foster interdisciplinary, intersectional, community-centered knowledge exchange on topics of relevance to HIV &amp; women - including cisgender, transgender, and gender diverse women; and individuals assigned female at birth - across the life course.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed June 11, 2025).12aHIV Infections12aWomen22aSexual and Gender Minorities22aIntersectoral Collaboration22aCommunity Health Services 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Research on Women's Health,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of H