600715337002800741338002700769650002200796651001100818655002700829999000900856101263118DNLM20260204171855.0051208s2005    ru c          101 0 ruso   a9785971600022  a5971600028  a(OCoLC)70326229  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Russia (Federation)00aWB 1022 aVserossiǐskai︠a︡ nauchno-prakticheskai︠a︡ konferent︠s︡ii︠a︡ "Molodye uchenye v medit︠s︡ine"n(10th :d2005 :cKazanʹ, Russia)10aX Vserossiǐskai︠a︡ nauchno-prakticheskai︠a︡ konferent︠s︡ii︠a︡ "Molodye uchenye v medit︠s︡ine" :bposvi︠a︡shchennai︠a︡ 1000-letii︠u︡ Kazani i 60-letii︠u︡ Pobedy v Velikoĭ Otechestvennoĭ voĭne : 26-27 apreli︠a︡ 2005 g. : tezisy dokladov /c[pod redakt︠s︡ieĭ V.A. Anokhina].  aKazanʹ :bMeddok,c2005.  a274 p. :bport.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aClinical Medicine 2aRussia 2aConference Proceedings  aAUTH02141cgm a22003974a 101507224DNLM20260227152949.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090605s2009    mdu774 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15130  a(OCoLC)423570942  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWB 1461 aUnited States.bDepartment of Health and Human Services.bChronic Fatigue Syndrome Advisory Committee.10aChronic Fatigue Syndrome Advisory Committee meeting.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screens (viewed June 26, 2009).  aStreaming video (12 hr., 53 min., 3 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded May 27-28, 2009.3 a(CIT): The Chronic Fatigue Syndrome Advisory Committee was established to provide science-based advice and recommendations to the Secretary of Health and Human Services and the Assistant Secretary for Health on a broad range of issues and topics pertaining to chronic fatigue syndrome (CFS).  Topics include:  (1) the current state of knowledge and research about the epidemiology and risk factors relating to CFS, and identifying potential opportunities in these areas; (2) current and proposed diagnosis and treatment methods for CFS; and (3) development and implementation of programs to inform the public, health care professionals, and the biomedical, academic and research communities about CFS advances.  The Committee meets twice a year, spring and fall.    For more information, visit:  http://www.hhs.gov/advcomcfs/.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aFatigue Syndrome, Chronic. 2aUnited States 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1513040uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15136  aAUTH01689cam a2200385 i 101724642DNLM20260211162405.0cr||||||||||||180404s1849    mau           000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)1031198080  aDNLMbengerdad20260211dDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 116 no.11 aMassachusetts.bGeneral Court.bHouse of Representatives.bCommittee on Public Charitable Institutions,eauthor.10aResolves for the purchase of land and the erection of a second hospital for the insane. 1a[Boston?] :b[publisher not identified],c[1849?]  a1 sheet ;c25 x 15 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  asheetbnb2rdacarrier1 aHouse ;v1849, no. 22  aTitle from caption on  page 2.  a"Commonwealth of Massachusetts, House of Representatives, February 7, 1849"--Page 1.  aRecommendation of the Committee on Public Charitable Institutions to adopt the accompanying resolves.  aAlso available online.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20180613lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM1 adigitizedc20202pda5DNLM12aHospitals, Psychiatric22aHospital Planning 2aMassachusetts 0aHouse document (Massachusetts. General Court. House of Representatives) ;v1849, no. 22.4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/101724642  aAUTH01758cas a2200481 i 101769238DNLM2