Lecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aMedicine for the public40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12202  aAUTH01463cas a2200457 a 101469707DNLM20260227090914.0cr|cn ||||||||071012c20079999mautr p       0    0eng    a  2007239327  a76697025  a1750-8592l1750-8592  a(OCoLC)174114249  z(OCoLC)76697025  aPAEcPAEdIULdOCLCQdHNKdMUQdDLCdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9United States00aW1bCH648510aChild Dev Perspect2dnlm00aChild development perspectives.13aCDP  aMalden, Mass. :bBlackwell Pub. for the Society for Research in Child Development,c2007-  av. ;c28 cm.  aThree issues per year  aSemiannual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol.1, no. 1 published in Oct. 2007.  aDescription based on first issue; title from cover.  aPrint issues ceased with v. 8 (2014).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aFirst issue lacks chronology.  aAlso issued online.12aChild Development 2aPeriodical2 aSociety for Research in Child Development.0 x1750-86064 uhttp://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1750-8606  aAUTH01363cgm a22004094a 101267926DNLM20260227145850.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2000    mdu028 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11067  a(OCoLC)70873940  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWJ 7621 aWurzburg, Gerardine.10aTake charge /cGerry Wurzburg.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2000]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed July 28, 2006).  aStreaming video (27 min., 13 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 2, 2000.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aProstatic Neoplasmsxpsychology22aPatient Education as Topic22aSocial Support 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11067  aAUTH02513cgm a22004334a 101468731DNLM20260227152355.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080307s2008    mdu062|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14305  a(OCoLC)219261787  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 4501 aIdeker, Trey.10aMapping gene regulatory pathways by assembly of physical and genetic interactions /cTrey Ideker.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed Mar. 29, 2008).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 2 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Feb. 19, 2008.3 a(CIT): Physical and genetic mapping data have become as important to Network Biology as they were to the Human Genome Project. Physical interaction maps are being constructed through systematic measurements of protein-protein, protein-DNA, and protein-small molecule interactions. Genetic interaction maps are being generated by large-scale screening of synthetic-lethals and epistasis, by multipoint gene association studies, and by mapping the effects of natural and prescribed genetic variations on gene expression. We are working on ways of integrating physical and genetic interaction maps to assemble models of gene regulatory pathways. These efforts face several challenges, including: increasing the coverage of each type of network; establishing methods to assemble individual interaction measurements into contiguous pathway models; and annotating these pathways with detailed functional information. Efforts in each of these areas will be described. Using integrative tools, we are constructing network models to explain the physiological response of yeast to DNA damaging agents.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aChromosome Mapping22aComputational Biologyxmethods22aGene Expression Regulation22aGene Regulatory Networksxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bSystems Biology Special Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14305  aAUTH01368cas a2200433 a 101530967DNLM20260227090912.0cr||||||||||||100324c20109999paubr p       0    0eng    a  20102018570 a2154-1264l2154-1272  a(OCoLC)568639985  aDLCcDLCdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW1bJR228JL10aTranscription2dnlm00aTranscription.  aAustin, TX :bLandes Bioscience3132015- :aPhiladelphia, PA :bTaylor & Francis  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, issue 1 (July/Aug. 2010).1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, July-Aug 2010-0 aPubMedbv1n1, July-Aug 2010-0 aPMC  aVol. 1 complete in three issues.  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Vol. 2, issue 1 (Jan./Feb. 2011); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 2, issue 1 (Jan./Feb. 2011).12aTranscription, Genetic 2aPeriodical0 x2154-12724 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/toc/ktrn20/current4 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101530967  aAUTH01599cas a2200457 a 9418292DNLM20260227091028.0cr|cn#||||||||940407c19939999nyuqr p       0    0eng    a1352-4658l1352-4658y0141-3473  a(DNLM)SR0079573(s)  a(OCoLC)28918424  aOAUcOAUdDNLM  9United States00aW1bBE135CR10aBehav Cogn Psychother2dnlm00aBehavioural and cognitive psychotherapy.  aLondon :bWisepress Ltd.,c1993-3 aNew York, NY :bCambridge University Press  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 21, no. 3-1 aMEDLINEbv37n1, Jan. 2009-0 aPubMedbv37n1, Jan. 2009-  aAlso issued online.  aJournal of the British Association for Behavioural and Cognitive Psychotherapies. 2aBehavior Therapy 2aCognitive Behavioral Therapy 2aMental Disordersxtherapy 2aPsychot