ecorded July 12 & 13, 2022.3 a(CIT): The goal of the Health Disparities in Osteoarthritis (OA) workshop, sponsored by NIAMS, NIA, and NIMHD, is to identify research gaps/needs that could be addressed in future NIH activities. The meeting will bring together OA investigators with others who have health disparities research expertise to exchange ideas regarding how/why disparities in OA treatment outcomes and access to care exist and how they can be addressed. It will highlight mechanisms through which integration of behavioral and biomedical science can lead to better health in OA.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed May 2, 2023).12aOsteoarthritisxepidemiology22aHealth Status Disparities22aSocial Determinants of Health22aHealth Services Accessibility22aPhysician-Patient Relations 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute of Arthritis and Musculoskeletal and Skin Diseases (U.S.),esponsoring body.2 aNational Institute on Aging,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institute on Minority Health and Health Disparities (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4500040uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45002  aAUTH01345cgm a2200409 a 101574470DNLM20260227154027.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u111208s2011    mdu073|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16946  a(OCoLC)778837489  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWH 2001 aZuniga-Pflucker, J. C.10aProgenitor T cells :bfrom in vitro generations to in vivo function /cJuan Zuniga-Pflucker.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2011]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 13 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aImmunology Interest Group Seminar  aRecorded Nov. 2, 2011.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aPrecursor Cell