ts and takeaways, ethicists, biomedical researchers, technology engineers and developers of hardware and software, public health experts, and clinician researchers who might utilize these technologies.  The NExTRAC WG will analyze and interpret the discussions from this event to inform the NExTRAC deliberations, which will ultimately be conveyed to NIH.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed October 25, 2024).12aBiomedical Researchxmethods22aData Aggregation22aData Curationxmethods22aCommunity Participation22aResearch Support as Topic22aResearch Design 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aUniversity of California, San Diego,ehost institution.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49084  aAUTH01159cas a2200361 i 101538787DNLM20260227090920.0cr||||||||||||100820c20049999fr || p       |    0fre    a  2010243955  a1769-4493l1769-4493  a(OCoLC)694609030  aDNLMcDNLMerdadDNLM  apcc  9France00aW1bME136H00aMédecine du sommeil.  aIssy-les-Moulineaux :bElsevier Masson SAS  aQuarterly  atext2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 2004.  aAlso issued online.  aSummaries in English and French; search interface in English.  aDescription based on: Vol. 7, no. 1 (Janvier/Mars 2010); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 7, no. 3 (Juillet/Septembre 2010).12aSleep Wake Disorders 2aPeriodical2 aSociété française de recherche et médecine du sommeil.4 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/17694493  aAUTH00811cam a22002537i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118245008400151264005900235300004100294336002600335337002800361338002700389600002100416650002400437650002600461651001000487710005100497999000900548101616135DNLM20260209145824.0130829s1967    cc ac      