ygiene.1 aJFSH 1aTehran, Iran :bTehran University of Medical Sciences,c[2015]-  a1 online resource  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, no 1 (Winter 2015).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aSome issues combined.  aVol. 1 complete in 2 issues.0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Winter 2015); title from journal homepage (publisher's website, viewed June 5, 2023).1 aVol. 9, no. 1 (Winter 2023) (viewed June 5, 2023).12aFood Safety22aHygiene22aFood Contaminationxprevention & control 2aPeriodical2 aDānishgāh-i ʻUlūm-i Pizishkī-i Tihrān,eissuing body.40uhttps://jfsh.tums.ac.ir/index.php/jfsh/index  aAUTH03502nam a2200565 i 9918986632406676DNLM20260220080936.0231125t20242024enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2023041293  a1396059398  a9781032464510qhardcover  a1032464518qhardcover  a9781032464503qpaperback  a103246450Xqpaperback  z9781003381723qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1396059412z(OCoLC)1396059398  aLBSORbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdYDXdOCLCOdIG#1 aenghita  apcc  ae-it---  9United Kingdom00aRC450.I82bS35 202400aWM 28 GI800a362.2/109451821223/eng/202312141 aSchinaia, Cosimo,d1951-eauthor.10aPresepe dei folli.lEnglish10aOutsider art and psychoanalytic psychiatry :bthe 'nativity of fools' at the Cogoleto Psychiatric Hospital /cCosimo Schinaia ; translated by Giuseppe Lo Dico and Kathryn Haralambous. 1aAbingdon, Oxon ;aNew York, NY :bRoutledge, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  axxxvi, 130 pages :bcolor illustrations;c25 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aPsychoanalytic ideas and applications series  aTranslation of: Il Presepe dei folli.  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aCogoleto Psychiatric Hospital -- Thinking beyond the asylum -- Projects and materials for a nativity scene in the asylum -- The nativity -- Segregation -- The square -- The doctors' office -- Electroshock -- The children's ward -- Work -- Death -- Between past and future.  a"Outsider Art and Psychoanalytic Psychiatry is a study of psychiatric institutes and psychiatric violence as seen through art created by the inhabitants of a psychiatric hospital. Cosimo Schinaia explores the history of the Cogoleto Psychiatric Hospital, now abandoned, and how its architecture and ideology influenced treatment of the patients who lived there. At the book's core is an in-depth historical, anthropological, and psychoanalytical study of the 'Nativity of Fools', a large art installation constructed from 1980 to 1984 by patients, nurses and psychiatrists, representing their everyday lives in the asylum. Schinaia's understanding of the scenes considers questions of nostalgia, isolation, privacy and freedom, and reflects on the risks of institutionalised segregation. The book proposes original psychoanalytic reflections on the subject of the obsolescence of psychiatric hospitals and treating mental suffering without institutionalising people. This book will be of great interest to psychoanalysts in practice and in training, psychiatrists, psychologists, social workers, and nurses as well as readers interested in outsider art, Arte Povera, and the history of psychiatric institutions and contemporary psychiatry"--cProvided by publisher.22aCogoleto Psychiatric Hospital.12aHospitals, Psychiatric12aArt22aPersons with Psychiatric Disorders22aCreativity22aArt Therapy 2aItaly1 aLo Dico, Giuseppe,d1979-etranslator.1 aHaralambous, Kathryn,etranslator. 0aPsychoanalytic ideas and applications series  aAUTH01650cgm a22004334a 101267595DNLM20260227145255.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2001    mdu009  |||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10423  a(OCoLC)71138916  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aW 20.51 aKirschstein, Ruth L.10aOpening remarks for Dr. Kirschstein /c2001 NIH Diversity For