nc2rdacarrier1 aState University of Iowa publication ;vnew series no. 1653  aNLM copy, bound 12th in a volume of 92 pamphlets.5DNLM22aState University of Iowa.bCollege of Medicine12aSchools, Medical 2aIowa2 aState University of Iowa,eissuing body. 0aState University of Iowa publication ;vnew ser. no. 1653.  aAUTH00998cam a22002777i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002200073040003500095044001800130060002500148110006200173245009700235264008300332300001300415336002600428337002800454338002700482500004900509610005300558650005400611650002800665651001800693999000900711101749121DNLM20260219155602.0190612s1951    ilu           000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)1110736724  aDNLMbengerdad20260219dDNLM  9United States00aWB 1 AA1bA849a 19512 aAssociation of American Physicians and Surgeons,eauthor.10aCode of medical practice and by-laws of the Association of American Physicians and Surgeons. 1aChicago, Illinois :bAssociation of American Physicians and Surgeons,c[1951?]  a15 pages  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"Reprinted with amendments, December, 1951."22aAssociation of American Physicians and Surgeons.12aSocieties, Medicalxorganization & administration12aConstitution and Bylaws 2aUnited States  aAUTH02269cgm a22004454a 101289634DNLM20260227151526.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061011s2006    mdu062  |||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13150  a(OCoLC)84709886  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 2951 aRutstein, David D.q(David Davis),d1909-1986.14aThe future of public health and medical support during disasters /cDavid Rutstein ; presented to the NIH Emergency Preparedness and Biodefense Interest Group.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Dec. 15, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 1 min., 28 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 6, 2006.3 a(CIT): Evident failures in the federal response to Hurricane Katrina led President Bush to call together a multi-agency "Katrina Lessons Learned Review Group" in September, 2005, to examine those deficiencies and make recommendations to improve national preparedness for major disasters.  The committee issued its report in February; Captain Rutstein represented DHHS in the Lessons Learned Review Group. He will first briefly review the course of Hurricane Katrina and areas of weakness in the federal response, then discuss the Review Group's recommendations for widespread reforms to foster a "culture of preparedness" and develop a new National Preparedness System.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.02aFederal response to Hurricane Katrina.12aDisaster Planningxorganization & administration22aOrganizational Culture22aPublic Policy22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bEmergency Preparedness and Biodefense Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13150  aAUTH02349cas a2200445 i 101767490DNLM20260224111541.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||190408c20199999gw || poo     0    0eng    a  2020243147  a2627-1850l2627-1850  a(OCoLC)1125749519  aSFBbengerdad20260224cSFBdZ5AdOCLCFdDNLM  apcc  9Germany00aW110aTransl Biophotonics2dnlm00aTranslational biophotonics.1 aTBIO 1aWeinheim :bWiley-VCH,c[2019]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1, issue 1/2 (December 2019).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aArticles are published as they become available before inclusion in an issue.  a"Translational medicine encompasses aspects of medicine from laboratory research, preclinical studies, clinical trials, clinical practice, through to diagnostics and therapy and combination technologies with a focus on cross-functional collaboration between researchers and clinicians.Translational Biophotonics (TBIO) is an international, peer-reviewed, open access journal dedicated to bridging the gap in translating medical photonic research into clinical practice. Optical and photonic technologies have proven their potential regarding specific diagnostic and therapeutic needs in proof-of-concept studies; however, their actual effectiveness has rarely been tested under routine clinical conditions on larger databases/patient cohorts."--Publisher.  aSome volumes contain special issues.  aSister journal to: Journal of biophotonics.0 aVolume 1, issue 1/2 (December 2019); title from journal home page (publisher's website, viewed June 10, 2020).1 aVolume 2, issue 1/2 (May 2020) (viewed June 10, 2020).12aOptics and Photonics22aTranslational Research, Biomedical. 2aPeriodical08iComplemented by (work):tJournal of biophotonicsx1864-063Xw(DLC)   2009243055w(OCoLC)30430280140uhttps://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/26271850  aAUTH02891nam a2200469 i 9918986640206676DNLM20260220080953.0230928t20242024enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2023044832  a1397313080a1397313930  a9781032663319qhardcover  a1032663316qhardcover  a9781032663296qpaperback  a1032663294qpaperback  z9781032663333qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1401004333z(OCoLC)1397313080z(OCoLC)1397313930  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdOCLCOdISUdOCLCOdYDXdPAUdBDX1 aenghheb  apcc  9England00aBF175.5.O33bE4813 202400aWM 46000a150.19/5223/eng/202309281 aEitan-Persico, Yifat,d1977-eauthor.10aMeshulash he-ḥadash.lEnglish10aOedipal experiences in same-sex families /cYifat Eitan-Persico. 1aAbingdon, Oxon ;aNew York, NY :bRoutledge, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  axxxi, 295 pages :billustrations (some color) ;c25 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aRelational perspectives  a"First English edition published 2023"--Title page verso.  a"First Hebrew edition published by the University of Haifa Press and Pardes Publishing, 2023"--Title page verso.  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"This book updates the Oedipus Complex for a contemporary audience in the light of social and cultural changes and explores its implications for psychoanalytic treatment and our understanding of queer families. Growing evidence during the past few decades indicates that children who grow up in same-sex families adapt well. These findings, which do not conform to the predictions of Oedipal theory, expose the theory's biases, and call for re-examination of its premises. This book based on ground-breaking research, pursues a methodical investigation of the characteristics of the same-sex family that defy the expectations of Oedipal theory. Furnished with vivid illustrations, it invites the reader to engage actively in the interpretive effort and presents a diverse and complex story about kinship, proffering a window onto a rich world of infantile phantasies and parents' psychological conflicts, at the fascinating intersection of the personal and the social. Oedipal Experiences in Same-Sex Families will appeal to psychoanalysts, psychotherapists, educators, and policymakers, same-sex parents, and parents who were assisted by gamete donation"--cProvided by publisher.12aOedipus Complex.22aFamily Relationsxpsychology 0aRelational perspectives book series  aAUTH01284nam a2200373 i 9918986633506676DNLM20260205105143.0201007s2021    ne a     b    001 0 eng    a  2020951448  aGBC0F88062bnb  a1130766990  a9780323683289qpaperback  a0323683282qpaperback  a(OCoLC)1202861704z(OCoLC)1130766990  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCOdBDXdOCLCFdYDXdZWUdOCLCOdNDDdOCLdYDXdDLCdOCLCOdOCLCLdIG#  apcc  an-us---  9Netherlands 4aRC568.O45bO76 202100aWM 28404a362.29322304aThe opioid e