umebnc2rdacarrier1 aInformes ;vnúmero 01/2024  a"Sesión ordinaria del Pleno de 28 de febrero de 2024."  aIncludes bibliographical references.22aSistema Nacional de Salud (Spain)12aNational Health Programs22aPublic Health Practice22aHealth Policy 2aSpain2 aConsejo Económico y Social (Spain),eissuing body. 0aColección Informes (Madrid, Spain) ;v2024/01.  aAUTH03280cgm a2200445 i 9918625745306676DNLM20260227163708.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230602s2023    mdu135|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33155  a(OCoLC)1455527122  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWA 300 AA12 aAnnual NIH Asian American, Native Hawaiian/Pacific Islander Health Research Conferencen(2nd :d2023 :cOnline)jauthor.10aAnnual NIH Asian American, Native Hawaiian/Pacific Islander Health Research Conference, May 3-4, 2023 :bcommenorating AANHPI May Heritage Month /csponsored by the National Cancer Institute ; host, NIH Asian American, Native Hawaiian, Pacific Islander Health Scientific Interest Group (AANHPI-HSIG). 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (2 hr., 15 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded May 3, 2023.3 a(CIT): A month-long annual observance in May, Asian American, Native Hawaiian/Pacific Islander (AANHPI) Heritage Month is to recognize the history and to celebrate the achievements and contributions of AANHPIs to our nation.  Following the successful inaugural NIH Annual AA and NHPI Health Research Conference on May 4-5, 2022 by Asian American, Native Hawaiian, and Pacific Islander Health Scientific Interest Group (NIH AAPI-HSIG) (agenda and recordings at: https://events.cancer.gov/nih/AANHPI-HSIG-Annual-Conference/agenda), NIH AANHPI-HSIG is hosting 2023 "Annual NIH AA and NHPI Health Research Conference" (virtual) on May 3-4th. This event is sponsored by the National Cancer Institute, NIH. HHS-wide participations in planning. This conference will bring together the world"s leading scientific and regulatory experts in the field of AA and NHPI research from government, academia, and the community. The event is open to the public. The PURPOSE: (1) celebrate and educate the AANHPI heritage, (2) highlight achievements in AA and NHPI health research and of AA and NHPI scientists, and (3) discuss AANHPI health research needs.   The 2023 Event THEME: " Improving the Health of AA and NHPI: Risk factors, Genetic ancestry, and Disease mechanisms."  https://events.cancer.gov/nih/AANHPI-HSIG-Conference.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 26, 2024).12aAsian American Native Hawaiian and Pacific Islander22aHealth Status Disparities22aTranslational Research, Biomedical22aRace Factors 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bAsian American, Native Hawaiian, Pacific Islander Health Scientific Interest Group,ehost.2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49711  aAUTH01339cgm a22003974a 101480538DNLM20260227152822.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080801s2008    mdu291|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14604  a(OCoLC)244264633  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWX 1732 aAmerican Health Information Community.bMeetingn(23rd :d2008 :cWashington, D.C.)10aAmerican Health Information Community :bJuly 2008 /cthe U.S. Department of Health and Human Services.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed Aug. 8, 2008).  aStreaming video (4 hr., 51 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded July 29, 2008.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aMedical Records Systems, Computerized22aHealth Policy 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14604  aAUTH01782cgm a2200409 i 101772135DNLM20260227151310.0m     o  z f      vz|czaz|ucr|cna||||||||201007s2013    mdu342 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:12908  a(OCoLC)1201223082  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 5052 aMERS-CoV Research: Current Status and Future Priorities Meetingd(2013 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aMERS-CoV Research :bCurrent Status and Future Priorities Meeting, Natcher Conference Center /cNIAID ; introduction by Anthony S. Fauci. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2013]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hrs. 42 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 24, 2013.3 a(CIT): This meeting will bring together leading virologists to discuss the current status of the coronavirus field in the context of the Middle East Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus (MERS-CoV).  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 20, 2020).12aCoronavirus Infections22aMiddle East Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings1 aFauci, Anthony S.,d1940-espeaker.2 aNational Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=12908  aAUTH02227cgm a2200445 i 9918681338906676DNLM20260227164150.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230929s2023    mdu535|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33482  a(DNLM)CIT:33484  a(OCoLC)1459861649  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 26.55.I42 aHINTS Data Users Conferenced(2023 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aHINTS data users conference :bcelebrating 20 years of HINTS 2023 /cNCI, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (8 hr., 55 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded September 21 & 22, 2023.3 a(CIT): The Health Information National Trends Survey (HINTS) routinely collects nationally representative data about the American public's access to health information, use of health information technology, and health-related knowledge, attitudes, and behaviors. The 2023 HINTS Data Users Conference will convene attendees from academic, private, and public sectors to share analyses of HINTS data on a broad range of topics in order to help the scientific community better understand information support needs in the population and plan more effective interventions for improving population health.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed August 28, 2024).22aHealth Information National Trends Survey.12aHealth Information Management22aRoutinely Collected Health Data22aHealth Knowledge, Attitudes, Practice 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.),ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4903740uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49039  aAUTH01514cgm a22003854a 101268000DNLM20260227145944.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2000    mdu375 ||||||f|   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11257  a(OCoLC)84671143  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWM 1882 aNational Center on Sleep Disorders Research (National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute).bSleep Disorders Research Advisory Board.bMeetingn(13th :d2000 :cBethesda, Md.)10aSleep Disorders Research Advisory Board :b[December 2000] /cNHLBI National Center on Sleep Disorders Research.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2000] 