 (Buffalo, N.Y.)  aAUTH01163nam a2200313 i 45000010017000000030005000170050017000220080041000390400025000800440011001050600023001161000045001392450062001842640077002463000041003233360026003643370028003903380027004185000016004455040041004615610130005026000037006326500028006696550014006976550020007117000055007317000054007869990009008409918734079806676DNLM20260211093013.0970701s1930    fr a     ab   000 0dfre    aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  9France00aWZ 100bR595e 19301 aRiser, Marcel Marie,d1891-1975,eauthor10aExposé des titres et travaux scientifiques du Dr Riser. 1aToulouse :bHenri Cléder ;aParis :bMasson et Cie, Éditeurs,c1930.  a100 pages :,billustrations ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"Mai 1930."  aIncludes bibliographical references,  aNLM copy, signed presentation inscription from Dr. Riser to Monsieur le Professeur Achard in blue ink on front flyleaf.5DNLM12aRiser, Marcel Marie,d1891-1975.12aNervous System Diseases 2aAbstracts 2aBiobibliography1 aRiser, Marcel Marie,d1891-1975,einscriber.5DNLM1 aAchard, Charles,d1860-1944,eformer owner.5DNLM  aAUTH02143cgm a2200445 i 101775916DNLM20260227160623.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210206s2020    mdu051|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31465  a(OCoLC)1241125204  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.500aSCORE Annual Meeting keynote.pSex differences research and the health of women :ban editor's perspective /cDr. Jocalyn Clark.1 aSex differences research and the health of women :ban editor's perspective 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2020]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (51 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded December 16, 2020.3 a(CIT): The Specialized Centers of Research Excellence on Sex Differences, or SCORE, program is the only NIH cooperative agreement program supporting disease-agnostic research on sex differences. Each center serves as a national resource for translational research to identify the role of biological sex differences in the health of women. At this year's SCORE Annual Meeting, Dr. Jocalyn Clark, Executive Editor of The Lancet, will present the keynote address: "Sex Differences Research and the Health of Women: An Editor's Perspective."  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed March 4, 2021).12aBiomedical Research22aSex Factors22aGender Identity22aPeriodicals as Topic22aWomen's Health 2aWebcast 2aAddress1 aClark, Jocalyn,cPh.D.espeaker.2 aSpecialized Centers of Research Excellence on Sex Differences (Program),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=40061  aAUTH01306cas a2200409 a 100883604DNLM20260227091048.0cr|cnu||||||||990112c19979999enkqr p       000  0eng    asn 99039672   a1460-4582l1460-4582y1355-4743  a(OCoLC)41732344  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcdansdp  9England00aW1bHE351210aHealth Informatics J2dnlm00aHealth informatics journal.  aSheffield, UK :bSheffield Academic Press,c[1997-3 aLondon :bSAGE Publications  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 3, no. 1 (Jan. 1997)-1 aMEDLINEbv12n1, Mar. 2006-1 aPubMedbv12n1, Mar. 2006-  aBeginning with 2021-, articles published as they are received and compiled into quarterly issues.  aAlso issued online.12aMedical Informatics 2aPeriodical0 x1741-281100tHealth informatics (Edinburgh, Scotland)x1355-4743w(DLC)sn 95038870w(OCoLC)332000954 uhttps://journals.sagepub.com/home/jhi  aAUTH01812cgm a2200469 i 101775939DNLM20260227160713.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210206s2021    mdu056|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31509  a(OCoLC)1248768420  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 506.500aInsights on viral and immune-mediated central nervous system pathology during SARS-CoV-2 infection /cShelli Farhadian.1 iTitle on PowerPoint screen:aNeurological complications during acute COVID-19 :bwhat can we learn from the bedside? 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (56 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNHLBI COVID-19 insights  aAccess restricted to NIH only.  aRecorded January 27, 2021.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed April 23, 2021).12aCOVID-19xcomplications22aCentral Nervous System Diseasesxetiology22aCentral Nervous System Diseasesxdiagnosis22aDiagnostic Techniques, Neurological22aCOVID-19xphysiopathology 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aFarhadian, Shelli,espeaker.2 aNational Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute,esponsoring body. 0aNHLBI COVID-19 insights webinar series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41357  aAUTH00888cam a22003017i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002100073040003500094044001000129060003200139100003500171245006200206250001400268264005400282300004100336336002600377336003300403337002800436338002700464650001200491650001000503650002100513655002400534655001900558999000900577101617685DNLM20260209150552.0130923s1961    cc a          000 0 chi    a(OCoLC)874960847  aDNLMbengerdad20260209dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1805 no.11 aYi, Fan,dactive 1961eauthor.10aJiang wei sheng shen ti hao /cYi Fan xie ; Yu Li hui tu.  aDi 1 ban. 1aShanghai :bShao nian er tong chu ban she,c1961.  a22 unnumbered pages :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aHygiene22aChild22aHealth Promotion 2aJuvenile Literature 2aPictorial Work  aAUTH03109cgm a2200457 i 101776740DNLM20260227160817.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210302s2021    mdu115|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31556  a(OCoLC)1249794955  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQW 10000aDemystifying medicine.pRole of microbiome in nutrition, inflammation and cancer /cYasmine Belkaid, Giorgio Trinchieri.1 aRole of microbiome in nutrition, inflammation and cancer 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 55 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 16, 2021.3 a(CIT): The human microbiome -- comprising the trillions of microorganisms that live on and in us -- is both an ancient and poorly explored frontier, defining our evolution and influencing our health in yet unknown ways.  Only in recent decades have we begun to understand the importance of the microbiome in preventing a broad range of diseases, such as obesity, diabetes, Parkinson"s disease, and cancer.  Yasmine Belkaid, Ph.D., is an NIH Distinguished Investigator and chief of the NIAID Metaorganism Immunity Section.  Her laboratory aims to understand the mechanisms controlling host microbe interactions at barrier sites such as the skin and the gut.  Her work has demonstrated that commensal organisms on the skin and in the gut play a critical role in host defense.  She has found that dietary factors control the induction of effector and regulatory responses in the gut, in particular, such as the induction of T cells and dendritic cells with regulatory functions.  Giorgio Trinchieri, M.D. is an NIH Distinguished Investigator, chief of the NCI Laboratory of Integrative Cancer Immunology, and head of the Cancer Immunology Section.  His lab's current focus is the role of inflammation, innate resistance, and commensal microbiota in carcinogenesis, cancer progression, and therapy of cancer.  He has previously identified the interplay between inflammation, adaptive immunity, and of the role of cytokines and interferons in the regulation of infections and cancer.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed May 3, 2021).12aMicrobiota22aNutritional Physiological Phenomena22aFood Microbiology22aInflammationxmicrobiology22aNeoplasmsxmicrobiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aBelkaid, Yasmine,espeaker.1 aTrinchieri, Giorgio,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bClinical Center,eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41286  aAUTH02076cas a2200505 a 101526034DNLM20260224111541.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||090603c20109999dcu|| pso     0   a0eng    a  20092031050 a1948-7185l1948-7185  a(OCoLC)369172846  aDLCcDLCdDLCdUABdCUSdDNLM  apccansdp  9United States 4aQD45000aW110a5412140 aJ. phys. chem. lett.10aJ Phys Chem Lett2dnlm 4aThe journal of physical chemistry letters04aThe journal of physical chemistry letters.13aJPC letters  aWashington, D.C. :bAmerican Chemical Society  aSemimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with vol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 7, 2010).1 aMEDLINEbv6n1, Jan. 2015-0 aPubMedbv6n1, Jan. 2015- ; Selected citations only before this date  aCovers all topic areas currently included in Journal of physical chemistry A, B, and C.  aBeginning with 2010 the Journal of physical chemistry letters replaces the section called Letters that appeared in Journal of physical chemistry A, B and C.  aDescription based on: Vol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 7, 2010); title from table of contents page (ACS Publications website, viewed Jan. 12, 2010).  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 6, no. 15 (Aug. 6, 2015) (viewed Aug. 12, 2015).12aChemical Phenomena 2aP