ited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aHamilton, Darrick,espeaker.2 aNational Institute on Aging,eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=34411  aAUTH01693cgm a22004694a 101549241DNLM20260227153827.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u101208s2010    mdu055 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16250  a(OCoLC)701450077  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWM 1721 aGill, Jessica M.10aInsights into the role of inflammation in post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) with and without depression /cJessica M. Gill.  Inflammatory profile for stroke diagnosis & outcome prediction / Taura L. Barr.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Clinical Center grand rounds lecture series  aTitle from title screen (viewed Feb. 2, 2011).  aStreaming video (55 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 3, 2010.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aStress Disorders, Post-Traumaticxetiology22aDepressive Disorderxcomplications22aInflammationxcomplications22aStroke22aTreatment Outcome 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)02aInflammatory profile for stroke diagnosis & outcome prediction. 0aClinical Center grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16250  aAUTH02400cgm a2200481 i 101778107DNLM20260227160941.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210408s2021    mdu999 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31606  a(DNLM)CIT:31607  a(DNLM)CIT:31608  a(OCoLC)1291166327  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 141.5.N472 aTransformative Non-Invasive Imaging Technologies (Workshop)d(2021 March :cOnline)jauthor.10aTransformative non-invasive imaging technologies /cNIH BRAIN Initiative. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (21 hr., 3 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 9, 10 & 11, 2021.3 a(CIT): Non-invasive brain functional imaging with high sensitivity and specificity is a central aim of the BRAIN Initiative. With the latest engineering advances, new imaging tools that could make a long-lasting, transformative impact on human neuroscience could likely to emerge in the near future. The goal of this workshop is to bring together neuroscientists, tool developers/engineers, and industry partners to discuss what new non-invasive functional imaging tools could be realized in the next five to ten years, their potential impact on human neuroscience research, and possible pathways forward for broader dissemination.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed December 27, 2021).12aFunctional Neuroimaging12aBrain Diseasesxdiagnostic imaging22aMinimally Invasive Surgical Procedures22aBrainxdiagnostic imaging 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aBRAIN Initiative,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4018240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4018340uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=40184  aAUTH01247cgm a2200385 i 101642833DNLM20260227154703.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u140926s2014    mdu068       fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18628  a(OCoLC)894125339  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 5341 aBausch, Daniel,eauthor.10aEbola virus infection /cDaniel Bausch. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 8 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded Sept. 19, 