-captioned.22aNational Centers for Biomedical Computing (U.S.)12aComputational Biology22aPeer Review, Researchxstandards22aResearch Support as Topicxorganization & administration 2aWebcast1 aAmero, Sally A.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12568  aAUTH01578cgm a22004454a 101267389DNLM20260227145005.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2002    mdu899 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:9992  a(DNLM)CIT:9993  a(DNLM)CIT:9994  a(OCoLC)85885128  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWC 53600aManagement of hepatitis C, 2002 /cNIDDK ... [et al.].  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2002]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Feb. 26, 2007).  aStreaming video (14 hr., 59 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 10-12, 2002.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aHepatitis Cxtherapy 2aConference Proceedings 2aConsensus Development Conference, NIH 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?999240uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?999340uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?9994  aAUTH02308cgm a2200433 a 101552186DNLM20260227153723.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u110119s2010    mdu720 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16313  a(DNLM)CIT:16319  a(OCoLC)702604696  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aW 84.32 aNIH/AHRQ Conference on Methodological Challenges in Comparative Effectiveness Researchd(2010 :cNational Institutes of Health)10aNIH/AHRQ Conference on Methodological Challenges in Comparative Effectiveness Research /cNIH & AHRQ.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (12 hr., 21 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 2, 2010.3 a(CIT): The conference will make use of case studies that pose difficult questions about what kinds of research, methods and analyses should be used to address limitations in current evidence for interventions and tests being examined by decision-making bodies. The cases will address a variety of important comparative effectiveness research questions facing U.S. researchers, care providers, health systems, and patients. This conference is being convened at a historic moment for the biomedical, clinical, biostatistical, research design and health services research communities. With the passage of the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), the nation stands at a critical juncture, as it ramps up efforts to streamline the delivery of high quality healthcare, bend the cost curve and ensure improved health outcomes.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aComparative Effectiveness Researchxmethods22aResearch Design 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1631340uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16319  aAUTH02370cgm a2200397 a 101537550DNLM20260227153632.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100804s2010    mdu326|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16030  a(OCoLC)732774682  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWS 350.8.P42 aInteragency Autism Coordinating Committee (U.S.)10aIACC Committee Meeting, July 2010 /cThomas Insel.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 26 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded July 16, 2010.3 a(CIT): The Interagency Autism Coordinating Committee (IACC) is a Federal advisory committee that coordinates all efforts within the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) concerning autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Through its inclusion of both Federal and public members, the IACC helps to ensure that a wide range of ideas and perspectives are represented and discussed in a public forum.  The IACC mission is to:  Provide advice to the Secretary of Health and Human Services regarding Federal activities related to autism spectrum disorder.   Facilitate the exchange of information on and coordination of ASD activities among the member agencies and organizations.   Increase public understanding of the member agencies' activities, programs, policies, and research by providing a public forum for discussions related to ASD research and services.   IACC meetings are open to the public and include presentations and discussions on a variety of topics, including activities and projects of the IACC, recent advances in science and autism policy issues. A portion of each meeting is reserved for public  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aChild Development Disorders, Pervasive 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aInsel, Thomas R.,d1951-40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16030  aAUTH01510cgm a22004454a 101268260DNLM20260227150258.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s1999    mdu092 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11586  a(OCoLC)71464140  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 4501 aRied, Thomas.10aCytogenetic mapping methods /cThomas Ried.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c1999]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCurent topics in genome analysis series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Aug. 23, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 31 min., 35 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jan. 26, 1999.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government.  No copyright exists on this material.  It may be disseminated freely.12aChromosome Mapping22aChromosome Aberrations22aCytogenetic Analysis22aNeoplasmsxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aCurrent topics in genome analysis40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11586  aAUTH01549cgm a22004334a 101268262DNLM20260227150303.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s1999    mdu090 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11588  a(OCoLC)71464149  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 4501 aReeves, Roger Harper,d1953-10aGenetic mapping in mouse /cRoger Reeves ; hosted by the National Human Genome Research Institute.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c1999]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCurrent topics in genome analysis series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Aug. 23, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 29 min., 30 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Feb. 9, 1999.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government.  No copyright exists on this material.  It may be disseminated freely.12aChromosome Mapping22aMicexgenetics22aRecombination, Genetic 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Human Genome Research Institute (U.S.) 0aCurrent topics in genome analysis40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11588  aAUTH01792cgm a22004214a 101268279DNLM20260227150331.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2003    mdu055 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11617  a(OCoLC)70873964  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQW 5731 aReth, Michael.10aInitiation and feedback regulation of the B cell antigen receptor signaling /cMichael Reth.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed July 28, 2006).  aStreaming video (54 min., 12 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 29, 2003.3 a(CIT): The Immunology Interest Group (IIG) organizes activities designed to promote information exchange and interactions among NIH scientists interested in the field of immunology, broadly defined. Interactions are facilitated via weekly meetings on current topics as well as an annual Immunology Retreat.  For more information, visit The Immunology Interest Group.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aReceptors, Antigen, B-Cell22aSignal Transduction 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11617  aAUTH03288cgm a2200493 a 101585229DNLM20260227154135.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120525s2012    mdu071|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17210  a(OCoLC)803799292  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWC 3351 aBrady, S. Kalaniq(Stephen Kalani),d1955-10aKalaupapa and Father Damien :bhere I am send me /cS. Kalani Brady.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 11 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Apr. 13, 2012.3 a(CIT): S. Kalani Brady MD, the primary care physician of the remaining Hansen's disease (leprosy) patients at Kalaupapa, Hawaii, will speak at the National Library of Medicine in honor of St. Damien's Day on April 13, 2012. Dr. Brady's talk is titled, "Kalaupapa and Father Damien: 'Here I am send me.'"    Dr. Brady is an expert on Kalaupapa's legacy, Father Damien (beatified as St. Damien by Pope John Paul II in 1995), and contemporary care issues. Interviews with Dr. Brady as well as a patient and caregiver at Kalaupapa are among the highlights of NLM's current exhibition, Native Voices: Native Peoples' Concepts of Health and Illness (http://www.nlm.nih.gov/nativevoices), on display at NLM through fall of 2013. There is also a section about Kalaupapa's legacy within the exhibition.   St. Damien's Day is an annual Hawaiian statewide holiday in commemoration of the priest who pioneered housing, food distribution, and health care for Kalaupapa's residents at the end of the 19th century. From the mid-19th to the mid-20th century, about 8,000 persons with Hansen's disease were exiled to Kalaupapa, a remote peninsula on the Hawaiian island of Molokai. The plight of Kalaupapa's patients in the late 19th - early 20th century was chronicled by authors Robert Louis Stevenson and Jack London.   Dr. Brady is an associate professor, John A. Burns School of Medicine, Department of Native Hawaiian Health, University of Hawaii at Manoa, and is chief of the medical staff, Kalaupapa Clinic. Dr. Brady is a fellow of the American College of Physicians and is board certified in internal medicine. Dr. Brady is featured in a periodic segment that answers patient health questions on a Honolulu commercial television station and is also a well-known musician in Hawaii.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aDamien,cFather, Saint,d1840-1889.12aLeprosyxhistory22aCatholicismxhistory22aHistory, 19th Century22aHistory, 20th Century22aLeper Coloniesxhistory22aMissionaries22aReligious Missions 2aHawaii 2aBiography 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17210  aAUTH01501cgm a22004694a 101468722DNLM20260227152408.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080307s2008    mdu062 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14285  a(OCoLC)316418333  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc