 This core dataset of outcome measures will be used in future NIH-funded music-based intervention protocols.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 13, 2022).12aBrain Diseasesxtherapy12aMusic Therapy22aAged22aTreatment Outcome22aAlzheimer Disease 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aNational Institute of Health (U.S.),esponsoring body,eissuing body.2 aFoundation for the National Institutes of Health (U.S.),esponsoring body.2 aRenée Fleming Foundation,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41753  aAUTH02085cgm a2200469 i 9918230800606676DNLM20260227161355.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210707s2021    mdu303|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31796  a(OCoLC)1263659981  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 506.22 aSummit on Anti-SARS-CoV-2 Antibodies for Treatment and Prevention of COVID-19d(2021 :cOnline)jauthor.10aSummit on Anti-SARS-CoV-2 Antibodies for Treatment and Prevention of COVID-19 :blessons learned and remaining questions /cDr. Francis Collins, Dr. Janet Woodcock, Dr. Anthony Fauci. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 3 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 15, 2021.3 a(CIT): To summarize current knowledge and lessons learned on clinically relevant anti-SARS-CoV-2 antibodies for the treatment and/or prevention of COVID-19 and to identify key unanswered scientific questions to catalyze antibody clinical development and implementation.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed August 11, 2021).12aCOVID-19xtherapy22aCOVID-19xprevention & control22aSARS-CoV-2ximmunology22aAntibodies, Viralximmunology22aCOVID-19 Serological Test