T): NIH Town Hall  The 4th NIH Virtual Town Hall which will focus on safety as staff in Group A start to return to their physical workspaces in some locations, and provide answers to pre-submitted questions.  Moderated by Francis Collins, NIH Director, joined by leadership: Alfred Johnson, NIH Deputy Director for Management, Julie Berko, Director, NIH Office of Human Resources, and Jessica McCormick-Ell, Director, NIH Division of Occupational Health and Safety.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed August 6, 2020).22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aAcademies and Institutes12aBiomedical Research22aCoronavirus Infectionsxprevention & control22aPandemics22aUnited States Government Agencies22aSafety Management22aWorkplace 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aCollins, Francis S.,espeaker,emoderator.1 aJohnson, Alfred,espeaker.1 aBerko, Julie,espeaker.1 aMcCormick-Ell, Jessica,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?29181  aAUTH01130cam a22003011  450000100100000000300050001000500170001500700140003200800410004603500200008704000210010704400110012806000210013910000270016024500870018725000110027426000510028530000110033633600260034733700280037333800270040150000570042853301100048554001420059558300390073758300430077699900090081912610310RDNLM20260206142421.0hd|bfa012baap810725s1926    bl ||||  |||| 00||0|por    a(OCoLC)14745203  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Brazil00aQZ 4bR788n 19261 aRosa, Alvaro do Couto.10aNotas de anatomia e physiologia pathologicasc[por] Alvaro do Couto Rosa [et al.].  a2. ed.  aRio de Janeiro,bRevista dos tribunaes,c1926.  a388 p.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 5983 no. 55DNLM  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d1993.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202602062pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202602065DNLM  aAUTH01265cas a2200397 a 101543518DNLM20260227090924.0cr||||||||||||100308c20119999nyubr p       0    0eng    a  20102018410 a2153-7658l2153-7658  a(OCoLC)547116681  aDLCcDLCdDLCdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW1bTH45510aTher Hypothermia Temp Manag2dnlm00aTherapeutic hypothermia and temperature management.  aNew Rochelle, NY :bMary Ann Liebert, Inc.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, no. 1 (2011).1 aMEDLINEbv4n1, Mar. 2014-0 aPubMedbv4n1, Mar. 2014- ; selected citations only before this date  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Vol. 1, no. 1 (2011); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 1, no. 1 (2011).12aHypothermia, Induced22aBody Temperature Regulation 2aPeriodical0 x2153-79334 uhttp://online.liebertpub.com/loi/ther  aAUTH02088cgm a2200445 i 101604601DNLM20260227154433.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u130322s2013    mdu056|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17801  a(OCoLC)841556697  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 704.61 aBushnell, Catherine,eauthor.10aNeural basis of mind-body pain therapies /cCatherine Bushnell. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2013]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (56 min.) :bcolor, sound).  atwo-dimensional moving image2rdacontent  acomputer2rdamedia  aonline resource2rdacarrier1 aNCCAM integrative medicine research lecture series  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded Feb. 11, 2013.3 a(CIT): This lecture will focus on the growing problem of chronic pain. Chronic pain has reached epidemic levels in the US, with more than 100 million American adults affected. Pain is costing our nation more than $600 billion each year. To face this growing problem, many people are turning to mind-body therapies, such as relaxation, meditation, yoga and cognitive-behavioral therapy, to help manage chronic pain. This lecture will address how these therapies alter pain processing and pain modulation in the brain, as well as how they may be protective against brain aging.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed Apr. 27, 2013.12aPain Managementxmethods22aMind-Body Therapies22aPain Perceptionxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNCCAM complementary and integrative medicine consult service lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17801  aAUTH02036cgmaa22004934a 101181162DNLM20260227144358.0vf|cbahoucr|cnu||||||||vd|cvaizuhd|bfa012baap030604s2003    mdu060       f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:1695  a(OCoLC)53286016  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aWF 668bVC no.13 200304aThe artificial lung :bbench to bedside via Bethesda /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3master.  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3viewing copy.  a1 videodisc of 1 (DVD) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c4 3/4 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aClinical Center grand rounds great teachers lecture series  aSpeaker, Robert H. Bartlett.  a"March 12, 2003."  aAlso available online.  aVideodisc (DVD)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2019.e1 videodisc (60 min.) : sd., col. ; 4 3/4 in.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM12aExtracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation12aLungxsurgery22