ot.  aEdinburgh ;aNew York :bChurchill Livingstone,cc1991-  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Apr. 1991)-  aFour issues per yr.  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv18n2, Mar. 2008-0 aPubMedbv18n2, Mar. 2008-  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 1, no. 1 (APR 1991)c19910515fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aFoot Diseases 2aFootxsurgery 2aPeriodical0 x1532-29634 uhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/the-foot  aAUTH02951cgm a2200445 a 101601860DNLM20260227154420.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u130208s2013    mdu091|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17753  a(OCoLC)828715807  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 900.11 aMurray, Christopher J. L.14aThe global burden of disease study :bwhat does it mean for the NIH and global health research? /cChris Murray.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2013]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 31 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Jan. 17, 2013.3 a(CIT): Please join the Fogarty International Center for a presentation and discussion regarding The Global Burden of Disease 2010 study, published recently in The Lancet. Presentation by Dr. Chris Murray and Colleagues Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME) University of Washington Co-author, The Global Burden of Disease 2010 study What diseases cause the greatest numbers of deaths and disabilities? They might not be what you'd expect. Hear the results of The Global Burden of Disease 2010 study from the senior author and his team. Come armed with the questions most pertinent to your research area so you can join in the discussion. The recent GBD 2010 study is the largest single report ever published by The Lancet. The project is a systematic, scientific effort to quantify the comparative magnitude of deaths and disability due to diseases, injuries and risk factors by age, sex and geography with a look at these trends over time. The GBD construct of the burden of disease is health loss, not income or productivity loss. For decision makers, health-sector leaders, researchers and informed citizens, this approach provides an opportunity to see the big picture, to compare diseases, injuries and risk factors, and to grasp the most important contributors to health loss.   For more information go to <a href='http://www.fic.nih.gov/News/Events/Pages/lecture-chris-murray-health-metrics-global-burden-disease.aspx'>http://www.fic.nih.gov/News/Events/Pages/lecture-chris-murray-health-metrics-global-burden-disease.aspx.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aHealth Status Indicators22aBiomedical Research22aGlobal Health22aHealth Status22aInternationality 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aFogarty International Center.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17753  aAUTH00803cam a22002537i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118245006100151250001400212264007400226300003000300336002100330337002500351338002300376490003400399650004800433700002500481830003400506999000900540101607304DNLM20260205124109.0130501s1961    cc a          000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdad20260205dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1773 no.1900aChan hou liu xue de yu fang ji chu li /cLi Wangni bian.  aDi 1 ban. 1aBeijing :bRen min wei sheng chu ban she,c1961 nian 5 yue [May 1961]  a50 pages :billustrations  atext2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier1 aFu you bao jian xiao cong shu12aPostpartum Hemorrhagexprevention & control1 aLi, Wangni,eeditor. 0aFu you bao jian xiao cong shu  aAUTH01633cgm a22004574a 101268603DNLM20260227150831.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2004    mdu060 ||||