101684392DNLM20260227155347.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u160601s2016    mdu055|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19663  a(OCoLC)952152909  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWA 11000aEmerging infectious diseases in the 21st century :ba prevention paradigm for surveillance, information sharing & health diplomacy /cJonna Mazet. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (55 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aJoseph Leiter memorial lecture  aRecorded May 4, 2016.3 a(CIT): Dr. Mazet's specialty is studying diseases that could jump from an animal host population to a human population, such as SARS and Ebola.  She will talk about the project and how to disseminate information to relevant agencies and groups to help prevent a pandemic or at least keep it smaller.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed June 14, 2016).12aCommunicable Diseases, Emergingxtransmission22aDisease Reservoirs22aDisease Transmission, Infectiousxprevention & control22aZoonoses 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aMazet, Jonna,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aJoseph Leiter lecture40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19663  aAUTH01485cas a2200481 a 8100317DNLM20260227091005.0cr|cn ||||||||810115c19809999ja  x m       0    0eng    a0388-6107l0388-6107  aBRESD5  a(DNLM)B18490000(s)  a(OCoLC)07111884  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aeng  9Japan00aW1bBI856C0 aBiomedical research (Tokyo, Japan)10aBiomed Res2dnlm 0aBiomedical researchb(Tokyo)10aBiomedical research.30aBiomedical research (Tokyo)  aTokyo :bBiomedical Research Foundation,c1980-  av. :bill.  aSix no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrie