 including Phase 1 research, randomization, children in research, international research, etc.  Identify the critical elements of informed consent and strategies for implementing informed consent for clinical research.  Describe the purpose, function, and challenges of IRBs.   Appreciate the experience of human subjects who have participated in research protocols.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aTissue Banksxethics12aTissue Preservationxethics22aEthics, Research22aRandomized Controlled Trials as Topicxethics22aResearch Design 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16188  aAUTH01738cgm a22004814a 101549225DNLM20260227153754.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u101208s2010    mdu053|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16232  a(OCoLC)698580040  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQV 7711 aThompson, Susan,d1957 May 19-10aGCP and responsibilities of the PI and research team /cSusan Thompson.1 iTitle on PowerPoint:aFDA expectations of clinical investigators  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (53 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 28, 2010.3 a(CIT): Dr. Susan Thompson is coming from the FDA to give a lecture on GCP and Responsibilities of the PI and Research Team when conduction FDA regulated clinical research.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aUnited States.bFood and Drug Administration12aResearch Personnelxstandards22aClinical Trials as Topicxstandards22aDrug Evaluationxstandards22aDrugs, Investigationalxstandards22aGovernment Regulation 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16232  aAUTH01750cas a2200505   7608465D