u017 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10583  a(OCoLC)70051253  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWR 2651 aBrooks, P. J.q(Philip J.)10aRepair of a cyclopurine lesion in DNA by nucleotide excision repair :bimplications for neurodegeneration in xeroderma pigmentosum /cP.J. Brooks.1 iTitle on PowerPoint screen:aRepair of 8,5'-cyclo-2'-deoxyadenosine by nucleotide excision repair (NER) :bimplications for neurodegeneration in xeroderma pigmentosum  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c1999]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed May 10, 2006).  aStreaming video (16 min., 55 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 23, 1999.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This videocast is the work of the United States Government and no copyright exists.  This may be disseminated freely.12aXeroderma Pigmentosumxgenetics22aDeoxyadenosines22aDNA Damage22aDNA Repair 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10583  aAUTH02849cgm a2200469 i 9918332582406676DNLM20260227161756.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220104s2021    mdu502|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32059  a(DNLM)CIT:32067  a(OCoLC)1312792961  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQV 7452 aAssay Guidance Manual Training Workshopsd(2021 November 16-17 :cOnline)jauthor.10aAssay Guidance Workshop for Cell-Based Assays and Lead Discovery /cNCATS, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (8 hr., 22 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded November 16 & 17, 2021.3 a(CIT): The NCATS Assay Guidance Manual (AGM) program is hosting a two-day workshop that will cover a broad range of critical concepts underlying high-content screening and analysis (Day 1) and complex in vitro models (CIVMs) in drug discovery (Day 2). This workshop is designed to disseminate critical information about the implementation of robust cellular assay methods and is particularly relevant for researchers developing molecular probes or clinical candidates. Many of the workshop instructors have 20 to 30 years of experience in the field of drug discovery and will share information not readily found in a classroom or published material outside of the AGM.  The goal of this workshop is to train scientists on the fundamentals and applications of image-based and 3D cellular assay technologies and engage in a dialogue with those curious to understand it on a deeper level. This workshop also aims to discuss challenges and standards for rigor to enable reproducible results, and provide a future perspective on the utility of complex cellular models in drug discovery.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 21, 2022).12aDrug Discoveryxmethods22aHigh-Throughput Screening Assaysxmethods22aIn Vitro Techniquesxmethods22aCell Culture Techniques22aImage Processing, Computer-Assisted 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNational Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4413240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44130  aAUTH02782cgm a2200457 i 9918503180806676DNLM20260227162709.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u221105s2022    mdu647|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32647  a(DNLM)CIT:32654  a(OCoLC)1411026736  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWH 7002 aYet to be Charted: Lymphatic System in Health and Disease (Workshop) :d(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aYet to be charted :blymphatic system in health and disease /cNIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (10 hr., 47 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded September 19 & 20, 2022.3 a(CIT): NIH is hosting a research workshop in September to help us better understand how the lymphatic system develops and functions in sickness and in health. The workshop aims to improve how we manage and treat lymphatic disorders. Hosted by the NHLBI and the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) in coordination with the Trans-NIH Lymphatic Coordinating Committee, the workshop will bring together basic, clinical, and translational scientists, along with members of the lymphatics community, to explore the latest advances in the field and share research progress.  International experts will discuss current research, explore knowledge gaps, and identify opportunities in lymphatic disease research. People with lymphedema, lipedema, and other lymphatic diseases will share their personal experiences. Workshop organizers hope the event will build collaborative partnerships among scientists, clinicians, patients, and patient advocates. Featured topics include lymphedema and the role of lymphatics in obesity. This virtual event is free and open to the public.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed November 6, 2023).12aLymphatic System22aLymphatic Diseases22aLymphedema22aObesity 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute,ehost institution.2 aNational Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (U.S.),ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4591240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45914  aAUTH02778cgm a2200457 i 9918503182206676DNLM20260227162635.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u221105s2022    mdu359|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32599  a(OCoLC)1378182835  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWZ 10000aScience, society, and the legacy of Donald A.B. Lindberg, M.D. /cNLM, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 59 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aLindberg-King lecture and scientific symposium ;v2022  aRecorded September 1, 2022.3 a(CIT): This virtual Lindberg-King Lecture & Scientific Symposium: Science, Society, and the Legacy of Donald A.B. Lindberg, M.D., honors the legacy and contributions of the former NLM Director, Donald A.B. Lindberg, M.D., and the former NLM Deputy Director for Research and Education, Donald West King, M.D. The event, co-sponsored by NLM and Friends of the National Library of Medicine (FNLM), will bring together a diverse group of speakers from various academic and professional institutions and will explore a range of topics such as bioinformatics, precision medicine, computing, and library management. It will include a keynote address by Isaac S. Kohane, M.D., Ph.D., of the Harvard Medical School Department of Biomedical Informatics; panels on both Dr. Lindberg"s leadership in the advancement of science through research training as well as the evolution of the library as research partner; and remarks by leaders of NIH, NLM, FNLM, the NLM Board of Regents, the American Medical Informatics Association, and the Medical Library Association.  For more information, visit  https://www.nlm.nih.gov/news/NLM_Lindberg_King_Lecture_Scientific_Symposium.html.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 10, 2023).12aLindberg, Donald A. B.,d1933-2019.22aNational Library of Medicine (U.S.)12aPhysicians22aMedical Informatics 2aUnited S