ation Psychology.00tInternational journal of aviation psychologyx1532-7108w(DLC)   2001214595w(OCoLC)4500719640uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/hiap20  aAUTH03413nam a2200469 i 9918986575906676DNLM20260227073232.0230531t20242024fluac    b    001 0 eng    a  2023003284  aGBC3G32052bnb  a1432099109  a9781032416861qhardcover  a1032416866qhardcover  a9781032416847qpaperback  a103241684Xqpaperback  z9781003359241qelectronic book  z9781000913095qelectronic publication  z9781000913088qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1367932318z(OCoLC)1432099109  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdUKMGBdOCLCOdOCLCQdYDXdAUV  apcc  9United States00aQP187b.S36225 202400aWK 9000a573.4223/eng/202306261 aSchreiber, A. M.c(Endocrinologist),eauthor.10aGeneral and comparative endocrinology :ban integrative approach /cA.M. Schreiber.  aFirst edition. 1aBoca Raton :bCRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  axix, 657 pages :billustrations (some color), portraits ;c29 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aUnit I: Introduction to endocrinology -- Chapter 1: The scope and growth of endocrinology -- Chapter 2: Fundamental features of endocrine signaling -- Chapter 3: Evolution of endocrine signaling -- Unit II: Mechanisms of hormone action -- Chapter 4: Hormone classes and biosynthesis -- Chapter 5: Receptors -- Chapter 6: Receptor binding kinetics -- Unit III: Neuroendocrinology -- Chapter 7: Neurosecretion and hypothalamic control of the pituitary -- Chapter 8: The pituitary gland and its hormones -- Chapter 9: Central control of biological rhythms -- Unit IV: Developmental endocrinology -- Chapter 10: Thyroid hormones - development and growth -- Chapter 11: Insect molting and metamorphosis -- Chapter 12: Calcium/phosphate homeostasis, skeletal remodeling, and growth -- Unit V: Stress, blood pressure, and ion balance -- Chapter 13: The multi-faceted adrenal gland -- Chapter 14: Adrenal hormones and the stress response -- Chapter 15: Blood pressure and osmoregulation -- Unit VI: Appetite, digestion, and metabolism -- Chapter 16: Digestion -- Chapter 17: Appetite -- Chapter 18: Energy homeostasis -- Chapter 19: Metabolic dysregulation and disruption -- Unit VII: Reproduction -- Chapter 20: Sexual determination and differentiation -- Chapter 21: Male reproductive system -- Chapter 22: Female reproductive system -- Chapter 23: The timing of puberty and seasonal reproduction -- Chapter 24: Pregnancy, birth, and lactation -- Unit VIII: Endocrine-disrupting chemicals -- Chapter 25: EDC's - assessing the risk -- Appendices  a"Integrative & Comparative Endocrinology takes a holistic approach to endocrinology, introducing students to the diverse facets of this interdisciplinary science ranging from the medical to comparative domains, while also exploring evolutionary, environmental, and conservation specializations within the field"--cProvided by publisher.12aEndocrine System22aEndocrine System Diseases22aEndocrinologyxmethods  aAUTH02192cgm a2200433 i 101716405DNLM20260227155731.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u171107s2017    mdu111 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:23535  a(OCoLC)1013594427  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWP 87000aTRACO 2017.pBreast cancer and SCLC /cFarah Zia, Haobin Chen.1 aBreast cancer and SCLC1 aTranslational research in clinical oncology 2017.pBreast cancer and small cell lung cancer 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2017]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 51 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded October 23, 2017.3 a(CIT): Translational Research in Clinical Oncology (TRACO)  Recent advances in understanding cancer biology are beginning to be translated into improvements in diagnosis and treatment of cancer. In the post-genome era, we increasingly rely on strong collaboration between basic and clinical scientists to develop novel approaches for treatment of human disease. The NCI Center for Cancer Research (CCR) is one of the largest cancer research organizations in the world, with more than 200 principal investigators, and has played a major role in developing and implementing many new technologies, such as nanotechnology, next generation sequencing, genomics and proteomics.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed November 22, 2017).12aBreast Neoplasms12aSmall Cell Lung Carcinoma 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aZia, F.q(Farah),espeaker.1 aChen, Haobin,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?23535  aAUTH02212ngmaa2200385 i 101773057DNLM20260210075225.0mr|cf##dunaoauuac202011c|#c|#010m|abpc|#c|#010m|cbac|#c|#008m|cba201105q1960    mdu012       f    mleng    aDNLMbengerdaeamimcDNLM  9United States00aWE 25000aDiaphyseal aclasia in the Marianas.  aUnited States. 1aBethesda, MD :bNational Institutes of Health,c[1960?].  a1 film reel of 1 (400 ft.) :bcolor, silent ;c16 mm3duplicate positive.  a1 online resource (1 digital preservation file (12 min.)) :bcolor, silent, FFV13preservation copy.  a1 online resource (1 production video file (12 min.)) :bcolor, silent, ProRes3mezzanine copy.  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (12 min.)) :bcolor, silent, H2643viewing copy.9DREP  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  aprojectedbg2rdamedia  afilm reelbmr2rdacarrier  aLast inspected: Answer print, 20240924 B-Wind; Double Perforation; Color Reversal; Silent; Acetate Base; Cupping; Edgewave; Edge Notches; Existing Splices; Opening Splices; Existing Repairs; Shrunken; 24 FPS; Ansco and Kodachrome stocks; 1958 Kodak date code; 0.85% shrinkage; processing streaks5DNLM  aFootage of doctors trying to identify a bone condition in patients called diaphyseal aclasia, charaterized by the development of multiple osteochondromas. Doctors use x-rays to locate tumors. They also manipulate patients' limbs to test joint mobility.  aElectronic reproductionsbBethesda, MD :cNational Library  of Medicine,d2021.eX files (12 min. each)  : color, silentnCreated by Media Preserve.   aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM12aExostoses, Multiple Hereditaryxdiagnosis 2aMicronesia 2aUnedited Footage2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.  aAUTH02054cas a2200553 i 9918734281906676DNLM20260227090918.0m     o  d        cr#|||||||||||230214c20239999nyuar poo     0   a0eng    a  2024228343  a1394004854a1395033796  a2949-7744l2949-7744  a(OCoLC)1371162349  aSFBbengerdad20260227cSFBdAUDdUSUdOCLCOdPFMdOCLCFdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW110aGenet Med Open2dnlm 0aGenetics in medicine open00aGenetics in medicine open.1 aGIM open 1a[New York] :bElsevier Inc.,c[2023]-  a1 online resource  aAnnual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1 (2023).  aRefereed/Peer-reviewed  aOpen Access.0 aPubMedbv1n1, 2023-0 aPMC  aArticles are published online as received and cumulated into annual volumes.  a"Positioned as an official journal of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics."  a"Companion journal of Genetics in medicine."0 aVolume 1 (2023); title from journal homepage (Elsevier website, viewed August 7, 2024).1 aVolume 2 (2024) (viewed August 7, 2024).12aGenetics, Medical22aGenomics 2aPeriodical2 aAmerican College of Medical Genetics and Genomics,esponsoring body.0 tScienceDirect Open Access TitlesdElsevier Science08iCom