  aAUTH02328cgm a2200469 i 101698556DNLM20260227155541.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u161224s2016    mdu059|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:20036  a(OCoLC)972805452  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aML 418.M11502aA morning with Yo-Yo Ma /cMr. Yo-Yo Ma, World-renowned cellist. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (59 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Wednesday afternoon lecture series1 aJ. Edward Rall cultural lecture  aAccess restricted to NIH only.5DNLM  aRecorded December 5, 2016.3 a(CIT): Annual J. Edward Rall Cultural Lecture   NIH has the honor of hosting world-renowned cellist Mr. Yo-Yo Ma for the Annual J. Edward Rall Cultural Lecture.   The presentation will be in interview format between Mr. Ma and NIH Director Dr. Francis Collins speaking about the commonalities between music and science. During the event, Mr. Ma will answer questions from the NIH staff.  The annual cultural lecture (part of the Wednesday Afternoon Lecture Series) honors the memory of J. Edward Rall, founder of the Clinical Endocrinology Branch (now within NIDDK), and the first Deputy Director for Intramural Research. He recommended in 1984 that NIH add a cultural lecture to its Director's Lecture series.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed February 14, 2017).12aMa, Yo-Yo,d1955-12aMusic22aScience 2aInterview 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aMa, Yo-Yo,d1955-eperformer,einterviewee.1 aCollins, Francis S.,einterviewer. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pNIH director's cultural lecture40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?20036  aAUTH00782cam a22002537a 450000100080000000300050000800500170001300800410003002000180007102000150008904000210010404