itter release /cRobert Edwards.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 22, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 7 min., 29 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Feb. 24, 2003.3 a(CIT): NIH Neuroscience Seminar Series  Dr. Edwards' research focuses on the identification, mechanism, regulation and physiological role of neurotransmitter transporters. To this end, he has identified and characterized the vesicular monoamine, acetylcholine and GABA transporters, and most recently a glutamine and a glutamate transporter.  He is studying their effects on synaptic physiology, as well as their biophysics, membrane trafficking, and regulation.  According to his colleagues, Edwards has greatly advanced the field of synaptic transmission, causing textbooks to be rewritten.  His work and interests are well described on an outstanding website.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeurotransmitter Agents22aMembrane Transport Proteins22aSynapses22aSynaptic Transmission 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10866  aAUTH01441cas a22004334a 9425651DNLM20260227091012.0cr|un#||||||||981016c19919999fr gr p       0    0fre    a1156-5233l1156-5233  a(DNLM)SR0071074(s)  a(OCoLC)32563816  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 afreaeng  9France00aW1bJO325310aJ Mycol Med2dnlm00aJournal de mycologie médicale.07iIssues for <juin 2000-7 has English parallel title :aJournal of medical mycology  aParis :bMasson,c1991-  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aBegan with v. 1, no 1 in 1991.  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv22n1, Ma