    cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u190815s2019    mdu348|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:28670  a(OCoLC)1114531891  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWN 212 aState of Data Science in Radiation Oncology Workshopd(2019 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aState of Data Science in Radiation Oncology Workshop /cNCI, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2019]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 48 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded July 25, 2019.3 a(CIT): This workshop highlights major domains of data science knowledge and research within the field of radiation oncology.  The explosion of data as well as data-focused initiatives in oncology has generated tremendous interest among clinicians and data scientists alike about how pragmatic data programs can advance cancer care. The course is geared towards clinicians and data scientists alike who have a strong interest in data science applications within radiation oncology, with a special emphasis on clinical provider engagement.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed August 28, 2019).12aRadiation Oncology22aBig Data22aData Sciencexmethods 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?28670  aAUTH01712cgm a2200469 i 101671865DNLM20260227155037.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u151031s2015    mdu100|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19169  a(OCoLC)932048727  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWP 3221 aAnnunziata, C.q(Christina)eauthor,espeaker.10aTRACO.pOvarian cancer.pImmune checkpoint /cC. Annunziata, S. Goff.1 aOvarian cancer1 aImmune checkpoint1 aTranslational research in clinical oncology 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Ins