 a1946 ed. issued under title: Florida state sanitary code.  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 10511 no. 45DNLM  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d2000.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20250627lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM1 adigitizedc20262pda5DNLM12aSanitationxlegislation & jurisprudence22aPublic Healthxlegislation & jurisprudence 2aFlorida 2aLegislation4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/29210880R  aAUTH02167cgm a22004694a 101268578DNLM20260227150834.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2004    mdu097 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:12242  a(OCoLC)123052312  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 340.61 aLyon, G. Reid,d1949-10aEvidence-based education :bpreventing reading failure in America /cG. Reid Lyon.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2004]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 26, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 37 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 19, 2004.3 a(CIT): NIH Clinical Center's 2004 Medicine for the Public lecture series. Reading proficiency is critical to academic learning and success in school. Studies show that children who learn to read in the early grades are more likely to become better students. In the United States, about 40 percent of children are left behind in reading. Scientists are researching how children learn to read and why some children have difficulty reading. Learn about the progress to date of a comprehensive study that examines children's reading abilities during the early years, including the efforts to understand how to prevent reading failure.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aDyslexiaxprevention & control22aChild22aEducation, Specialxmethods22aLearning22aReading 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12242  aAUTH01474cas a2200493   0375363DNLM20260227090921.0cr|cn ||||||||731113c19399999enkmr p       0    0eng    a   64005925   a0022-0795l0022-0795  aJOENAK  a(DNLM)J19940000(s)  a(OCoLC)01754564  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9England00aW1bJO64210aJ Endocrinol2dnlm04aThe Journal of endocrinology.13aJOE  aBristol, UK :bSociety for Endocrinology3 3Jan. 2011- :aBristol, UK :bBioScientifica  av.billus., ports.  aMonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-        June 1939-1 aMEDLINEbv33n1,Aug. 1965-1 aPubMedbv33n1,Aug. 1965-0 aOLDMEDLINE1 aIndex medicus  aSome v. have suppls.  aAlso available online.  aOfficial journal of the Society for Endocrinology, Apr. 1949-  aVol. 1-20, 1939-60.  1 v.  3Vol. 127, no. 1 (1990)c19920824fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aEndocrinology 2aPeriodical2 aSociety for Endocrinology.0 x1479-68054 uhttps://joe.bioscientifica.com  aAUTH01662cai a2200373 a 101535765DNLM20260205104629.0m        d f      cr|cn#||||||||100714c20109999gau|| wss    f|    2eng    a  2010243634  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 48500aDeepwater Horizon response :bNIOSH report of BP illness and injury data.1 aNIOSH report of BP illness and injury data  aAtlanta, GA :bCenters for Disease Control, National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 2010.  aDescription based on July 27, 2010 update; title from caption (viewed Aug. 9, 2010).3 aThi