 Expression Profiling.22aMass Spectrometry22aProteomics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12987  aAUTH01739cgm a2200445 a 101589409DNLM20260227154345.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120725s2012    mdu090|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17364  a(OCoLC)805647117  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aW 20.500aNIH director's awards ceremony 2012.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 30 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aAccess restricted to NIH only.5DNLM0 aFrancis Collins.  aRecorded July 18, 2012.3 a(CIT): The NIH Director"s Awards are presented annually to recognize superior performance or special efforts significantly beyond regular duty requirements and directly related to fulfilling the NIH mission.  The Ruth L. Kirschstein Mentoring Awards are presented annually to recognize exemplary performance while providing mentoring functions and support to others.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aBiomedical Research22aAwards and Prizes22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aWebcast1 aCollins, Francis S.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17364  aAUTH02289cgm a2200397 a 101589408DNLM20260227155019.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120725s2012    mdu077|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17350  a(OCoLC)805647116  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWS 1041 aCollins, Francis S.10aMolecular insights on aging from Hutchinson-Gilford progeria syndrome /cFrancis Collins ; Geroscience Interest Group (GSIG).  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 17 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded July 12, 2012.3 a(CIT): The Geroscience Interest Group (GSIG) cordially invites you to the seminar listed above. Dr. Collins is the Director of the NIH, a post he has held since 2009. Previously he was the Director of the National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI) of the NIH for 15 years. In that capacity his leadership was crucial to the landmark feat of sequencing the entire human genome in 2001. Before joining the NIH, as a Howard Hughes Investigator at the University of Michigan he made many seminal discoveries in the area of disease-associated genes, including discovery of the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator gene (CFTR), the first gene ever identified to be directly responsible for a disease phenotype, cystic fibrosis. In 2003 his team identified Lamin A as the gene whose mutation is responsible for the extreme accelerated aging phenotype observed in Hutchinson-Gilford progeria patients. His seminar will focus on recent developments in the field of Hutchinson-Gilford progeria.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aProgeriaxgenetics22aAging 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bGeroscience Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17350  aAUTH01424cas a2200433 a 101277157DNLM20260227090913.0cr||||||||||||060519c20069999enkqr p       0    0eng    a  2006243384  a1818-6300l1818-6300  a(OCoLC)69677574  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9England00aW1bEU612G10aEur Arch Paediatr Dent2dnlm00aEuropean archives of paediatric dentistry :bofficial journal of the European Academy of Paediatric Dentistry.  aLeeds, England :bEuropean Academy of Paediatric Dentistry,c[2006]-3132013- :aLondon :bSpringer  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0