Journal of prosthodontic research.  aAmsterdam :bElsevier3132020- :aTokyo :bJapan Prosthodontic Society  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 53, no. 1 (Jan. 2009).  aDescription based on: Vol. 53, no. 1 (Jan. 2009); title from title page.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 53, no. 1 (Jan. 2009).1 aMEDLINEbv53n1, Jan. 2009-0 aPubMedbv53n1, Jan. 2009-  aAlso issued online.12aProsthodontics 2aPeriodical2 aNihon Hotetsu Shika Gakkai.0 x2212-463200tNihon Hotetsu Shika Gakkai zasshix0389-5386w(OCoLC)325658134 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/188319584 uhttps://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/browse/jpr  aAUTH02571cgm a22004574a 101303657DNLM20260227151908.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070403s2007    mdu128|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13712  a(OCoLC)130547312  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 10000aSystems methodologies for solving real-world problems :bapplications in public health /c[introduced by] Patty Mabry, Bobby Milstein ; [speakers] John Sterman, Ken McLeroy.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aSymposia series on systems science and health  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 25, 2007).  aStreaming video (2 hr., 8 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 22, 2007.3 a(CIT): The first in a series of four educational seminars featuring leaders in various areas of systems science.  The purposes are to raise awareness of particularly promising methodologies; and improve our collective understanding about how and when they may be used effectively by behavioral and social scientists (including researchers, policy analysts, planners/evaluators, grant reviewers, journal editors and government officials).  This first symposium provides an introduction to and overview of the rest of the series.  The core principles of system-oriented inquiry will be described, while briefly surveying a variety of methodological traditions and emerging directions in the field. John Sterman (Director, System Dynamics Group at MIT) will share his view of the field followed by Ken McLeroy (Associate Dean at Texas A&M and Department Editor for AJPH), who will explore further implications and assess the prospects for incorporating systems methodologies more fully into routine public health work.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aPublic Health22aBiomedical Research22aModels, Theoretical22aSystems Analysis 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aSterman, John.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aSymposia series on systems science and health40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13712  aAUTH01739cgm a2200457 i 101684412DNLM20260227155441.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u160601s2016    mdu058|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19709  a(OCoLC)953601621  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQZ 34500aKaposi sarcoma :bthe prototypic AIDS malignancy /cRobert Yarchoan.  KSHV-associated B-cell tumors : multicentric Castleman disease and primary effusion lymphoma / Thomas S. Uldrick.1 iTitle of second lecture on PowerPoint screen:aKaposi sarcoma herpesvirus (KSHV)-associated B-cell tumors 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (58 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aRecorded May 25, 2016.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 1, 2016).12aSarcoma, Kaposi22aHerpesvirus 8, Human 2aLecture 2aWebcast12aYarchoan, Robert,espeaker.12aUldrick, Thomas S.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S