 that informs the fields of global social work, social development, and social welfare policy and practice. It serves as an outlet for manuscripts and brief reports of interdisciplinary applied research which advance knowledge about global threats to the well-being of individuals, groups, families and communities. This research spans the full range of problems including global poverty, food and housing insecurity, economic development, environmental safety, social determinants of health, maternal and child health, mental health, addiction, disease and illness, gender and income inequality, human rights and social justice, access to health care and social resources, strengthening care and service delivery, trauma, crises, and responses to natural disasters, war, violence, population movements and trafficking, war and refugees, immigration/migration, human trafficking, orphans and vulnerable children." --Publisher description, viewed SpringerLink, 21 July 2015.  aDescription based on: Volume 1, issue 1 (March 2014); title from journal cover image on homepage (publisher's Web site, viewed May 8, 2014).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 5, issue 4 (December 2018) (SpringerLink, viewed November 26, 2018).12aSocial Work22aSocial Welfare 2aPeriodical2 aGeorge Warren Brown School of Social Work,eissuing body.40uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/40609  aAUTH01674cam a2200385 a 30420440RDNLM20260212091953.0hd|bfa012baap810815m19101911dcu          f000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14779252  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aWA 525bU57h 191000aW6bP3 v.7481 box 914 no.171 aUnited States.bCongress.bHouse.bCommittee on Interstate and Foreign Commerce.10aHearings before the Committee on Interstate and Foreign Commerce of the House of Representatives on bills relating to health activities of the general government.3 aHearing on bills relating to the health activities of the general government3 aHealth activities of the general government  aWashi