22, 2004.3 a(CIT): Road to Discovery, Summer Research Program 2004.  For more information, visit the Office of Intramural Training and Education.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aWaardenburg Syndromexgenetics22aMelanocytes22aMice, Neurologic Mutantsxgenetics22aModels, Animal22aNeural Crest22aTranscription Factors 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12080  aAUTH01735cgmaa22004694a 101247913DNLM20260227144636.0vf|cbahouvf|cjahoucr|cna||||||||050513s2005    mdu060       f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:3452  a(OCoLC)60414614  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aWD 30500aTranscriptional control of immunological tolerance /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2005]  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aThe NIH Wednesday afternoon lecture  aSpeaker, Diane Mathis.  aPresented April 27, 2005.  aAlso available online.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aPolyendocrinopathies, Autoimmunexgenetics22aImmune Tolerance22aTranscription Factors22aStromal Cells22aAutoimmunity22aAutoantibodies1 aMathis, Diane.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=3452  aAUTH02355cgm a2200457 i 9918434186806676DNLM20260227162447.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220706s2022    mdu578|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32437  a(DNLM)CIT:32443  a(OCoLC)1379265216  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 704.62 aNIH Pain Consortium.bAnnual Symposiumn(17th :d2022 :cOnline)eauthor10aNIH Pain Consortium Symposium on Advances in Pain Research :bJune 2022 /cNIH Pain Consortium.1 iTitle on PowerPoint screen:aSeventeenth Annual NIH Pain Consortium Symposium :bpain management through the lens of whole person health 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 19 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 1 & 2, 2022.3 a(CIT): On June 1st - 2nd, the NIH Pain Consortium will convene the 17th Annual NIH Pain Consortium Symposium on Advances in Pain Research via a virtual platform. The symposium: "Pain Management through the lens of Whole Person Health", will address the importance of whole person health on pain management. Topics will include the consideration of pain conditions and models through the lens of whole person health, integrating data science and multi-modal approaches into analyses and treatments, and methods for engaging patients and other stakeholders in the whole person approach to pain management.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed May 1, 2023).12aPain Managementxmethods22aPrecision Medicine22aPatient-Specific Modeling 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNIH Pain Consortium,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4526040uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45262  aAUTH02950cgm a2200457 i 9918434187206676DNLM20260227162437.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220706s2022    mdu893|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32429  a(DNLM)CIT:32431  a(DNLM)CIT:32439  a(OCoLC)1381435916  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQU 145.52 aMary Frances Picciano Dietary Supplement Research Practicumd(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.14aThe Mary Frances Picciano dietary supplement research practicum /cOffice of Dietary Supplements, NIH.1 aDietary supplement research practcum 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (14 hr., 53 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded May 23, 24 & 25, 2022.3 a(CIT): The Office of Dietary Supplements (ODS) at the National Institutes of Health (NIH) is offering a three day educational opportunity to provide fundamental knowledge of dietary supplements to faculty, students, and practitioners with a serious interest in this subject. This intensive practicum will provide a thorough overview and grounding about issues, concepts, unknowns, and controversies about dietary supplements and supplement ingredients. It will also emphasize the importance of scientific investigations to evaluate the efficacy, safety, and value of these products for health promotion and disease prevention as well as how to carry out this type of research. Topics to be addressed include: Supplement use in the United States and reasons for use; The regulatory framework governing supplements; Differences in bringing foods, drugs, and supplements to market; Supplement quality; Assessing the health effects of foods and supplements; and Developing policies and advice about supplement use based on science. Participants will also hear from various stakeholders--the dietary supplement industry, consumer advocacy groups, and media--who study, advocate, regulate, or educate about dietary supplements.For more information go to https://odspracticum.od.nih.gov.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed May 25, 2023).12aDietary Supplements 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNIH Office of Dietary Supplements,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4499240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4499440uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44996  aAUTH02715cgm a2200517 i 9918820070406676DNLM20260227164439.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u240501s2024    mdu451|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33771  a(DNLM)CIT:33778  a(DNLM)CIT:33781  a(DNLM)CIT:33784  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 704.62 aAnnual NIH HEAL Initiative Investigator Meetingn(5th :d2024:cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10a5th Annual NIH HEAL Initiative Scientific Meeting (parts 1-4) /cThe Helping to End Addiction Long-term(r) Initiative, or NIH HEAL Initiative(r). 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (4 streaming video files (7 hr., 31 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 7 & 8, 2024.3 a(CIT): The 5th Annual NIH HEAL Initiative Scientific Meeting will be Wednesday and Thursday, February 7-8, 2024. The Helping to End Addiction Long-term(r) Initiative, or NIH HEAL Initiative(r), will bring together HEAL-funded researchers, people with living and lived experience and other community partners, National Institutes of Health (NIH) leadership and scientific staff, and other stakeholders to share research findings, explore trends and shared interests and challenges, and identify opportunities to advance the goals of the initiative. View the meeting plenary sessions via livestream, no meeting registration required. Find more details, including the agenda, on the event website.<p>For more information go to https://heal.nih.gov/news/events/5th-heal-scientific-meeting</p>.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed March 5, 2025).12aPain Management22aOpioid-Related Disorders22aCommunity-Based Participatory Research22aEvidence-Based Practice22aClinical Trials as Topic 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNIH HEAL Initiative,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institute on Drug Abuse,eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5414440uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5414640uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5414840uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=54150  aAUTH02515cgm a2200493 i 9918299483506676DNLM20260227161714.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u211110s2021    mdu058|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32012  a(OCoLC)1333917548  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aHT 150500aOutcomes from NASEM's June 2021 anti-Racism in STEMM summit /cChief Officer for Scientific Workforce Diversity, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (58 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH scientific workforce diversity seminar  aRecorded October 25, 2021.3 a(CIT): Please join our second event in the NIH Scientific Workforce Diversity Seminar Series, which addresses the state of the science on anti-racism in science, technology, engineering, mathematics, and medicine (STEMM) based on findings from a national, public summit sponsored by the National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine"s (NASEM) Committee on Addressing Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Anti-Racism in 21st Century STEMM Organizations. NASEM staff will debrief the NIH community on the summit discussions and findings to give NIH leaders, policy makers, and other interested staff the opportunity to map a way forward on this important topic.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed June 14, 2022).22aAddressing Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Anti-Racism in 21st Century STEMM Organizations (Summit)d(2021 :cOnline)12aSystemic Racismxprevention & control12aCongresses as Topic22aOrganizational Culture22aCultural Diversity22aSocial Inclusion 2aUnited States 2aWebcast 2aLecture1 aBernard, Marie A.,emoderator,ehost.1 aBarabino, Gilda A.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aScientific workforce diversity seminar series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=43967  aAUTH01164cas a2200397 a 101249598DNLM20260227090916.0cr|cn#||||||||050606c20059999ii || p       |    0eng    a  2007243287  a0973-1482l1998-4138  a(OCoLC)171286940  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9India00aW1bJO574ED10aJ Cancer Res Ther2dnlm00aJournal of cancer research and therapeutics.13aJCRT  aMumbai, India :bMedknow Publications  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with v. 1 in 2005.  aDescription based on: Vol. 2, issue 1 (Jan./Mar. 2006); title from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan./Mar. 2005-1 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan./Mar. 2005-  aAlso issued online.12aNeoplasms 2aPeriodical2 aAssociation of Radiation Oncologists of India.0 x1998-41384 uhttp://www.cancerjournal.net/  aAUTH01497cas a2200469 a 8303541DNLM20260211111822.0cr||||||||||||830519c19829999pr qr         0||| 0eng    a0738-0658l0738-0658  aPRHJDB  a(DNLM)P60565000(s)  a(OCoLC)09424146  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aengaspa  9Puerto Rico00aW1bPU787JR10aP R Health Sci J2dnlm 0aPuerto Rico health sciences journal00aPuerto Rico health sciences journal.1 aPRHSJ  a[Puerto Rico] :bUniversity of Puerto Rico Medical Sciences Campus,cc1982-  av. :bill., ports.  aQuarterly,b1993-  aQuarterlyb1982-84  aThree no. a yearb1985-1992  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2r