inical Center. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (6 hr., 12 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 29, 2024.3 a(CIT): <p><p>Rare diseases affect an estimated 30 million people in the United States. On February 29, 2024, NIH will host its annual Rare Disease Day event to raise awareness about these disorders, the people they affect, and NIH collaborations that advance research for new treatments. Sponsored by the National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (NCATS) and the NIH Clinical Center, the event will feature panel discussions, rare diseases stories, and more. Participants can share their thoughts, photos, and experiences via social media using the hashtag #RDDNIH.</p><p></p><p>Interact with other attendees and view a listing of the in-person exhibits and scientific posters in this year"s event app: https://app.socio.events/Mjc2NjY%3D.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For more information go to https://ncats.nih.gov/news-events/events/rdd</p></p>.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed September 20, 2024).12aRare Diseases 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (U.S.),esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bClinical Center,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=52569  aAUTH01841cgm a2200433 i 101690015DNLM20260227155640.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u160804s2016    mdu055|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19810  a(OCoLC)956966295  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWC 53400aEthics and Ebola :brecommendations of the Presidential Commission for the Study of Bioethical Issues /cKata Chi