book  z9781003856542qPDF ebook8 aCIPO000049628  a(OCoLC)1398211376z(OCoLC)1398212552  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdYDXdOKXdUKMGBdIG#  apcc  9United States00aRM218.7b.P39 202400aQU 14500a613.2023223/eng/202402281 aPatterson, J. Barretto,eauthor.10aThink like a dietitian :ba nutrition counseling starter kit /cJ. Barretto Patterson.  aFirst edition. 1aBoca Raton :bCRC Press,c2024.  axx, 216 pages :billustrations (colour) ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aPart I. Share. SHARE -- A step-by-step approach to nutrition counseling ; Start with a blank sheet ; Hear and understand ; Assess and review ; Empower the patient -- Part II. Everyday eating routines : a different EER. Motivations and barriers ; A different EER ; Commonly reported eating patterns -- Part III. Common referrals and FAQs. Common referrals ; Type 2 diabetes and prediabetes ; Heart disease prevention and management ; Chronic kidney disease ; IBS and the low FODMAP diet ; Weight counseling -- Part IV. Putting it all together. Health literacy ; Cultural competence ; SHARE your screen -- and other virtual care tips ; Making PLANS and taking action.  a"While courses in nutrition counseling teach providers to listen to their patients, this book gives registered dietitian nutritionists (RDNs) a heads up on what to listen for, with educational materials that address the everyday challenges many people, hence many RDNs, face. Split into four distinct sections, this book equips readers to with comprehensive education and counselling for the most common nutrition referrals. Topics covered include: How to structure a nutrition counseling session, from getting a patient to open up right through to addressing personal challenges such as cultivating empathy and dealing with implicit bias. Routine eating patterns and challenges reported in nutrition counselling, such as night eating, emotional eating, and more. Common reasons for referral to a dietitian and frequently asked questions Special issues in health education This book is appealing to both early nutrition professionals and experienced dietitians alike, providing a holistic toolkit for RDNs of all levels of experience"--cProvided by publisher.12aDiet, Healthy22aCounseling22aHealth Promotion22aNutritionistsxeducation  aAUTH01219nam a2200337 i 101778671DNLM20260220080943.0210430s1862    mau          l000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5573 no.151 aBoston (Mass.).bCity Council,eauthor.10aFree City Hospital request for additional appropriation. 1a[Boston] :b[publisher not identified],c1862.  a13 pages ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aCity document ;vno. 54  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM22aBoston City Hospital.12aHospitals, Municipalceconomics22aFinancing, Government 2aBoston2 aBoston (Mass.).bCommittee on a Free City Hospital.1 aBoston (Mass.).tDocument ;v1862, 54.  aAUTH02138cgm a2200481 i 9918592679706676DNLM20260227163510.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230429s2023    mdu382|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33064  a(OCoLC)1450521933  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQZ 2752 aChildhood Cancer Data Initiative.bSymposiumd(2023 :cBethesda, Md.)eauthor.10aChildhood Cancer Data Initiative (CCDI) Symposium /cNCI, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (6 hr., 22 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 24, 2023.3 a(CIT): The purpose of the Childhood Cancer Data Initiative (CCDI) Symposium is for the childhood cancer community to gather to receive and exchange information about the progress the Institute has made on this initiative, and better understand what the future holds.  Speakers and panelists will share their expertise on subjects related to the symposium"s three main topics: Cohorts for Clinical and Translational Research, Clinical Data and Annotation, and Accelerating Clinical Trials in Childhood Cancer.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 19, 2024).12aNeoplasms12aChild22aAdolescent22aData Aggregation22aData Sciencexmethods22aDatasets as Topic22aResearch Design 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aChildhood Cancer Data Initiative,esponsoring body.2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49171  aAUTH01853cgm a22003974a 101267740DNLM20260227145451.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2001    mdu070 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10618  a(OCoLC)64588912  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 4751 aWood, R. D.q(Richard D.)10aTolerating damaged DNA /cRichard Wood ; sponsored by NIH DNA Repair Interest Group.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2001]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Feb. 26, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 10 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 18, 2001.3 a(CIT): The DNA Repair Interest Group is concerned with all forms of DNA damage and repair. As a major defense against environmental damage to cells DNA repair is present in all organisms examined including bacteria, yeast, drosophila, fish, amphibians, rodents and humans. The members of the DNA Repair Interest Group perform research in areas including DNA repair enzymology and fine structure, mutagenesis, gene and cell cycle regulation, protein structure, and human disease.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aDNA Repair22aDNA Damage 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bDNA Repair Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10618  aAUTH01343nam a2200373 i 101778829DNLM20260205142706.0210504s1871    mau           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5574 no.21 aCowdin, Robert,d1805-1874,eauthor.10aRemarks of Alderman Robert Cowdin on the subject of admitting female students to clinical lectures at the City Hospital. 1a[Boston] :b[publisher not identified],c[1871]  a11 pages ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aCity document ;vno. 37  aCover title.  a"In Board of Aldeman, May 8, 1871."  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM22aBoston City Hospital.12aStudents, Medical12aWomen22aSexismxprevention & control22aEducation, Medical 2aBoston1 aBoston (Mass.).tDocument ;v1871, 37.  aAUTH01132pam a2200361 i 9918987878106676DNLM20260212090706.0t|231124s2023    njua     b    001 0 eng    aGBC4308052bnb  a9781394174737qhardback  a139417473Xqhardback8 aCIPO000005516  a(OCoLC)1458039225  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCO  apcc  9United States00aQU 56004a616.04222300aIntegration of biomaterials for gene therapy /cedited by Rishabha Malviya, Sonali Sundram, Neelam Jain. 1aHoboken, NJ :bWiley-Scrivener,c2023.  axxi, 438 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm  atext2rdacontent