M)CIT:2872  a(OCoLC)56011546  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aWM 270bVC no.232 200400aBehavioral and neuronal mechanisms of relapse to addictive drugs :bevidence from preclinical studies /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2004]  a1 videocassette of 1 (DVCPRO) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/4 in.3master.  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (61 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videodisc of 1 (DVD) (61 min.) :bsd., col. ;c4 3/4 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's seminar series lecture  aTitle from cassette label.  aSpeaker, Yavin Shaham.  aPresented Apr. 23, 2004.  aAlso available online.  aVideocassette (Betacam SP)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2011.e1 videocassette (61 min.) : sd., col. ; 1/2 in.  aVideodisc (DVD)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2011.e1 videodisc (61 min.) : sd., col. ; 4 3/4 in.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aSubstance-Related Disorders.22aRecurrence22aStress, Psychological22aCocaine-Related Disorders1 aShaham, Yavin.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's seminar series4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=2872  aAUTH02901cgm a2200421 a 101578523DNLM20260227154457.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120215s2012    mdu345|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17084  a(OCoLC)785706129  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWM 2000aOpportunities in data visualization and visual analytics for behavioral and social science research /cOffice of Behavioral and Social Science Research.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 45 min.) :bsd., col.).  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Jan. 30, 2012.3 a(CIT): The NIH Office of Behavioral and Social Science Research, in partnership with the National Cancer Institute and the National Institute on Drug Abuse, present a meeting on Opportunities in Data Visualization and Visual Analytics for Behavioral and Social Science Research. The meeting will explore the use of data visualization and visual analytics software in the context of health-related behavioral and social science research. Although this conference will highlight the use of visualization and visual analytics to facilitate both communication and data analysis, the emphasis will be on the power these tools hold to elucidate complex data from behavioral and social science research in new ways to advance public health.  Specifically, this workshop seeks to:  (a) Highlight existing developments in the field of data visualization and visual analytics  (b) Provide an overview of current challenges and opportunities in statistical methodologies such as geographic analyses and longitudinal social networks that might be advanced through better visualization tools  (c) Identify relevant areas of behavioral and social science research supported by NIH that are highly complex and could make the best use of data visualization and visual analytics.For more information go to <a href='http://conferences.thehillgroup.com/obssr/DataVisualization/index.html'>http://conferences.thehillgroup.com/obssr/DataVisualization/index.html.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aBehavioral Researchxmethods22aAudiovisual Aids22aElectronic Data Processing22aInformation Dissemination22aSocial Sciencesxmethods 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Behavioral and Social Sciences Research.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.as