damedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Feb. 27, 2008).  aStreaming video (11 hr., 50 min., 6 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 14-15, 2001.3 a(CIT): The RAC is a technical committee whose goal is to consider the current state of knowledge and technology regarding recombinant DNA.  This includes review of human gene transfer trials, and an assessment of the ability of DNA recombinants to survive in nature and the potential for transfer of genetic material to other organisms.  It also considers hypothetical hazards and methods for monitoring and minimizing risks. Approximately one-third of the 15 members do not have scientific expertise but represent public interests and attitudes. This balance is intended to provide a forum for open public debate of social and scientific issues attendant to recombinant DNA research.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aDNA, Recombinant22aClinical Protocolsxstandards22aGene Transfer Techniques22aGenetic Therapy 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1148540uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?11486  aAUTH01356cas a2200433 i 101634540DNLM20260227090909.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||140130c20139999ne || poo    |0    0eng    a  2014243609  a2214-2509l2214-2509  a(OCoLC)869799858  aCNCGMbengerdad20260227cCNCGMdOH1dDNLM  apcc  9Netherlands10aW1  aRC10910aIDCases2dnlm00aIDCases.1 aID cases 1aAmsterdam :bElsevier Ltd.,c[2014]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with 1 (2014).0 aPubMedbv2n1, 2015-0 aPMC  aSome articles in Volume 1 published electronically in 2011.  aDescription based on: 1 (2014); title from cover image (publisher's Web site, viewed Oct. 8, 2014).  aLatest 