?10605  aAUTH01332cgm a22004214a 101294870DNLM20260227151621.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu061 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13352  a(OCoLC)84717670  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2691 aLarson, Steven M.,d1941-10aMolecular imaging and targeted radiotherapy in oncology /cSteven M. Larson.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCCR grand rounds  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan 16, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 19 sec. : sd., col.).  aAccess restricted to NIH only.  aRecorded Sept. 12, 2006.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxradiotherapy 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aCCR grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13352  aAUTH02828cgm a2200445 i 101774301DNLM20260227160526.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u201211s2020    mdu329 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31420  a(DNLM)CIT:31428  a(OCoLC)1248768069  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWM 202 aNIH Behavioral and Social Sciences Research Festivald(2020 :cOnline)jauthor.10aNIH Behavioral and Social Sciences Research Festival 2020 /cOBSSR, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2020]  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (5 hr., 29 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded December 1&2, 2020.3 a(CIT): The Office of Behavioral and Social Sciences Research (OBSSR), in collaboration with the NIH Behavioral and Social Sciences Research Coordinating Committee (BSSR-CC), holds the annual NIH Behavioral and Social Sciences Research Festival on the NIH campus. This new annual meeting is organized to inform the wider BSSR community, stakeholders, and NIH Institutes and Centers (ICs) about the latest BSSR funded by the NIH and its overall impact and importance across the entire field of biomedical research. Additional goals are to assist the ICs with the establishment of research priorities and the coordination of their programmatic efforts, thus minimizing redundancy and maximizing returns on NIH investments in BSSR. The festival highlights exciting research results, emerging areas, and innovations in health-related BSSR. This trans-NIH event enables efficient leveraging of NIH resources and expertise. The BSSR-CC members contribute diverse and comprehensive perspectives on the NIH BSSR portfolio, thus facilitating the selection of an outstanding array of research results that are highlighted at the festival.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 22, 2021).12aBehavioral Research22aSocial Sciences22aResearch 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Behavioral and Social Sciences Research,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bBehavioral and Social Sciences Research Coordinating Committee,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4005740uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=40058  aAUTH01154nam a2200325 i 101778798DNLM20260204153638.0210503s1901    nyua          000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5573 no.272 aAlbany Hospital,eauthor.10aAnnouncement provisional program :bclinical days, 1901 : Albany Hospital July-August..1 aClinical days, 1901 1aAlbany, N.Y. :bPress of Brandow Printing Co.,c[1901]  a5 unnumbered pages :billustration ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCover title.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM22aAlbany Hospital.12aEducation, Medical, Continuing 2aNew York 2aProgram  aAUTH02232cgm a22004334a 101267598DNLM20260227145354.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2003    mdu056 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10426  a(OCoLC)65195209  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 26700aTour of hope at NIH with Lance Armstrong /cLance Armstrong.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 9, 2006).  aStreaming video (55 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 17, 2003.3 a(CIT): Play Video   Lance Armstrong, cancer survivor, member of the President's Cancer Panel, founder of the Lance Armstrong Foundation, and five-time winner of the Tour de France, is anchoring a bicycle tour across America to raise awareness of cancer research and the vital importance of clinical trials.   Lance and a contingent of cyclists will speak to NIH to emphasize the value of clinical trials. NCI is pleased to participate in the NIH salute to the Tour of Hope, which will be a fitting tribute to cancer researchers at NIH and others whose clinical trial work, collaborative arrangements, and cancer communications ultimately work together to provide hope to cancer patients and survivors, their family and friends, and individuals who may be helped through cancer prevention and early detection.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxdrug therapy22aBicycling22aClinical Trials as Topic22aHealth Education 2aWebcast1 aArmstrong, Lance.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10426  aAUTH01568cgm a22004454a 101267564DNLM20260227145244.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2002    mdu064 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10374  a(OCoLC)70217850  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWP 8701 aOlopade, Olufunmilayo I.10aDissection of cooperating genetic pathways involved in aggressive early onset breast cancer research /cOlufunmilayo I. Olopade.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2002]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aJohn Diggs lecture  aTitle from PowerPoint screen (viewed June 25, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 4 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded July 15, 2002.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aBreast Neoplasmsxgenetics22aGenes, BRCA122aErb-b2 Receptor Tyrosine Kinases 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aJohn Diggs lecture40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10374  aAUTH01641cgm a2200445 i 9918384669406676DNLM20260227162135.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220426s2022    mdu081|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32274  a(OCoLC)1331665695  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWM 2742 aReducing Stigma around Alcohol Use Disorder in Minority Communities (Webinar)d(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aReducing stigma around alcohol use disorder in minority communities /cNIAAA, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 21 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 21, 2022.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed June 15, 2022).12aAlcohol-Related Disordersxethnology22aAlcohol Drinkingxethnology22aSocial Stigma22aHispanic or Latino22aBlack or African American22aMinority Health 2aUnited Statesxethnology 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44317  aAUTH01205nam a2200349 i 9918977657806676DNLM20260223082420.0250130s2022    ck a     b    000 0 spa    a9786287554214  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9Colombia00aWS 462.5.S551 aVelasco Salamanca, Marcela,eauthor.10aDiseño de un modelo de prevención del inicio de consumo de tabaco y exposición al humo /cMarcela Velasco Salamanca, Carlos Antonio Pardo.  aPrimera edición. 1aBogotá, D.C. :bUniversidad Católica de Colombia,c2022.  a60 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aColección logos vestigium ;v1612aTobacco Usexprevention & control12aTobacco Smoke Pollutionxprevention & control22aTobacco Use Disorderxprevention & control22aChild22aAdolescent 2aColombia1 aPardo, Carlos Antonio,eauthor. 0aColección logos vestigium ;v16.  aAUTH03424cgm a2200517 i 9918681340606676DNLM20260227164118.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230929s2023    mdu441|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33461  a(DNLM)CIT:33462  a(DNLM)CIT:33465  a(DNLM)CIT:33466  a(OCoLC)1459861417  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.52 aNIH Research Festivald(2023 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aNIH research festival /cNIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (4 streaming video files (7 hr., 21 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aLecture session I : meet the IRS! (part 1) -- Lecture session II : meet the ACI! (part 1) -- Lecture session III : meet the ACI! (part 2) -- Lecture session IV : meet the IRS! (part 2).  aRecorded September 18 & 19, 2023.3 a(CIT): That"s the newer IRS, the NIH Independent Research Scholars(external link) (IRS). IRS program scholars are independent, non-tenure track principal investigators selected for their readiness to conduct independent research and their commitment to enhancing diversity within the biomedical workforce. Divided into two lecture sessions (Lecture Session I & IV), we will feature 12 IRS PIs in all, each providing a 15-minute snapshot of their research. Join us for this first session with six IRS PIs. Chairs: Parinaz Fathi, Ph.D., NIBIB(external link) and Tokunbor Lawal, Ph.D., FNP-BC, NINR(external link) Speakers: Andrew Kesner, Ph.D., NIAAA(external link) Elucidating the role of medial septum glutamate neurons in reward seeking behaviors Carrie Mae Long, Ph.D., NIAID(external link) From Allergy to lipopolysaccharide: Modeling Coxiella burnetii-host interactions for an improved Q fever vaccine Emily E. Ricotta, Ph.D., M.Sc., NIAID(external link) Turning data into science with the Epidemiology and Data Management Unit Oyebola Oyesola, DVM, Ph.D. (NIAID)(external link) Helminth exposure protects against murine SARS-CoV-2 infection through macrophage dependent T cell activation Shaun Abrams, D.D.S, Ph.D., NIDCR(external link) Central role of centrioles: tissue-specific requirements for coordinating facial development Mary Diaz Santana, Ph.D., NIEHSFor more information go to <a href="https://researchfestival.nih.gov/2023">https://researchfestival.nih.gov/2023.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed August 27, 2024).22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aBiomedical Research22aResearch Personnel22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),ehost institutio