rence Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aEunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4246440uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=42466  aAUTH01865cgm a22004454a 101294867DNLM20260227151714.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu147|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13329  a(OCoLC)84714557  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2412 aPreapplication Meeting for Alliance of Glycobiologists for Detection of Cancer and Cancer Riskd(2006 :cNational Institutes of Health)10aPreapplication Meeting for Alliance of Glycobiologists for Detection of Cancer and Cancer Risk /cKarl Krueger ... [et al.].  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 8, 2007).  aStreaming video (2 hr., 27 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded July 14, 2006.3 a(CIT): This videocast will cover the preapplication meeting for RFA CA-07-020. This public meeting will provide details of concern for investigators intending to submit applications in response to this RFA. The meeting will also permit an opportunity for investigators to ask questions to program staff involved with this funding initiative.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxdiagnosis22aBiomarkers, Tumor22aFinancing, Government22aGlycoconjugates 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aKrueger, Karl,d1954-40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13329  aAUTH02044cgm a22004814a 101294883DNLM20260227151839.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu101 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13432  a(OCoLC)123689192  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 1801 aGladwin, Mark.10aRedox biology.pPhysiology, carcinogenesis /cGladwin and Hussain.30aPhysiology, carcinogenesis1 iTitle from title screen:aUnraveling the reactions of nitric oxide, nitrite, and hemoglobin in human physiology and therapeutics  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 23, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 40 min., 16 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 17, 2006.3 a(CIT): Redox Biology (RB). The course is designed for NIH fellows to enhance their knowledge of redox biology. Reactive species such as superoxide, hydrogen peroxide and nitric oxide are associated with cellular toxicity, however, nitric oxide is useful in the treatment of cardiovascular disease.  The course will examine the role of reactive nitrogen and oxygen species in carcinogenesis, cancer proliferation and angiogenesis.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aFree Radicalsxadverse effects12aNitric Oxidexphysiology22aHemoglobinsxphysiology22aInflammationxcomplications22aNeoplasmsxcomplications22aVasodilation 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13432  aAUTH01446cas a2200457 a 9308901DNLM20260227091012.0cr#un#||||||||930520c19829999ja fr p       0||| 0jpn    a0287-7651l0287-7651  a(DNLM)SR0059482(s)  a(OCoLC)31332569  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 ajpnaeng  9Japan00aW1bKI185G10aJpn J Psychon Sci2dnlm00aKiso shinrigaku kenkyū.15aJapanese journal of psychonomic science  aTōkyō :bNihon Kiso Shinri Gakkai,cShōwa 57 [1982]-3 aTokyo :bNihon Kiso Shinri Gakkai  av. :bill.  aSemiannual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aDai 1-kan dai 1-gō (1982-nen 10-gatsu)-  aTwo no. a year.  aTitle from cover.0 aMEDLINEbSelected citations only0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aText chie