States00aWH 2602 aINSPIRED Symposium: Insights in Pediatric CAR T-cell Immunotherapy: Recent Advances and Future Directionsd(2023 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aINSPIRED Symposium :binsights in pediatric CAR t-cell immunotherapy : recent advances and future directions /cNCI, NIH.1 aInsights in pediatric CAR t-cell immunotherapy: recent advances and future directions 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (7 hr., 30 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 1, 2023.3 a(CIT): With the primary goal to bring together the expanding pediatric and young adult CAR T-cell community, in addressing major clinical advances achieved over the last decade and outstanding gaps warranting further focus, we aim to reflect on the 10+ year experience of CAR T-cell delivery to pediatric and young adults with B-cell malignancies. Based on experience gained over this time, this conference will focus on highlighting current best practices, opportunities to address unmet needs, and areas where future research is needed or ongoing. Our primary goal for this conference is to allow for cross-fertilization and collaboration as we strive to improve outcomes using CAR T-cell therapy in pediatric cancers.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed August 13, 2024).12aLeukemia, Lymphocytic, Chronic, B-Cellxtherapy22aImmunotherapy, Adoptive22aNeoplasm Recurrence, Localxprevention & control22aReceptors, Chimeric Antigen22aChild22aAdolescent 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49224  aAUTH01135cam a2200301 i 450000100100000000300050001000500170001500700150003200800410004701000170008803500190010504000350012404400180015906000190017710000670