aWL 704.62 aHEAL Multi-Disciplinary Working Group (Meeting)d(2022 March 1 :cOnline)jauthor.10aHelping to End Addiction Long-term Initiative Multi-Disciplinary Working Group /cNIH.1 iTitle on PowerPoint slide:aNIH HEAL Initiative :bMulti-Disciplinary Working Group Spring Meeting 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 38 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aYear shown on title screen is incorrect.  aRecorded March 1, 2022.3 a(CIT): The Multi-Disciplinary Working Group serves as a fact-finding body of experts external to the National Institutes of Health (NIH) to provide input to guide Helping to End Addiction Long-term(r) Initiative, or NIH HEAL Initiative(r), research. The working group assists the NIH Institute and Center Advisory Councils to help ensure that NIH HEAL Initiative research meets the bold, trans-NIH goals for the initiative. Its meetings serve as a forum to engage partners in the private sector and research community, provide a transparent venue for stakeholders and members of the public, and help facilitate exchange of scientific information among NIH HEAL Initiative projects.For more information go to <a href="https://heal.nih.gov/events/mdwg">https://heal.nih.gov/events/mdwg.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed December 5, 2022).22aNIH HEAL Initiative.12aPain Management12aTranslational Research, Biomedical22aOpioid Epidemic22aDrug Overdose 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNIH HEAL Initiative.bMulti-Disciplinary Working Group,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44811  aAUTH02186cas a2200553 a 8302815DNLM20260227090954.0cr|cn ||||||||830421c19829999gw br p       0||