tions only  aAlso issued online.  aJournal of the International Association for the Study of Traditional Asian Medicine.12aMedicine, East Asian Traditional 2aPeriodical2 aInternational Association for the Study of Traditional Asian Medicine.0 x1573-42184 uhttp://booksandjournals.brillonline.com/content/journals/15734218  aAUTH02220cgm a22004334a 101516503DNLM20260227153137.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u091002s2009    mdu090|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15299  a(OCoLC)655609861  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aW 84.31 aIsrael, Barbara A.10aCommunity-based participatory research :bpartnership approach to address health disparities /cBarbara Israel and Angela Reyes.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH health disparities seminar series  aTitle from title screen (viewed Nov. 30, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 30 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Aug. 13, 2009.3 a(CIT):  The forum disseminates information on advances, gaps, and current issues related to health disparities research. It features national and international health disparities research experts including many who are funded by the NCMHD, the other NIH Institutes and Centers, and federal agency partners. The theme for the July seminar series is the social determinants of health.   Place matters: where we live, work, study and play is critically important for health - and more so for children. This presentation will summarize research on the negative effects of racial and socioeconomic segregation on health, and highlight some of the challenges and opportunities in applying research to policy and practice to address health inequities and improve health opportunities.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aCommunity-Based Participatory Research12aHealthcare Disparities 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH health disparities seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15299  aAUTH01281nam a2200361 i 9918900816206676DNLM20260204152116.0240920s2019    bl ac         000 0 por    a9788560162697  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  9Brazil00aQV 711 DB81 aCarneiro, Pauloc(Of SINDUSFARMA),eauthor.12aA era educacional.nII,pSinergia entre saber e prática na busca do aprimoramento constante da qualidade /cPaulo Carneiro, Lauro D. Moretto, Dan Gedankien.1 aSinergia entre saber e prática na busca do aprimoramento constante da qualidade 1aSao Paulo :bSINDUSFARMA,c[2019]  a152 pages :billustrations, portraits ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier22aSINDUSFARMA.12aDrug Industryxhistory12aDrug Industryxeducation12aQuality Improvementxhistory22aHistory, 21st Century 2aBrazil 2aPictorial Work1 aMoretto, Lauro Domingos,eauthor.1 aGedankien, Dan,eauthor.22aSINDUSFARMA,eissuing body.  aAUTH01945cgm a2200481 i 101609770DNLM20260227154706.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u130604s2013    mdu057|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17925  a(OCoLC)854907452  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWH 30000aRenal complications after hematopoietic stem cell transplantation :btransplant-associated thrombotic microangiopathy /cMeryl Waldman. Current approaches to assessing kidney function : who, how, and why? / Jeffrey B. Kopp.1 aCurrent approaches to assessing kidney function 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2013]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (57 min.) :bcolor, sound).  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdm2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded May 1, 2013.  aDescription based on version viewed June 25, 2013.12aThrombotic Microangiopathiesxcomplications22aGraft vs Host Diseasexcomplications22aHematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantationxadverse effects22aKidney Function Testsxmethods22aKidneyxphysiopathology22aPostoperative Complications 2aLecture 2aWebcast12aWaldman, Meryl.tRenal complications after hematopoietic stem cell transplantation.12aKopp, Jeffrey B.tCurrent approaches to assessing kidney function.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aClinical Center grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17925  aAUTH02691cgm a2200433 i 9918663286706676DNLM20260227164013.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230815s2023    mdu383|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33332  a(OCoLC)1455526765  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.52 aCollaborative Models for Building Equality and Equity in Research (Conference)d(2023 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aCollaborative models for building equality and equity in research /cNIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (6 hr., 23 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aAccess restricted to NIH only.  aRecorded July 19, 2023.3 a(CIT): This dynamic conference will host approximately 400 research leaders, legislators, Federal, state, and local program managers, Historically Black Colleges and Universities, Minority Serving Institutions, diversity directors, industry stakeholders, community advocates, and policymakers. It will feature keynote speakers, panel discussions, breakout groups, and interactive sessions centered around current collaborative models and innovative research initiatives for underserved populations.   The conference will focus on successes, best practices, and knowledge dissemination to strengthen and advance educational equality, excellence, and economic opportunities in research. The goal of the conference is to create opportunities that will foster and enhance the capacity of HBCUs and MSIs to participate in or be eligible to participate in Agency programs and to address barriers these institutions face when accessing programs that benefit and impact underserved communities. In addition, the conference seeks to help prepare and encourage more institutions to participate in the medical research enterprise.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 30, 2024).12aBiomedical Research22aHealth Equity22aMedically Underserved Area22aPublic-Private Sector Partnerships 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=51080  aAUTH01319cas a2200409 i 101639933DNLM20260227090918.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||140130c20139999enk|| poo     0    0eng    a  2014243637  a2213-5383l2213-5383  a(OCoLC)869799749  aCNCGMbengcCNCGMerdad20260227dOH1dOCLCOdDNLM  apcc  9England10aW1  aRC261.A110aJ Cancer Policy2dnlm00aJournal of cancer policy. 1a[London] :bElsevier Ltd,c[2013]-  a1 online resource  aFour issues a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with 1 (2013).1 aMEDLINEbv27, Mar. 2021-0 aPubMedbv27, Mar. 2021- ; Selected citations only before this date  aDescription based on: 1 (2013); title from PDF cover image (publisher's Web site, viewed Oct. 22, 2014).  aLatest issue consulted: 2 (2014) (viewed Oct. 22, 2014).12aMedical Oncology22aPublic Health 2aPeriodical40uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/22135383  aAUTH01244cas a2200385 i 101655178DNLM20260227090913.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||141124c20149999ne || poo     0    0eng    a  2015243202  a2214-1804l2214-1804  a(OCoLC)896822502  aOH1bengerdad20