apanese Society for Cardiovascular Surgery.30aJapanese journal of cardiovascular surgery  aTōkyō-to :bDō Gakkai,3 aTokyo-To :bNihon Shinzo Kekkan Geka Gakkai  av. :bill.  aSix no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 1972.  aDescription based on: Dai 17-kan, dai 1-gō (Aug. 1987); title from cover.  aAlso issued online.  aArticles in Japanese; table of contents in English and Japanese. 2aCardiovascular Surgical Procedures 2aPeriodical2 aNihon Shinzō Kekkan Geka Gakkai.0 x1883-41084 uhttps://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/browse/jjcvs/list/-char/ja  aAUTH01542cas a2200469 a 9214969DNLM20260223143949.0cr|cn#||||||||921008c19849999nju x m       0||| 0eng    asn 92005585   a1064-3745l1064-3745  a(OCoLC)24839341  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bME9616J0 aMethods in molecular biology (Clifton, N.J.)10aMethods Mol Biol2dnlm 0aMethods in molecular biologyb(Clifton, N.J.)10aMethods in molecular biology.  aClifton, N.J. :bHumana Press,3 aTotowa, NJ :bHumana Press  av. :bill.  aIrregular  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 1984.  aIrregular.  aPublished: Totowa, N.J., 1992?- .  aDescription based on surrogate of: Vol. 7, c1991.1 aMEDLINEbv14, 1993-1 aPubMedbv14, 1993-1 aIndex medicus  aVol. 417 not published.  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 36 (1994)c19950516fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paperxFurther review is required to determine exactly when acid-free paper was first used for this title 2aMolecular Biologyxmethods 2aPeriodical0 x1940-60294 uhttps://link.springer.com/bookseries/7651  aAUTH01994cgm a22004454a 101268606DNLM20260227150939.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2004    mdu052 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:12299  a(OCoLC)137294695  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 3751 aGould, Kathleen.10aProbing unexpected connections between cell cycle control and pre-mRNA splicing /cKathleen Gould.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2004]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 27, 2007).  aStreaming video (51 min., 23 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 5, 2004.3 a(CIT): The fission yeast cdc5 gene was identified in a genetic screen for mutants defective in cell cycle progression.  Since that time, our laboratory and others have found that Cdc5p and its orthologs in other organisms including human are essential components of a subcomplex of the spliceosome termed the nineteen complex (NTC).  Using Cdc5p as a target for tandem affinity purification, we have determined the composition (by mass spectrometry) and structure (by cryo-electron microscopy) of the assembled spliceosome.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aCell Cycle22aCell Cycle Proteins22aGenes, cdc22aRNA Splicing22aSpliceosomes 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12299  aAUTH01644cgm a22004694a 101268526DNLM20260227150810.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2004    mdu254|||||||f||||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:12153  a(OCoLC)130523237  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWE 3461 aClauser, Karl.10aProteomic approaches for understanding kinase mediated signalling and discovering arthritis biomarkers /cKarl Clauser.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2004]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed Apr. 28, 2007).  aStreaming video (4 hr., 14 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Sept. 9, 2004.  