e clinician lecture ;v[7th]  aTitle from cassette spine label.  aSpeaker, Gerald M. Reaven.  aOriginally presented Nov. 2, 2004.3 a(Producer) Sensitivity to insulin-mediated glucose disposal varies widely in the population at large. The abnormalities related to insulin resistance have broadened considerably, and the adverse clinical outcomes extend beyond type 2 diabetes and CVD. The Insulin Resistance Syndrome seeems to be a logical choice to replace the term Syndrome X to provide a pathophysiological construct with which to view the different clinical syndromes that occur more commonly in insulin resistant individuals.  aAlso available online.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aMetabolic Syndrome1 aReaven, Gerald M.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pNIH director's astute clinician lecture ;v7th.4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=3430  aAUTH00967cam a22002777a 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040002100073044001200094060003300106100001900139245009300158260004700251300002000298336002600318337002800344338002700372500008900399500003600488561008600524650003200610650002000642700001800662999000900680101272157DNLM20260204124351.0060322s1880    be            000 0 fre    aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Belgium00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1285 no.201 aBruylants,cM.10aRecherches sur le microbe de la pleuropneumonie bovine /cpar MM. Bruylants et Verriest.  aBruxelles :bLibrairie H. Manceaux,c1880.  a23 p. ;c23 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"Extrait du Bulletin de l'Académie royale de médecine, t. XIV, 3e série no 7."  aNLM copy: unopened bolts.5DNLM  aNLM copy provenance: April 8, 1895 stamp of Johns Hopkins Hospital Library.5DNLM12aPleuropneumonia, Contagious22aCattle Diseases1 aVer