ebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, no. 1 (Jan. 2008)-  aDescription based on first issue; title from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan. 2008-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan. 2008-  aAlso issued online.12aGeriatric Nursing 2aPeriodical0 x1938-24644 uhttps://journals.healio.com/journal/rgn  aAUTH01381cas a2200409   7503834DNLM20260227090924.0cr|cn#||||||||750516c19749999xxuqr         0||| 0eng    a0096-3925l0096-3925  aMUBBDD  a(DNLM)M49280000(s)  a(OCoLC)01245905  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM1 aenghrus  9United States00aW1bMO931N10aMoscow Univ Biol Sci Bull2dnlm00aMoscow University biological sciences bulletin.  aNew York,bAllerton Press.  av.billus.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 29-    1974-  aAlso issued online.  aTranslation of the Biology section of issues of Vestnik Moskovskogo Universiteta, Seriia 6: Biologiia, pochvovedenie. 2aBiology 2aPeriodical2 aMoskovskiĭ gosudarstvennyĭ universitet im. M.V. Lomonosova.2 aVestnik Moskovskogo Universiteta.bSeriia 6: Biologiia, pochvovedenie.1 tthe Biology section of issues of Vestnik Moskovskogo Universiteta, Seriia 6: Biologiia, pochvovedenie.0 x1934-791X4 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/11966  aAUTH02878cgm a22004214a 101524371DNLM20260227153259.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u100213s2010    mdu053|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15527  a(OCoLC)614264622  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWD 3801 aCharles, Nicolas,d1978-14aThe Th2 environment and autoimmunity :bmaking sense of IgE in lupus /cNicolas Charles ; Immunology Interest Group.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (53 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jan. 6, 2010.3 a(CIT): The first seminar of the new year features one of our own, Dr. Nicolas Charles of the Laboratory of Molecular Immunogenetics of NIAMS.  As a native of France, Nico appropriately began his scientific career working towards the discovery of new molecules to combat cryptogamic diseases of the grapevine. He then started his PhD studies in the laboratory of Boris Vargaftig at the Institut Pasteur but subsequently moved to Xavier Bichat Medical School in Paris with his mentor, Marc Benhamou. During his PhD studies, Nico discovered that phospholipid scramblase and p28 are part of the high affinity IgE receptor signal transduction cascade and showed that phospholipid scramblase is activated by the IgE receptor and is required for normal mast cell degranulation, a previously unrecognized role for this family of proteins.  Nico received his PhD in 2005 and subsequently came to the NIH to work in the Laboratory of Molecular Immunogenetics with Juan Rivera.  Since his arrival he has explored whether there exists a relationship between allergic and autoimmune diseases.  In recently published work (Immunity 30:533-543, 2009), Nico found that basophils control the Th2 differentiation and that basophil-expressed Lyn kinase is necessary to govern the extent of Th2 differentiation and response.  In more recent work he has uncovered a connection between the dysregulation of the Th2 environment and lupus nephritis.  This provocative finding is supported by preliminary studies in SLE patients.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aLupus Erythematosus, Systemicximmunology22aImmunoglobulin Eximmunology22aTh2 Cellsximmunology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bImmunology Interest Group.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15527  aAUTH01437cgm a22004094a 101267704DNLM20260227145550.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2000    mdu018 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10581  a(OCoLC)70051251  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10