ries, is the genetic basis for the capacity of C. elegans to survive bouts of hypoxia. This work, which has obvious clinical relevance, has uncovered important connections between protein homeostasis and the ability of organisms to deal with hypoxic insults.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aHypoxiaximmunology22aCaenorhabditis elegans Proteinsxmetabolism22aCaenorhabditis elegansxgenetics22aDisease Models, Animal22aHomeostasisxphysiology22aImmunity, Innatexgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH neuroscience seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15382  aAUTH02272cgm a22004454a 101498039DNLM20260227152952.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090303s2009    mdu223 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14924  a(OCoLC)359240061  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQV 7712 aNIH STEP Forum.10aFinders, keepers :brecruitment and retention of research participants in NIH-Supported clinical trials /cKay Dickersin ... [et al.].  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed May 11, 1990).  aStreaming video (3 hr., 42 min., 13 sec. : sd., col.).  aAccess restricted to HHS.5DNLM  aRecorded Feb. 19, 2009.3 a(CIT): Clinical trials investigators have difficulties recruiting and retaining volunteers. Insufficient numbers, lack of diversity, and attrition pose threats to the progress and success of these studies. What motivates individuals to participate in clinical trials? What are the strategies for long term retention? What are roles for Scientific Review Officers, Program Officials, Grants Management Specialists, and Data and Safety Monitoring Board members related to study design and progress? This forum will explore challenges to the identification, enrollment, and retention of research participants in clinical trials; and discuss successful techniques for recruitment and retention of study participants.  For more information, visit  http://odoerdb2.od.nih.gov/oer/training/step/step_training_20090219.htm.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aClinical Trials as Topic22aPatient Selection22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aDickersin, Kay.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14924  aAUTH01259cas a2200409 a 9605507DNLM20260227091021.0cr|cn#||||||||961121c19969999nyu x p       0    0eng    a1082-6076l1082-6076  aJLCTFC  a(DNLM)SR0086576(s)  a(OCoLC)32501604  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bJO745P10aJ Liq Chromatogr Relat Technol2dnlm00aJournal of liquid chromatography & related technologies.3 aJournal of liquid chromatography and related technologies  aMonticello, NY :bMarcel Dekker,c1996-  av. :bill.  aTwenty no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 19, no. 1 (Jan. 1996)-  aTitle from cover.0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online. 2aBiotechnology 2aChromatography, Liquid 2aPeriodical0 x1520-572X00tJournal of liquid chromatographyx0148-3919w(OCoLC)35273064 uhttps://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ljlc20  aAUTH01812cam a22004094a 101119656DNLM20260204164649.0010604s1999    gw a     b    100 0 eng    a9783000042768  a3000042768  a(OCoLC)48435318  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aengager  apcc  9Germany00aQZ 269bI6195s 19992 aInternational Symposium on Recent Advances in Radiation Oncologyd(1999 :cMunich, Germany)10aSymposiumsband /c"International Symposium on Recent Advances in Radiation Oncology," 4.-6. März 1999, Klinikum Grosshadern, München ; Herausgeber, E. Dühmke, S. Sehlen.  a[München] :bLudwig-Maximilians-Universität München, Klinik und Poliklinik für Strahlentherapie und Radioonk