ay press conference  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2000]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed on June 12, 2006).  aStreaming video (50 min., 28 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded May 3, 2000.3 a(CIT): May 3, 2000 marks the second annual World Asthma Day, and more than 80 countries across the globe will observe it with special events.  The official U.S. World Asthma Day event will be held in Washington, DC.  Co-sponsored by the NHLBI and NLM, along with the Office of the Mayor, District of Columbia, and the Washington, D.C. Asthma Coalition, it will focus on the high prevalence of asthma in the U.S., especially in inner-city communities like the District of Columbia, and steps to curb it.  The program will be hosted by NHLBI Director Dr.  Claude Lenfant.  Other participants include NLM Director Dr.  Donald A.B. Lindberg, D.C.  Department of Health Director Dr. Ivan Walks, and Grammy Award-winning Rap Artist and Asthmatic Coolio,   Children from a Washington, D.C. School Asthma Club will perform a skit and sing a song to celebrate their ability to control their asthma.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aAsthmaxprevention & control22aAsthmaxepidemiology22aPublic Health Practice 2aUnited Statesxepidemiology 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10072  aAUTH01840cas a2200505 i 101638820DNLM20260224111548.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||140806c20149999nyu|| poo     |    0eng    a  2018243243  a2426-0266l2274-5807  a(OCoLC)1048007708  aAU@bengcAU@erdadDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW110aJ Prev Alzheimers Dis2dnlm04aThe journal of prevention of Alzheimer's disease.23aJPAD 1aAuzeville-Tolosane :bSERDI éd.,