ds22aMidwiferyxmethods 2aAddress2 aTri-State Medical Society of Illinois, Indiana, and Kentucky.0 aSaint Louis medical and surgical journal.  aAUTH01614cas a2200457 a 101502773DNLM20260227090911.0cr|cn ||||||||090420c20099999ne || p       |    0eng    a  2009243262  a1877-0657l1877-0657  a(OCoLC)319148735  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aengafre  alcd  9Netherlands00aW1bAN377F10aAnn Phys Rehabil Med2dnlm00aAnnals of physical and rehabilitation medicine.  aAmsterdam :bElsevier Masson  aBimonthly,b2015-  aTen no a year,b2009-2014  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 52, no 1 (Feb. 2009).  aDescription based on: Vol. 52, no 1 (Feb. 2009); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 52, no 1 (Feb. 2009).1 aMEDLINEbv52n1, Feb. 2009-0 aPubMedbv52n1, Feb. 2009-  aAlso issued online.  aArticles in English and French, with French text coming after the English text in each article.12aPhysical and Rehabilitation Medicine22aRehabilitation 2aPeriodical2 aSociété française de médecine physique et de réadaptation.0 x1877-066500tAnnales de réadaptation et de médecine physiquex0168-6054w(DLC)sn 870268543w(OCoLC)152858134 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/18770657  aAUTH02056cgmaa22004334a 101180569DNLM20260227144255.0vf|cbahouvf|cjahou030530s2003    mdu060 ||    f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:1892  a(OCoLC)53476953  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWP 870bVC no.143 200300aInflammatory breast cancer :bgenetic determinants and challenges for novel therapeutics /c[Office of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch].  a[Bethesda, MD :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3master.  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (60 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aThe NIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture0 aSpeaker, Sofia D. Merajver.  aPresented April 23, 2003.3 a(Producer) Inflammatory breast cancer is the most lethal form of breast cancer.  Two genes appear to be important determinants of this aggressive breast cancer phenotype.  When acting in concert, over-expression of RhoC and loss of WISP3 cooperate to create an inflammatory-like phenotype in breast cells. Targeting these alterations may lead to a rational therapy for aggressive breast cancer phenotypes.  aVHS.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aBreast Neoplasmsxgenetics22aOncogenes22aGenes, Tumor Suppressor.1 aMerajver, Sofia D.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=1892  aAUTH01722cgm a2200469 i 101772121DNLM20260227160150.0m     o  z f      vz|czaz|ucr|cna||||||||201006s2019    mdu048 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33370  a(OCoLC)1201223376  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.500aNIH's scientific approach to inclusive excellence /cHannah A. Valantine. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2019]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (48 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Clinical Center grand rounds, contemporary issues in graduate medical education  aRecorded July 10, 2019.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed October 20, 2020).22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aResearch Personnel22aCultural Diversity22aAcademies and Institutes22aUnited States Government Agencies22aResearch Support as Topic 2aUnited States 2