2rdacarrier  aRecorded Nov. 17, 2011.3 a(CIT): The event will feature the latest interdisciplinary research findings on women's health and sex and gender factors that affect health and disease. For more information, visit: http://orwh.od.nih.gov.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aSex Factors22aWomen's Health 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Research on Women's Health.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16985  aAUTH02192cgm a22003854a 101463201DNLM20260227152321.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080102s2007    mdu328 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14186  a(OCoLC)228114629  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWM 1882 aNational Center on Sleep Disorders Research (National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute).bSleep Disorders Research Advisory Board.bMeetingn(27th :d2005 :cBethesda, Md.)10aNIH Sleep Disorders Research Advisory Board Meeting :bDecember 2007 /cNational Center on Sleep Disorders Research, NHLBI.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Apr. 2, 2008).  aStreaming video (5 hr., 28 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 4, 2007.3 a(CIT): The National Center on Sleep Disorders Research (NCSDR), located within the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) of the National Institutes of Health (NIH), was established in 1993 to combat a serious public health concern. About 70 million Americans suffer from sleep problems; among them, nearly 60 percent have a chronic disorder. Each year, sleep disorders, sleep deprivation, and sleepiness add an estimated $15.9 billion to the national health care bill. Additional costs to society for related health problems, lost worker productivity, and accidents have not been calculated. Sleep disorders and disturbances of sleep comprise a broad range of problems, including sleep apnea, narcolepsy, insomnia, parasomnia, jet-lag syndrome, and disturbed biological and circadian rhythms.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aSleep Wake Disorders 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14186  aAUTH01589cgm a2200457 i 101546200DNLM20260227153914.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u101027s2010    mdu257 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16096  a(DNLM)CIT:16095  a(OCoLC)685111219  aDNLMcDNLMerdadDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2061 aUnited States.bNational Cancer Advisory Board.bMeetingn(155th :d2010 :cBethesda, Md.)14aThe National Cancer Advisory Board Meeting :bSeptember 2010 /cNCI.  a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2010]  a1 online resource (4 hr., 13 min.) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdm2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded September 7 & 8, 2010.3 a(CIT): The 155th meeting of the National Cancer Advisory Board.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.)12aBiomedical Researchxorganization & administration12aNeoplasms22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1609640uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16095  aAUTH01815cas a2200517 a 9112018DNLM20260227091022.0cr|cnu||||||||910912c19919999gw qr p       0    0eng    asn 91033492   a1210-0668l1210-0668y0013-7200  aEREGE3  a(DNLM)SR0072018(s)  a(OCoLC)24270847  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcdansdp  9Germany00aW1bEN367CH10aEndocr Regul2dnlm 0aEndocrine regulationsb(Bratislava)00aEndocrine regulations.  aBratislava, Czech and Slovak Federal Republic :bVeda ;aBasel, Switzerland :bKarger Libri, distributor,c1991-3132016- :aBerlin :