well as identify future research agendas.  Leading breast cancer physicians will be presenting the state of the science and engaging in a panel discussion in which audience participation is encouraged.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aBreast Neoplasmsxdrug therapy22aAntineoplastic Agentsxtherapeutic use22aNeoadjuvant Therapy22aNeoplasm Invasiveness22aPreoperative Carexmethods 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1371840uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13719  aAUTH02494cgm a2200421 i 9918332580706676DNLM20260227161814.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220104s2021    mdu616|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32088  a(DNLM)CIT:32089  a(OCoLC)1299139209  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQU 260.5.M62 aMitochondrial Dysfunction as a Universal Driver for Increased Health Risks (Meeting)d(2021 :cOnline)jauthor.10aMitochondrial Dysfunction as a Universal Driver for Increased Health Risks :bfrom COVID to COSMOS /cNIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (10 hr., 16 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded December 2 & 3, 2021.3 a(CIT): We are delighted to welcome you to join us for this exciting meeting on the relevance of mitochondrial biology to multiple health states and diseases.The goal of this meeting is to increase the awareness of the importance of mitochondria in disease initiation and progression, plus highlight the effects of unique environments on mitochondrial function and discuss what is needed to support the development of advanced diagnostics and sensors for bioenergetics that can monitor for disease onset and progression.The meeting is split up into four sessions over two days with the following main topics: 1. Mitochondrial impact on immune function and inflammation; 2. Impact of viral and bacterial pathogenesis on mitochondria; 3. Mitochondria in space and other unique environments; and 4. Preventative and therapeutics impact on bioenergetics and mitochondria impact with disease progression.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed February 17, 2022).12aMitochondrial Diseases12aMitochondriaxpathology 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4417240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44175  aAUTH01276nam a2200373 i 9918863366506676DNLM20260209062223.0240323s2023    au ac    bc   000 0 ger    a9783903179646qpaperback  a3903179647qpaperback  a(OCoLC)1427695375  aOHXbengerdacOHX  apcc  9Austria00aWZ 17 7aR2lcco0 aHeilkunst (Krenn)10aHeilkunst :bzur Geschichte der Medizin : 09. April bis 31. Oktober 2022 ; 01. April bis 31. Oktober 2023 /cherausgegeben von Katharina Krenn. 1aTrautenfels :bSchloss Trautenfels, Universalmuseum Joanneum,c2023.  a221 pages :billustrations (chiefly color), portraits ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 212-215).12aHistory of Medicine22aExhibitions as Topic 2aAustria 2aCatalog 2aPictorial Work1 aKrenn, Katharina,eeditor.2 aUniversalmuseum Joanneum.bSchloss Trautenfels,eissuing body.  aAUTH02552cgm a2200541 i 101776743DNLM20260227160825.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210302s2021    mdu072|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31559  a(OCoLC)1249794395  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWY 20.500aJourneys into nursing research /cAlyson Ross, Caroline Frazier, Cecelia Henry, and Alexis Braxton. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[Nation