onal Service Center (U.S.)12aNeoplasmsxtherapy12aUnited States Government Agencies22aAnniversaries and Special Events 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aDeVita, Vincent T.,cJr.,d1935-40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?12942  aAUTH02575cgmaa22005294a 101233371DNLM20260227144531.0vf|czahmucr|cna||||||||vf|cjahouvd|cvaizuhd|bfa012baap041103s2004    mdu059 ||    f    vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:3427  a(OCoLC)57422717  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aQW 165.5.P2bVC no.1 200400aLife cycle of human papillomaviruses in differentiating epithelia /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2004]  a1 videocassette of 1 (DVCPRO) (59 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/4 in.3master.  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (59 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videodisc of 1 (DVD) (59 min.) :bsd., col. ;c4 3/4 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aWALS--the George Khoury lecture  aTitle from cassette spine label.  aSpeaker, Laimonis A. Laimins.  aOriginally presented Oct. 13, 2004.3 a(Producer) The productive life cycle of human papillomaviruses is dependent upon epithelial differentiation with synthesis of new virions restricted to highly differentiated suprabasal cells. Methods have been developed to synthesize HPV 31 virions from cloned transfected DNA templates, allowing for a genetic analysis of HPV functions during the productive life cycle.  aAlso available online.  aVideocassette (Betacam SP)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2011.e1 videocassette (59 min.) : sd., col. ; 1/2 in.  aVideodisc (DVD)bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2011.e1 videodisc (59 min.) : sd., col. ; 4 3/4 in.  aVHS.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public do