  9Switzerland00aW1bAC80710aActa Haematol2dnlm00aActa haematologica.  aBasel,bKarger.  av.billus.  aEight no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       1948-1 aMEDLINEbv34n1,Jul. 1965-1 aPubMedbv34n1,Jul. 1965-0 aOLDMEDLINE1 aIndex medicus  aAlso available online.  aArticles in English, French or German, with summaries in all three languages.  aOfficial organ of the société internationale européene d'hématologie, 1950-June 1951; of the Société européene d'hématologie, July 1951-1967 (no. 2/3); of the European Division of the International Society of Haematology, 1967 (no. 5/6)-  aEvery 5th vol. includes a five year cumulative index.  3Vol. 87, no. 1 (1992)c19921001fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aHematology 2aPeriodical2 aEuropean Society of Haematology.2 aInternational European Society of Hematology.2 aInternational Society of Hematology.bEuropean Division.0 x1421-96624 uhttp://www.karger.com/Journal/Home/223829  aAUTH02070cgm a22004334a 101294897DNLM20260227151937.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu064 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13526  a(OCoLC)84725864  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aBF 3211 aNobre, Kia.10aOrienting attention in the human brain :bbeyond space and time /cKia Nobre.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 23, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 3 min., 24 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 4, 2006.3 a(CIT): Dr. Nobre's research investigates the principles of functional organisation of neural systems controlling cognition. She uses state-of-the-art methodology with which to image non-invasively the human brain at work (e.g., functional magnetic resonance imaging and event related potentials), in order to characterise the neural systems underpinning selective attention, language and memory.  She is an elected Council Member of the Organisation of Human Brain Mapping.  Dr. Nobre also heads the Brain & Cognition Lab.  The methodological approach is to combine behavioural measures (e.g., reaction times, eye movements) with non-invasive brain imaging methods (mainly fMRI and ERPs).    NIH Neuroscience Seminar Series.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aAttentionxphysiology22aBrainxphysiology22aNeural Pathwaysxphysiology22aOrientationxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13526  aAUTH01342cgm a22004214a 101294033DNLM20260227144808.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061129s2006    mdu065|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:5534  a(OCoLC)84725731  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 26.51 aBassingthwaighte, James B.10aIntegrating biology from gene to organism :bthe physiome projects /cJames Bassingthwai[h]te.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Dec. 19, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 5 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 21, 2006.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aPhysiome Project.12aSystems Biology22aGenetics, Medical22aPhysiological Phenomenaxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5534  aAUTH01690cgm a22004574a 101294893DNLM20260227151910.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061206s2006    mdu540 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13522  a(DNLM)CIT:13523  a(OCoLC)84722508  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2061 aUnited States.bNational Cancer Advisory Board.bMeetingn(140th :d200