z|u060209s1999    mdu347 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10023  a(OCoLC)64760696  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 3000aLeadership conference :bbiomedical research and the environment.nDay 1 /cNIEHS.30aBomedical research and the environment.nDay 1  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c1999]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Mar. 10, 2006).  aStreaming video (5 hr., 46 min., 45 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 1, 1999.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aEnvironmental Health22aBiomedical Research22aEnvironmental Pollution 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute of Environmental Health Sciences.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10023  aAUTH02600cgm a22004814a 101267511DNLM20260227145158.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2002    mdu999 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10139  a(DNLM)CIT:10140  a(DNLM)CIT:10141  a(OCoLC)69391290  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWE 2582 aNorth American Symposium on Skeletal Complications of Malignancyn(3rd :d2002 :cNational Institutes of Health)10aThird North American Symposium on Skeletal Complications of Malignancy /cPaget Foundation, NCI, and Penn State Milton S. Hershey Medical Center.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2002]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed May 17, 2006).  aStreaming video (18 hr., 3 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 25-27, 2002.3 a(CIT): Skeletal Complications of Malignancy will address the pathophysiology of the special forms of bone disease that occur in breast cancer, prostate cancer and multiple myeloma and the role of the bone marrow microenvironment in supporting bone metastases.  Recent data show significant new information on the molecular mechanisms responsible for the effects of these different malignancies on the skeleton, and are providing novel and exciting potential targets for innovative drug therapies.    These new findings will be presented by the international experts with updates on preclinical and clinical studies of currently utilized therapeutic agents.  The symposium is designed for basic scientists and clinicians with interest in oncology, urology, hematology, and bone metabolism.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aBone Neoplasmsxsecondary22aBreast Neoplasmsxpathology22aMultiple Myelomaxpathology22aProstatic Neoplasmsxpathology 2aWebcast2 aPaget Foundation.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1013940uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1014040uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10141  aAUTH00819cam a22002537i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002100073040003500094044001000129060003300139110006000172245006900232264004500301300005100346336002600397337002800423338002700451650003200478650003400510655001200544999000900556101610049DNLM20260209111714.0130610s1951    cc ac    c    000 0 chi    a(OCoLC)894626105  aDNLMbengerdad20260209dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1777 no.162 aTianjin Shi guo yao ye cheng yao lian ying zu,eauthor.10aTianjin Shi guo yao ye cheng yao lian ying zu cheng yao shou ce. 1aTianjin Shi :bGuo yao gong hui,c[1951]  a26 unnumbered pages :billustrations, portrait  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aPharmaceutical Preparations22aMedicine, Chinese Traditional 2aCatalog  aAUTH02213cgm a2200457 i 9918299484006676DNLM2026022716