ns for treating adolescents /cNational Institute of Mental Health.1 iAt head of title:aNational Children's Mental Health Awareness  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 54 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded May 10, 2012.3 a(CIT): As part of National Children"s Mental Health Awareness, NIMH is sponsoring a videocast panel of children"s mental health researchers.  Panelists will discuss neuroscience research findings related to: teen brain development, cognition and emotional and behavioral growth, and treatment for teens.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aBrainxgrowth & development12aMental Disordersxtherapy22aAdolescent22aAdolescent Behaviorxphysiology22aAdolescent Development22aCognitionxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute of Mental Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17260  aAUTH01386cas a2200433 a 101531704DNLM20260227090908.0cr||||||||||||100524c20079999it || p       |    0ita    a  2011243889  a1877-9344l1877-9344  a(OCoLC)762755140  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 aitaaeng  apcc  9Italy00aW1bIT1355M00aItalian journal of medicine.  aMilano :bElsevier Srl3132013- :aVoghera :bPAGEPress  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, 1 (mar. 2007).  aPrint issues ceased with v. 13 (2019).  aAlso issued online.  aText in Italian and English.  aDescription based on: Vol. 5, n. 1 (mar. 2011); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 5, n. 3 (sett. 2011).12aMedicine 2aPeriodical2 aFederazione delle associazioni dei dirigenti ospedalieri internisti.0 x1877-935200tGiornale italiano di medicina interna4 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/187793444 uhttps://www.italjmed.org/i