tional information about the High Risk-High Reward program is available at http://commonfund.nih.gov/highrisk/   Addtional information about the High Risk-High Reward program is available at http://commonfund.nih.gov/highrisk/.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed Feb. 2, 2015.22aHigh-Risk High-Reward Program (NIH Common Fund)12aBiomedical Researchxeconomics22aAwards and Prizes22aFinancing, Governmentxeconomics22aGovernment Programsxeconomics22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1878640uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1878540uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18784  aAUTH02518cgm a2200469 i 101647951DNLM20260227154759.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u141202s2014    mdu406|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18708  a(OCoLC)900626373  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQT 25600aUnderstanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms of physical activity-Induced health benefits /cNIH Common Fund, NIDDK, NIAMS, NIA. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (6 hr., 46 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aRecorded October 30, 2014.3 a(CIT): The NIH Common Fund is currently exploring research needs and opportunities related to the molecular mechanisms whereby physical activity prevents disease and improves health outcomes. This activity is undertaken with the leadership of the NIH Institute Directors Richard Hodes, M.D., National Institute on Aging (NIA), Stephen I. Katz, M.D., Ph.D., National Institute of Arthritis and Musculoskeletal and Skin Diseases (NIAMS), and Griffin Rodgers, M.D., National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK), and with broad support throughout the NIH. The Trans NIH Committee Physical Activity Common Fund (PACF) Working Group plans to cover the broad aspects of physical activity related benefits under 5 sub-working groups within these ICs (NIAMS, NIDDK, NIA and OSC).  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed January 16, 2016.12aExercisexphysiology22aHealth Behavior22aHealth Promotionxmethods22aMotor Activityxphysiology22aPhysical Fitness 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNIH Common Fund,eissuing body.2 aNational Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNational Institute of Arthritis and Musculoskeletal and Skin Diseases (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNational Institute on Aging,eissuing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18708  aAUTH01677cgm a2200469 i 101752797DNLM20260227160043.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u190815s2019    mdu044|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:28680  a(OCoLC)1121608928  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 2600aOD launch of the NIH property management portal /cEmily Ballou. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2019]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (44 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aAccess restricted to NIH only.5DNLM  aRecorded July 31, 2019.3 a(CIT): The event will be used to launch the NIH Property Portal for the Office of the Director.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed September 13, 2019).22aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)12aBiomedical Research12aEquipment and Supplies22aOffice Management22aSoftware22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aUnited States 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aBallou, Emilyq(Emily Moore),espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of 