101718810DNLM20260227155739.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u180103s2017    mdu727 ||||||fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:23642  a(DNLM)CIT:23644  a(OCoLC)1020448898  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 3541 aUnderstanding Traumatic Brain Injury in Women (Workshop)d(2017 :cBethesda, Md.)jauthor.10aUnderstanding traumatic brain injury in women workshop /cNINDS, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2017]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (12 hr., 7min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded December 18-19, 2017.3 a(CIT): The purpose of the "Understanding TBI in Women" workshop is to bring together researchers and clinicians to identify knowledge gaps, best practices, and target populations in research that focuses on females and/or sex differences within the field of traumatic brain injury (TBI).  Women are under-represented in TBI clinical trials, and the reasons for this disparity in enrollment need to be identified and addressed.  In addition, pre-clinical studies have often excluded females or have used ovariectomized rather than intact animals, leading to an incomplete understanding of TBI in females.  This workshop will focus on the existing knowledge regarding sex differences in TBI research and how these differences can be incorporated in pre-clinical and clinical efforts going forward.  Deliverables from the workshop will include a White Paper that can be converted into a journal publication that describes the workshop, outlines the state of the science, and identifies future directions for research.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed January 16, 2018 ).12aBrain Injuries, Traumatic22aSex Factors22aWomen 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute of Neurological Diseases and Stroke,