istics & numerical data22aElectronic Health Records22aInformation Dissemination22aConfidentiality22aOutcome Assessment, Health Care 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aRutter, Joni L.,espeaker.2 aNational Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (U.S.),esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44660  aAUTH01332cam a2200349 i 101766767DNLM20260212085929.0cr||||||||||||200501r18881888miu      b    000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)1153550059  aDNLMbengerdad20260212dDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5391 no.211 aMarshall, John,d1855-1925eauthor.10aOn the absorption of lead chromate /cby John Marshall. 1aDetroit, Mich. :bGeorge S. Davis,c1888.  a18 pages ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCover title.  aReprinted from the Therapeutic gazette for February 15, 1888.  aIncludes bibliographical references.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aNLM copy, inscription, Comps of J.M., on cover.5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20210201lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM1 adigitizedc20232pda5DNLM12aLeadxpharmacokinetics22aChromatesxpharmacokinetics4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/101766767  aAUTH02259cgm a2200445 i 9918573277106676DNLM20260227162851.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230302s2022    mdu087|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32740  a(OCoLC)1428107684  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.52 aGender and Health Workshop Concurrent Session: Measurements & Methodsd2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aGender and health workshop concurrent session :bmeasurements & methods /cORWH, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 27 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded October 26, 2022.3 a(CIT): In recognition of the significant health impacts of gender as a social and cultural variable, the NIH ORWH and the Eunice Kennedy Shriver NICHD convened a series of roundtable discussions for NIH staff members in the fall of 2021. Participants discussed the landscape of NIH-supported research on gender roles, gender norms, and gender inequity and identified opportunities in this space.  This scientific workshop is an exciting opportunity to convene the extramural community, NIH scientific and program staff members, and other stakeholders to discuss methods and best practices for biomedical and sociobehavioral research on gender roles, gender norms, and gender inequity.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed March 1, 2024).12aGender Equity12aSexism12aQualitative Research22aCohort Studies22aRisk Factors22aPublic Policy 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Research on Women's Health,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=46416  aAUTH02461cgm a2200493 i 9918592672106676DNLM20260227163451.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230429s2023    mdu705|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33046  a(DNLM)CIT:33052  a(DNLM)CIT:33054  a(OCoLC)1437827881  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWM 2202 aNational Research Summit on Care, Services, and Supports for Persons with Dementia and their Care Partners/Caregiversd(2023 :cOnline)jauthor.10aNational research summit on care, services and supports for persons living with dementia and their care partners/caregivers (day 1, 2 & 3) /cNational Institute on Aging, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (3 streaming video files (11 hr., 45 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded March 20, 21 & 22, 2023.3 a(CIT): The National Institute on Aging (NIA) will host the third triennial National Research Summit on Care, Services, and Supports for Persons with Dementia and their Caregivers/Care Partners on March 20-22, 2023. The Summit will build on the progress of the previous Summits to review research progress, highlight innovative and promising research, and identify remaining unmet research needs with input from the research community, persons living with dementia and their care partners, those who provide healthcare or services and supports to persons living with dementia, and other stakeholders.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed May 29, 2024).12aDementia22aCaregivers22aHealth Services Research22aHealth Workforce22aHealth Equity22aHealthcare Disparities 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institute on Aging,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4931140uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4931340uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49315  aAUTH01217cam a2200325 i 60441430RDNLM20260206221705.0cr||||||||||||820514s1902    iluc     b    000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14776629  aDNLMbengerdad20260206dDNLM  9United States00aHQbC295L 19021 aCarpenter, Edward,d1844-1929,eauthor.10aLove's coming-of-age :ba series of papers on the relations of the sexes /cby Edward Carpenter. 1aChicago :bStockham Publishing Co.,c1902.  a162 pages :bportraits ;c17 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20250625lconservation not necessar