e (1 streaming video file (41 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNCI's Center for Cancer Research grand rounds  aAccess restricted to HHS only.5DNLM  aRecorded October 7, 2016.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed December 5, 2016).12aPancreatic Neoplasmsximmunology12aPancreatic Neoplasmsxtherapy22aImmunotherapy 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aJaffee, Elizabeth M.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aCCR grand rounds40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19920  aAUTH03048cgm a22004214a 101507155DNLM20260227152927.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090605s2009    mdu084|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15048  a(OCoLC)723031254  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 530.11 aSachs, Jeffrey.10aPlanet in crisis :bthe case for investing in global health during a financial meltdown /cJeffrey Sachs.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner.  aStreaming video (1 hr., 24 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 22, 2009.3 a(CIT): Notable economist, best-selling author and global health advocate Jeffrey Sachs will visit NIH on April 22 as a Fogarty International Center Scholar-in-Residence, part of its 40th anniversary activities.  The event is sponsored by the Foundation for NIH.  "Planet in Crisis: The Case for Investing in Global Health During a Financial Meltdown"  Professor Jeffrey Sachs Director of the Earth Institute Quetelet Professor of Sustainable Development Professor of Health Policy and Management at Columbia University   Professor Sachs is director of the Earth Institute, Quetelet professor of sustainable development, and professor of health policy and management at Columbia University. For more than 20 years he has been in the forefront of the challenges of economic development, poverty alleviation, and enlightened globalization, promoting policies to help all parts of the world to benefit from expanding economic opportunities and wellbeing. He is also one of the leading voices for combining economic development with environmental sustainability, and as director of the Earth Institute leads large-scale efforts to promote the mitigation of human-induced climate change.  He is the author of hundreds of scholarly articles and many books, including the New York Times bestsellers "Common Wealth: Economics for a Crowded Planet" and "The End of Poverty." Sachs is a member of the Institute of Medicine and is a Research Associate of the National Bureau of Economic Research.  The event is sponsored by the Foundation for NIH with generous support from Lilly, the Abbott Fund, Bristol-Myers Squibb Foundation, ExxonMobil, Pepsico, Aeras Global TB Vaccine Foundation, the Burroughs Wellcome Fund, Merck, Pfizer, Tibotec and the United Nations Foundation.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGlobal Health22aEnvironmental Health22aPoverty 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15048  aAUTH01616cgm a22004094a 101285767DNLM20260227151554.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060822s2006    mdu109|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13265  a(OCoLC)71233130  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aBF 57600aEmotional intelligence /cNIH Work/Life Center (WLC).  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Aug. 28, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 49 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jun. 1, 2006.3 a(CIT): What is Emotional Intelligence (EI)? It captures what "smarts" doesn't, e.g., initiative, adaptability, collaboration, and performance improvement drive. Learn how "EI" can be critical to your career development and professional success and then begin to identify ways to enhance your personal EI.   For more information, visit   http://wlc.od.nih.gov.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aExpressed Emotion22aIntelligence22aInterprofessional Relations 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bWork Life Center.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13265  aAUTH01257cas a2200409 a 101554949DNLM20260224111557.0cr||||||||||||110226c20109999oncfr p       0    0eng    a  2012243210  a2040-5111l2040-5111  a(OCoLC)695296427  aEQOcEQOdDNLM  apcc  9Canada00aW1bJO716DL10aJ Interact Res Commun Disord2dnlm00aJournal of interactional research in communication disorders.13aJIRCD  aLondon :bEquinox Pub.3132025- :aToronto :bUniversity of Toronto Press  av. :bill. ;c24 cm.  aSemiannual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with: Vol. 1.1 (2010).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Vol. 1.1 (2010); title from title page.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 2.2 (2011).12aCommunication Disorders22aInterpersonal Relations0 x2040-512X4 uhttps://utppublishing.com/journal/jircd  aAUTH01648cgm a22004814a 101285736DNLM20260227151723.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060822s2006    mdu093|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13331  a(OCoLC)71233122  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 20.51 aClaycamp, Rebecca.10aGMAC-the times-they are a changing /cRebecca Claycamp, Pierre Noel, and George B. Gardner.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Aug.