 animal models of human conditions such as addiction, depression, and dementia.  What are these assays and what are their limits?  How are they validated?  How closely do they really mimic human biology and behavior?  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aModels, Animal22aBehavior, Animal 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aCrawley, Jacqueline N.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bStaff Training-Extramural Programs Committee.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13624  aAUTH01401cas a2200445 a 101582666DNLM20260227090923.0cr||||||||||||120321c20129999enk|| p       0    0eng    a  20122433467 a0157834912Uk  a2046-9047l2046-9047  a(OCoLC)781114060  aHNCcHNCdHNCdUKMGBdDNLM  apcc  9England00aW1bAN627U10aPaediatr Int Child Health2dnlm00aPaediatrics and international child health.  aLondon :bManey Publishing,c2012-3132016- :aAbingdon :bTaylor & Francis  aFour issues yearly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 32, no. 1 (Feb. 2012)-1 aMEDLINEbv32n1, Feb. 2012-0 aPubMedbv32n1, Feb. 2012-  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Vol. 32, no. 1 (Feb. 2012); title from cover.  aLatest issued consulted: Vol. 32, no. 1 (Feb. 2012).12aPediatrics22aGlobal Health22aPublic Health 2aPeriodical0 x2046-905500tAnnals of tropical paediatricsx0272-4936w(OCoLC)068550694 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ypch20  aAUTH01696cas a2200493 i 101706458DNLM20260227090929.0m     o  d        cr#|||||||||||160224c20169999enkqr poo     0    0eng    a  2016229320  a2396-9776l2396-9776  a(OCoLC)940788658  aCUVbengerdad20260227cCUVdOCLCOdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCOdDNLM  apcc  9England00aW110aVet Evid2dnlm10aVet. evid. 0aVeterinary evidence00aVeterinary evidence.13aVeterinary evidence online 1aLondon :bRCVS Knowledge,c[2016]-  a1 online resource  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acom