 av. :bill. ;c28 cm.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 376, nos. 1-6 (Jan.-Feb. 2001)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv376, Jan.-Feb. 2001-0 aPubMedbv376, Jan.-Feb. 2001-1 aIndex medicus  aCarries vol. numbering and date of the Russian original.  aAlso issued online.  aTranslated and published by: Maik nauka/Interperiodica Pub.  aEnglish translation of the biochemistry and biophysics sections of: Doklady Akademii nauk.  aMerger of: Doklady biochemistry, and: Doklady biophysics.12aBiochemistry12aBiophysics 2aPeriodical2 aAkademii︠a︡ nauk SSSR.2 aMAIK Nauka/Interperiodica Publishing.0 aDoklady Akademii nauk.lEnglish.1 tDoklady Akademii naukx0869-5652w(DLC)   93646040w(OCoLC)260021280 x1608-309114tDoklady biochemistryx0012-4958w(DLC)   96646621w(OCoLC)147878714tDoklady biophysicsx0012-4974w(DLC)   95647207w(OCoLC)331843224 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/10628  aAUTH01183nam a2200301 a 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002000073040007400093043001200167044001800179060003300197110006300230245013700293246005700430260008000487300007000567336002600637337002800663338002700691610006600718650002400784650002300808650002600831651001500857999000900872101778151DNLM20260226113603.0951211s1908    dcuaf        f000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)19808015  aHMSbengcHMSdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCFdOCLCAdOCLCQdOCLCOdOCLCLdOCLCQ  an-us-nm  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5570 no.281 aUnited States.bPublic Health and Marine Hospital Service.14aThe United States Marine-Hospital Sanatorium :bFort Stanton, New Mexico /cUnited States Public Health and Marine Hospital Service.14aMarine-Hospital Sanatorium, Fort Stanton, New Mexico  a[Washington, D.C.] :b[Public Health and Marine Hospital Service],c[1908?]  a50 pages, 3 unnumbered leaves of plates :billustrations ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier22aUnited States Marine Hospital Sanatorium (Fort Stanton, N.M.)12aHospitals, Military22aHospitals, Special22aTuberculosisxtherapy 2aNew Mexico  aAUTH02331cgm a2200457 a 101574445DNLM20260227154109.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u111208s2011    mdu058|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16900  a(OCoLC)772582423  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQV 381 aAltman, Russq(Russell Biagio),d1961-14aThe emerging network of data for understanding the interactions of genes and drugs /cRuss B. Altman.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2011]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (58 min.) :bsd., col.).  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Wednesday afternoon lecture  aRecorded Oct. 12, 2011.3 a(CIT): The last two decades have provided a flood of data relevant to drug action--from both basic science and clinical sources.  These data provide molecular, cellular, tissue, organism and population-level information about how drugs work to create both efficacy and adverse events.  Any single data source is imperfect, but integration of these sources can yield remarkable and practical discoveries as well as opportunities for application.  In this talk, I describe our recent work using informatics technologies to (1) assess the potential impact of pharmacogenomics in the era of personal genome sequencing, (2) analyze the corpus of published medical literature to extract potentially novel drug interactions along with putative mechanisms, and (3) discover a novel drug-drug interaction that may affect up to 1 million Americans.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aDrug Interactionsxgenetics22aBase Sequencexdrug effects22aGenomexdrug effects22aMedical Informatics22aPharmacogenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16900  aAUTH02200cgm a22004214a 101518942DNLM20260227153051.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u091105s2009    mdu371|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15319  a(OCoLC)529281648  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 58.52 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bRecombinant DNA Advisory Committee.10aRecombinant DNA Advisory Committee, September 2009 /cOffice of Biotechnology Activities.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner.  aStreaming video (6 hr., 11 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Sept. 9, 2009.3 a(CIT): The RAC is a technical committee whose goal is to consider the current state of knowledge and technology regarding recombinant DNA.  This includes review of human gene transfer trials, and an assessment of the ability of DNA recombinants to survive in nature and the potential for transfer of genetic material to other organisms.  It also considers hypothetical hazards and methods for monitoring and minimizing risks. Approximately one-third of the 15 members do not have scientific expertise but represent public interests and attitudes. This balance is intended to provide a forum for open public debate of social and scientific issues attendant to recombinant DNA research.  The RAC has been overwhelmingly successful in achieving this goal.   For more information, visit the  Recombinant DNA Advisory Committee (RAC) Conference Web Site.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aDNA, Recombinant22aClinical Protocolsxstandards22aGene Transfer Techniques22aGenetic Therapy 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15319  aAUTH01664cas a2200517 a 100883603DNLM20260227091039.0cr|cn ||||||||981223c19989999enkbr p       0    0eng    asn 98048097   a1462-0049l1462-0049  a(OCoLC)40540743  aJAAcJAAdWAUdEYMdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9England00aW1bEV25310aEvid Based Dent2dnlm00aEvidence-based dentistry.3 aEvidence based dentistry1 iIssues for <2004-> called also:aEBD  aLondon :bBritish Dental Journal,cc1998-3 3<2004->:aLondon :bNature Publishing Group  av. ;c28 cm.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Nov. 1998)-  aTitle from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 5, no. 1 (2004).1 aMEDLINEbv5n1, 2004-1 aPubMedbv5n1, 2004-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aOfficial publication of the British Dental Association, <2004->  3v. 1, no. 1 (JAN 1993)c20040802fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper12aDentistry22aEvidence-Based Medicine 2aPeriodical2 aBritish Dental Association.0 aBritish dental journal.0 tBritish dental journalx0007-0610w(DLC)sc 79004902w(OCoLC)15372290 x1476-54464 uhttp://www.nature.com/ebd  aAUTH01120nam a2200313 i 45000010017000000030005000170050017000220080041000390400031000800440018001110600033001291000047001622450043002092640051002523000027003033360026003303370028003563380027003845000019004115000049004305400142004795830039006215830043006606500028007036500015007316500029007467300022007759990009007979917780293406676DNLM20260226121317.0950119s1868    mau           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5570 no.171 aHelmuth, William Tod,d1833-1902,eauthor.10aSome of the wonders of modern surgery. 1a[Boston] :b[publisher not identified],c1868.  apages 373-380 ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCaption title.  aDetached from Atlantic monthly, March, 1868.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aGeneral Surgeryxtrends22aAnesthesia22aGeneral Surgeryxhistory0 aAtlantic monthly.  aAUTH01618cgm a2200445 a 101574468DNLM20260227154253.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u111208s2011    mdu180|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16944  a(OCoLC)778837487  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aW 20.55.H91 aGrady, Christine.10aEthical and regulatory aspects of clinical research.nCourse 6,pInformed consent, research with persons at risk for impaired decision-making, ethics of use of stored tissue and data /cChristine Grady, Don Rosenstein, Sara Hull.1 aInformed consent, research with persons at risk for impaired decision-making, ethics of use of stored tissue and data  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2011]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (3 hr., 0 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Nov. 2, 2011.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aInformed Consent22aConfidentiality22aConsent Forms22aDisclosure22aMental Competency22aTissue Preservationxethics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?16944  aAUTH02187cgm a2200457 i 101660619DNLM20260227155121.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u150602s2015    mdu052|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18979  a(OCoLC)911194423  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQZ 2021 aDang, Chi V.,d1954-eauthor,espeaker.10aMyc, metabolism, and cancer /cChi V. Dang. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2015]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (52 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNCI Center for Cancer Research grand rounds  aAccess restricted to HHS only.5DNLM  aRecorded May 1, 2015.3 a(CIT): The Dang laboratory has contributed to the understanding of the function of the MYC cancer gene, which has emerged as a central transcription factor or gene switch in many different human cancers.  His laboratory established the first mechanistic link between the MYC cancer gene and cellular energy metabolism, contributing to the concept that genetic alterations in cancers re-program fuel utilization by tumors and render cancers addicted to certain fuel sources. His laboratory is now exploiting these concepts for therapeutic targeting of cancer cell metabolism as a new way to treat cancer.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed June 15, 2015).12aProto-Oncogene Proteins c-mycxmetabolism22aCell Transformation, Neoplasticxgenetics22aNeoplasmsxetiology22aNeoplasmsxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aCenter for Cancer Research (National Cancer Institute (U.S.)),eissuing body. 0aCCR grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18979  aAUTH01181nam a2200289 i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003100073044001800104060003200122245013500154264005900289300003200348336002600380337002800406338002700434500005100461500006300512540014200575583003900717583004300756610004000799650002500839655001800864999000900882101778170DNLM20260225120423.0210416s1867    mau           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5571 no.200aSt. John's Hospital :bunder the charge of the Sisters of Charity : High Street Square, Lowell, Mass. : established May 1st, 1867. 1a[Lowell, Mass.] :b[publisher not identified],c[1867]  a4 unnumbered pages ;c15 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aAt head of title: Read and keep for reference.  aNLM copy, ms. corrections to text in ink throughout.5DNLM  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM22aSt. John's Hospital (Lowell, Mass.)12aHospitals, Religious 2aAdvertisement  aAUTH01435cam a2200361 i 9919051836906676DNLM20260206222516.0cr||||||||||||250623t19231923paua          001 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdad20260206dDNLM  9United States00aQL 805bD265m 19231 aDavison, Alvin,d1868-1915,eauthor.10aMammalian anatomy :bwith special references to the cat /cby Alvin Davison.  aFourth edition /brevised by Frank A. Stromsten. 1aPhiladelphia :bP. Blakiston's Son & Co.,c[1923] 4c©1923  axi, 286 pages :billustrations ;c19 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes index.  a"With 123 illustrations, most of which were made by W.H. Reese, A.M., from the Author's dissections."  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc202506232pda5DNLM  aConservedc202506232pda5DNLM1 adigitizedc20262pda5DNLM12aAnatomy, Comparative22aCatsxanatomy & histology1 aStromsten, Frank A.,d1872-1958,eeditor.4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/9919051836906676  aAUTH02313cgm a22004334a 101306078DNLM20260227152406.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070430s2007    mdu229|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13956  a(OCoLC)173469441  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWX 1732 aAmerican Health Information Community.bMeetingn(13th :d2007 :cHubert Humphrey Building)10aAmerican Health Information Community :bApril 24, 2007 /cU.S. Department of Health and Human Services.1 iTitle screen:aCommunity  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Aug. 13, 2007).  aStreaming video (3 hr., 49 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 24, 2007.3 a(CIT): The American Health Information Community (the Community), is a committee established under the Federal Advisory Committee Act (Pub. L. No. 92-463, 5 U.S.C., App.), by the Secretary of the Department of Health and Human Services.  The Community will advise the Secretary and recommend specific actions to achieve a common interoperability framework for health information technology (IT) and serve as a forum for participation from a broad range of stakeholders to provide input on achieving interoperability of health IT. The Community is made up of 17 voting members, including the Chair, and members have been appointed by the Secretary.   The Web address for the Community's draft charter is: http://www.hhs.gov/healthit/ahiccharter.pdf   A complete list of members can be found at: http://www.hhs.gov/healthit/ahic.html.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aMedical Records Systems, Computerized22aHealth Policy 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aUnited States.bDepartment of Health and Human Services.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13956  aAUTH01501cas a22004217a 9807278DNLM20260227091052.0cr|cn ||||||||980604c19989999gw qr p       0||| 0ger    asn 98039264   a1434-0275l1434-0275  a(DNLM)SR0092803(s)  a(OCoLC)39231909  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 agerbengfeng  amsc  9Germany00aW1bE2200aKlinische Neurophysiologie :borgan der Deutschen Gesellschaft für klinische Neurophysiologie.  aStuttgart ;aNew York :bGeorg Thieme Verlag ;aNew York :bThieme Medical Publishers,cc1998-3 aStuttgart :bGeorg Thieme Verlag  av.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 a29. Jahrg., Heft 1 (März 1998)-  aTitle from cover.  aSome vols. have supplements.  aAlso issued online.  aSummaries and table of contents also in English.02aNervous System Diseasesxdiagnosis 2aPeriodical2 aDeutsche Gesellschaft für klinische Neurophysiologie.00tEEG-EMG Zeitschrift für Elektroenzephalographie, Elektromyographie und verwandte Gebietew(DLC)sn 85006058w(OCoLC)52759304 uhttps://www.thieme-connect.de/products/ejournals/journal/10.1055/s-00000032  aAUTH02399cgm a2200421 i 9918450787006676DNLM20260227162555.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220804s2022    mdu242|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32497  a(OCoLC)1381435993  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.52 aStakeholder Engagement Meeting on USG Policies for the Oversight of Life Sciences Dual Use Research of Concernd(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aStakeholder engagement meeting on USG policies for the oversight of life sciences dual use research of concern /cOffice of Science Policy, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (4 hr., 2 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 29, 2022.3 a(CIT): NIH is moving to an all-virtual stakeholder engagement meeting on June 29, 2022, to discuss the U.S. Government policies for the oversight of Dual Use Research of Concern (DURC).The purpose of this meeting is to gather feedback from stakeholders about their experiences implementing these policies, the effect of these policies in terms of achieving their stated goals, the overarching definition of DURC, and possible alternative approaches for the oversight and responsible conduct of DURC. This feedback will also be used to inform the discussions of the National Science Advisory Board for Biosecurity (NSABB) in fulfillment their current charge to evaluate and analyze the DURC policies. For more information go to https://osp.od.nih.gov/.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed May 25, 2023).12aDual Use Research12aPublic Policy22aBiomedical Researchxlegislation & jurisprudence 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Science Policy,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45698  aAUTH00962cam a22002897i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002100073040003500094044001000129060003300139245009400172264010200266300003000368336002100398336003300419337002500452338002300477500002200500650003400522650002100556651001000577655001900587710005700606999000900663101607406DNLM20260205124539.0130502n19001999cc a          000 0 chi    a(OCoLC)893646310  aDNLMbengerdad20260205dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1773 no.1400aFuer de bing :bfang zhi ma zhen gu shi /cChangsha Xian ren min zhang fu wei sheng yuan. 1a[Changsha Xian] :b[Changsha Xian ren min zhang fu wei sheng yuan xuan],c[between 1900 and 1999]  a35 pages :billustrations  atext2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier  aTitle from cover.12aMeaslesxprevention & control22aHealth Education 2aChina 2aPictorial Work1 aChangsha Xian (Hunan Sheng, China).bWei sheng yuan.  aAUTH01614cas a2200421 i 101691262DNLM20260227090922.0m     o  d        cr#|nu||||||||160209c20169999ii || pso     0    0eng    a2589-0425l2311-3006  a(OCoLC)947093125  aAU@bengcAU@dOH1dOCLCOdOCLCFdOCLCOdUSUdOCLdOCLCOerdadDNLM  9India14aRC261.A100aW110aJ Cancer Res Pract2dnlm00aJournal of cancer research and practice.11aTaiwan ai zheng yi xue za zhi  a[Taipei] :bChinese Oncology Society; production and hosting by Elsevier B.V.,c2016-31a[Mumbai] :bWolters Kluwer - MedKnow  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 3, no. 1 (March 2016).