(viewed Jan. 4, 2007).  aStreaming video (15 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Apr. 18, 2006.3 a(CIT): The DNA Repair Interest Group is sponsor.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aDNA-Directed DNA Polymerasexchemistry12aDNA-Directed DNA Polymerasexmetabolism22aProtein Interaction Mapping22aUbiquitinxmetabolism 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13294  aAUTH02343cgm a2200445 i 101763750DNLM20260227160143.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u200303s2020    mdu082|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:29004  a(OCoLC)1149800226  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aHF 5549.5.M500aLeading culture :bdiversity and inclusion in action /cDeEtta Jones.1 iSubtitle on PowerPoint:aLecture in honor of the retirement of Joyce Backus 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2020]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 22 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 12, 2020.3 a(CIT): Please join us on February 12 for a lecture and reception in honor of NLM Associate Director for Library Operations, Joyce Backus, who will be retiring on February 29, 2020 after over 34 years of extraordinary service here at NLM. Throughout her career, Joyce widely encouraged and supported diversity and inclusion in NLM's workforce. The lecture will feature special guest, DeEtta Jones, Principal and Founder, of DeEtta Jones and Associates (DJA). DeEtta has been a leading voice in shaping contemporary thinking and practice around integrated and sustainable approaches to workplace culture, diversity and inclusion. She also served for 10 years as Director of Diversity and then Director of the Office of Leadership and Management Services at the Association of Research Libraries.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed March 27, 2020).12aBackus, Joyce E. B.22aNational Library of Medicine (U.S.)12aCultural Diversity12aWorkplace22aAnniversaries and Special Events 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aJones, DeEtta,espeaker.2 aNational Library of Medicine (U.S.),ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?29004  aAUTH02077cas a2200505 i 101763536DNLM20260227090923.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||180907c20169999onc|| poo     0    0eng    a  2020243094  a2371-0888l2371-0888  a(OCoLC)1076694581  aLVTbengerdad20260227cLVTdOCLCQdDNLM0 aengafre  apcc  9Canada00aQR00aW110aJ Assoc Med Microbiol Infect Dis Can2dnlm00aJournal of the Association of Medical Microbiology and Infectious Disease Canada =bJournal officiel de l’Association pour la microbiologie médicale et l’infectiologie Canada.11aJournal officiel de l’Association pour la microbiologie médicale et l’infectiologie Canada1 aJAMMI 1a[Toronto, ON, Canada] :bUniversity of Toronto Press,c[2016]-  a1 online resource  a4 times a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, issue 1 (March/April 2016).0 aPubMedbv4n1, Mar. 2019- ; Selected citations only before this date0 aPMC  aArticles in English and French.  aOfficial publication of the Association of Medical Microbiology and Infectious Disease Canada.  aDescription based on: Vol. 1, issue 1 (March/April 2016); title from journal homepage (publisher's website, viewed April 9, 2020).  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 5, issue 1 (March 2020) (viewed April 9, 2020).12aCommunicable Diseasesxmicrobiology22aMicrobiological Phenomena 2aCanada 2aPeriodical2 aAssociation of Medical Microbiology and Infectious Disease Canada,eissuing body.40uhttps://jammi.utpjournals.press/40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101763536  aAUTH01530cgm a22004574a 10129483