btxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with: Volume 25, number 1 (January/March 2014).0 aPubMedbv25n1, 2014-0 aPMC  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: Volume 25, number 1 (January/March 2014); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 25, number 1 (January/March 2014).12aVirus Diseases22aVirology22aViruses 2aPeriodical2 aIndian Virological Society,eissuing body.0 x2347-351700tIndian journal of virologyx0970-2822w(DLC)sn 88026362w(OCoLC)142757504 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/133374 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101624144  aAUTH02242cgm a22004454a 101478250DNLM20260227152856.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080702s2008    mdu169 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14557  a(OCoLC)240988481  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWZ 10000aTribute to John William Daly :ba life dedicated to chemistry in nature /cNIDDK, Laboratory of Bioorganic Chemistry.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed July 23, 2008).  aStreaming video (2 hr., 48 min., 34 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 12, 2008.3 a(CIT): Colleagues, friends and family will celebrate the life and 50-year career of NIH Scientist Emeritus John W. Daly, Ph.D., who died March 5, 2008, in Rockville, MD, at the age of 74. He had pancreatic cancer. Daly was an international leader in chemical and pharmacological research, especially in the fields of drug metabolism, biologically active natural products, and adenosine receptors. Daly expanded the boundaries of chemistry and changed the course of research in pharmacology. He was a world authority on amphibian alkaloids and expert in many areas of natural products. The twenty-six classes of alkaloids he discovered have had a major impact on knowledge of how the nervous system functions and how drugs interact with the nervous system.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aDaly, John W.12aResearch Personnel22aHistory, 20th Century22aHistory, 21st Century22aPharmacologyxhistory 2aUnited States 2aBiography 2aWebcast2 aLaboratory of Bioorganic Chemistry (National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (U.S.))40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14557  aAUTH01352cas a22004454a 101088685DNLM20260227090916.0m        d        cr|cn ||||||||010221c20029999enkar pss     0    0eng    a  2002252920  a1472-684Xl1472-684X  a(OCoLC)49623185  aVAMcVAMdWAUdNLMdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9England10aW110aBMC Palliat Care2dnlm00aBMC palliative care.3 aBioMed Central palliative care30aPalliative care  aLondon :bBioMed Central,c[2002-  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1 (2002)-  aTitle from BioMedCentral archive screen (viewed Aug. 16, 2002).1 aMEDLINEbv14, 2015-0 aPubMedbv1, 2002-0 aPMC  aArticles are added consecutively to the current annual volume.  aElectronic journal (HTML, PDF)  aMode of access: Internet.12aPalliative Care22aHospice Care 2aPeriodical40uhttps://bmcpalliatcare.biomedcentral.com/40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101088685  aAUTH01342cas a2200421 a 101576204DNLM20260227090924.0cr||n|||||||||110420c19739999ii qr p       0    0eng    a  2011312448  a0974-5009l0974-5009  aI-D-E-2011-312448; 42  a(OCoLC)713546447  aDLCcDLCdDLCdDNLM  apcc  9India00aW1bJO954FV0 aJ. sci. soc. (Belgaum) 0aJournal of the scientific society (Belgaum)00aJournal of the scientific society.  aBelgaum [India] :bKLE University's J.N. Medical College,c[1973]-3 3<2012-> :aMumbai :bMedknow  av. :bill. ;c26-29 cm.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 a