 a(DNLM)CIT:15273  a(DNLM)CIT:15279  a(OCoLC)472719510  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 530.12 aConsortium of Universities for Global Health.bMeetingn(1st :d2009 :cNational Institutes of Health)10aConsortium of Universities for Global Health Meeting /cCUGH ; with NIAID and Fogarty.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed Oct. 30, 2009).  aStreaming video (11 hr., 31 min. : sd., col.).0 aDay 1 -- Day 2.  aRecorded Sept. 14 & 15, 2009.3 a(CIT): The Consortium of Universities for Global Health (CUGH) 2009 Annual Meeting will bring key stakeholders together to define and articulate the important role that universities should play in global health worldwide. The meeting is expected to draw over 250 invited participants, representing more than 50 North American university programs in global health and their partners from more than ten countries, along with representatives from NIH Fogarty Framework program, NGOs, foundations, and government. It is co-sponsored by CUGH, the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, and The Fogarty International Center.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGlobal Health22aInternational Cooperation22aUniversities 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1527340uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15279  aAUTH02703cgm a22004454a 101516501DNLM20260227153049.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u091002s2009    mdu284 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15297  a(OCoLC)470693977  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 3202 aNational Advisory Child Health and Human Development Council (U.S.).bMeetingn(139th :d2009 :cBethesda, Md.)10aNational Advisory Child Health and Human Development Council Meeting :bSeptember 21, 2009 /cEunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (NICHD).  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen (viewed Oct. 27, 2009).  aStreaming video (4 hr., 43 min., 14 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Sept. 21, 2009.3 a(CIT): The NICHD Advisory Council has two specific functions:  (1) to advise the NICHD on policy and procedures affecting the extramural research programs and (2) to provide the second level of review for grant applications requesting Institute funding support. The Council meets for one day three times a year in January, June, and September.The morning session is Open to the Public and is devoted to bringing Council members up-to-date with a Report of the Director, NICHD, a report by the Council Subcommittee on Planning and Policy, a review of one of the extramural program areas, discussion and review of proposed concepts for NICHD initiatives, the annual review of the Board of Scientific Counselors reports on intramural research programs, and new business items identified by the Council membership and Institute staff. The afternoon session is closed to the Public for the confidential Review of Applications.   For more information, visit  http://www.nichd.nih.gov/about/overview/advisory/NACHHD/agenda.cfm.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.22aNational Institute of Child Health and Human Development (U.S.)12aChild Welfare22aHuman Development22aResearch Support as Topicxorganization & administration22aResearchxorganization & administration22aUnited States Government Agencies 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15297  aAUTH01277cam a2200349 i 03920150RDNLM20260206220450.0cr||||||||||||810622s1926    nyu      b    000|0 eng    a   27001384   a(O