shington, D.C. :bPublished by the Helen Dwight Reid Educational Foundation, in cooperation with the American College Health Association,cc1982-3 32010- :aNew York :bRoutledge  av. :bill.  aEight no. a year,b2010/2011-  aBimonthly,b1982-2009/2010  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 30, no. 5 (Apr. 1982)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv30n5,Apr. 1982-0 aPubMedbv30n5,Apr. 1982-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  c19950523lNot printed on acid-free paper 2aStudent Health Services 2aPeriodical2 aAmerican College Health Association.2 aHelen Dwight Reid Educational Foundation.0 x1940-320800tJournal of the American College Health Associationx0164-4300w(DLC)   86641326w(OCoLC)10824214 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/vach20  aAUTH03406cgm a22004574a 101501622DNLM20260227152929.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090407s2009    mdu068 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:15002  a(OCoLC)359240086  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aBF 4481 aLee, Daeyeol.10aPrimate cortico-basal ganglia network and decision making /cDaeyeol Lee.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH neuroscience seminar series  aTitle from title screen (viewed May 11, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 7 min., 57 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 30, 2009.3 a(CIT): Decision making is ubiquitous, and the ability to develop the knowledge about the animal's environment from experience and use this knowledge to produce a series of actions that will maximize the overall reward is essential for survival. Dr. Lee's laboratory focuses on the role of the prefrontal cortex and the basal ganglia in evaluating the outcomes of the animal's previous choices and incorporating this information to improve the animal's decision-making strategies. His research is highly inter-disciplinary and capitalizes on the insights from formal theories of economics and reinforcement learning as well as computational neuroscience of neural coding and behavioral studies of decision making. His laboratory also develops novel behavioral paradigms that can probe the core processes of decision making. Combined with the use of a large-scale multi-electrode recording system, this research seeks to unravel the biological basis of willful actions.  Selected Publications:     Behavioral and neural changes after gains and losses of conditioned reinforcers. Seo H, Lee D., J Neurosci. 2009 Mar 18;29(11):3627-41.  Neural dissociation of delay and uncertainty in intertemporal choice. Luhmann CC, Chun MM, Yi DJ, Lee D, Wang XJ., J Neurosci. 2008 Dec 31;28(53):14459-66.  Prefrontal coding of temporally discounted values during intertemporal choice. Kim S, Hwang J, Lee D., Neuron. 2008 Jul 10;59(1):161-72. Erratum in: Neuron. 2008 Aug 14;59(3):522.   Game theory and neural basis of social decision making. Lee D., Nat Neurosci. 2008 Apr;11(4):404-9. Epub 2008 Mar 26. Review.  Order-dependent modulation of directional signals in the supplementary and presupplementary motor areas. Sohn JW, Lee D., J Neurosci. 2007 Dec 12;27(50):13655-66.  To touch or not to touch: posterior parietal cortex and voluntary behavior. Lee D., Neuron. 2007 Nov 8;56(3):419-21.  For more information see our website -  NIH Neuroscience Seminar Series.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aDecision Makingxphysiology22aBasal Gangliaxphysiology22aPrefrontal Cortexxphysiology22aPrimatesxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH neuroscience seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15002  aAUTH01785cam a2200397 i 29210750RDNLM20260206221157.0cr||||||||||||hd|bfa012baap810815s1921    cou      l    001 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14790705  aDNLMbengerdad20260206dDNLM  9United States00aWA 32 AC6bC718p 19211 aColorado.bState Board of Health,ecompiler,eissuing body.14aThe public health law :bcontaining also the sanitary code, the provisions in other general laws relating to public health, opinions rendered on water pollution, birth registration, etc., and rules and regulations of the Colorado State Board of Health. 1aDenver, Colorado :bColorado State Board of Health,c1921.  a262 pages :billustrations ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes index.  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 4182  no. 55DNLM  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d1998.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20250627lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM1 adigitizedc20262pda5DNLM12aColorado.bState Board of Health12aPublic Healthxlegislation & jurisprudence22aPublic Health Practicexlegislation & jurisprudence22aConstitution and Bylaws 2aColorado 2aLegislation4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/29210750R  aAUTH02499cgm a2200445 i 101628115DNLM20260227154651.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u140312s2014    mdu050       fo   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:18295  a(OCoLC)883365648  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWA 530.11 aFrenk, Julio,eauthor.10aHealth without boundaries :brethinking global and domestic health /cJulio Frenk. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2014]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (50 min.) :bcolor, sound)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aSecretary's global health lecture series  aTitle from title screen.  aAccess restricted to HHS only.5DNLM  aRecorded Feb. 24, 2014.3 a(CIT): The Secretary"s Global Health Lecture Series  Please join Secretary Sebelius for the Secretary"s Global Health and Human Services Lecture Series. Dr. Julio Frenk will speak about the growing intersection of domestic and global health.  Since 2009, Dr. Frenk has served as the Dean of the Faculty at the Harvard School of Public Health.  As the Minister of Health of Mexico, Dr. Frenk introduced a program of comprehensive national health insurance, expanding access to health care for tens of millions of previously uninsured Mexicans. He was the founding director-general of the National Institute of Public Health in Mexico and in 1998, Dr. Frenk joined the World Health Organization as executive director in charge of Evidence and Information for Policy, WHO"s first-ever unit explicitly charged with developing a scientific foundation for health policy to achieve better outcomes.  Dr. Frenk has also written two best-selling novels for youngsters explaining the functions of the human body.  aClose-captioned.  aDescription based on version viewed June 26, 2014.12aGlobal Health22aInternationality 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aSecretary's global health and human services lecture40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18295  aAUTH02089cgm a22003974a 101501601DNLM20260227153338.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090407s2009    mdu118 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14971  a(OCoLC)370602134  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 540 AA12 aWhite House Regional Forum on Health Reformd(2009 :cUniversity of Vermont)10aWhite House Regional Forum on Health Reform, March 17, 2009.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2009]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed May 20, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 58 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 17, 2009, University of Vermont.3 a(CIT): Building on the forum held at the White House on March 5, Burlington, Vermont will host the second in a series of Regional White House Forums on Health Reform on Tuesday, March 17 at 1:00 pm EDT.  In keeping with the Obama administration's commitment to a transparent, accountable government, the forum will bring together a diverse group of people with a stake in reforming our health care system to voice their concerns and ideas.  Forum participants will include doctors, patients, providers, insurers, policy experts and health care advocates of all kinds - both Democrats and Republicans - who will discuss the urgent need to curb skyrocketing health care costs that are draining our federal budget, devastating families and small businesses and undermining our long-term economic prosperity.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aHealth Care Reform 2aUnited States 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14971  aAUTH01530cas a2200493 a 8703571DNLM20260227091013.0cr|cn#||||||||870326c19879999gw  x p       0    0eng    a0932-0113l0932-0113y0044-3255  aPARREZ  a(DNLM)SR0058221(s)  a(OCoLC)15110644  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Germany00aW1bPA64EF10aParasitol Res2dnlm 0aParasitology researchb(1987)00aParasitology research.  aBerlin :bSpringer International,cc1987-  av. :bill.  a18 no. a year,b2003-  aEight no. a year,b-1997  a10 no. a year,b1997-1998  a12 no. a year,b1999-2002  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 73, no. 1 (Jan. 1987)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv79n3, 1993-1 aPubMedbv79n3, 1993-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aOrgan of: Deutsche Gesellschaft für Parasitologie.  3(1988)c19890818fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aParasitology 2aPeriodical2 aDeutsche Gesellschaft für Parasitologie.0 x1432-195500tZeitschrift für Parasitenkunde (Berlin, G