al moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded January 12, 2021.3 a(CIT): Dr. Fauci will discuss the status of the COVID-19 pandemic; Dr. Taubenberger will discuss the status of the emerging influenza season, as well as the 1918-1919 flu.  While COVID-19 vaccines are now being distributed, the worse of the pandemic in terms of death and illness is still ahead of us.  Where do we stand with diagnostics and treatments?  What challenges require more research?  And the flu  remember the flu?  That"s still a serious concern, too.  What can we expect from this influenza season?  How close are we to a universal flu vaccine?  These and other questions will be discussed.  CME credits will be available.  These complementary lectures mark the beginning of the 20th year of the Demystifying Medicine course.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed March 10, 2021).12aCOVID-1922aInfluenza, Human22aInfluenza Pandemic, 1918-191922aEpidemicsxhistory 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aFauci, Anthony S.,d1940-espeaker.1 aTaubenberger, Jeffery,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=41281  aAUTH02251cgm a2200457 i 9918418881606676DNLM20260227162356.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220616s2022    mdu062|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32383  a(OCoLC)1350874921  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWA 300 AA100aVivek Murthy lecture for public health leadership /cVivek Murthy, Michelle Wu. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 2 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aDr. Vivek H. Murthy distinguished lecture series on public health leadership  aRecorded May 11, 2022.3 a(CIT): In celebration of Asian American and Native Hawaiian/Pacific Islanders (AA and NHPI) Heritage Month, join us for the Dr. Vivek H. Murthy Distinguished Lecture Series on Public Health Leadership. This is the second in a series of fireside chats in honor of Dr. Murthy, the 19th and 21st Surgeon General of the United States. The goal of the series is to recognize a public health leader whose enduring efforts have made a significant impact on advancing public health. At this upcoming event, Dr. Murthy will recognize Michelle Wu, Mayor of Boston, for her leadership in addressing racism and mental health stigma impacting AA and NHPI communities.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed November 16, 2022).12aPublic Health12aAsian.22aNative Hawaiian or Pacific Islander.22aMental Disorders22aHealth Status Disparities22aLeadership 2aWebcast1 aMurthy, Vivek Hallegere,d1977-espeaker.1 aWu, Michelle,d1985-espeaker. 0aVivek Murthy distinguished lecture40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45154  aAUTH01561cas a2200481 i 101626355DNLM20260227090914.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||131030c20139999enk|| poo     0    0eng    a  2013254585  a2194-7899l2194-7899  a(OCoLC)861751435  aCUVbengerdad20260227cCUVdDNLM  apcc  9England00aW110aHealth Justice2dnlm00aHealth Justice00aHealth & justice.3 aHealth and justice 1aHeidelberg, Germany :bSpringer-Verlag, GmbH,c[2013]-[2017]313[2018]- :a[London, United Kingdom] :bBioMed Central  a1 online resource  aTen issues per year,b2015-  aThree issues per year,b2013  aSix issues per year,b2014  atext2rdacontent  acomputer2rdamedia  aonline resource2rdacarrier1 aBegan with 1:1 (24 October 2013).0 aPubMedbv1, Dec. 2013-0 aPMC  aDescription based on: 1:1 (24 October 2013); title from journal homepage (SpringerOpen website, viewed Oct. 30, 2013).  aLatest issue consulted: (2015) 3:19 (vi