e is open to the entire NIH community as well as to those from outside NIH, and is also available through Videocast. The recommended textbook is Ethical and Regulatory Aspects of Clinical Research, edited by Emanuel et al (Johns Hopkins University Press). The course is taught by guest faculty and faculty members from the National Institutes of Health.  aDescription based on version viewed January 3, 2013.12aControlled Clinical Trials as Topicxethics22aPlacebos22aRandomized Controlled Trials as Topicxethics22aTherapeutic Equipoise 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bClinical Center.bDepartment of Bioethics,eissing body.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?18139  aAUTH01356cgm a22004334a 101289595DNLM20260227151416.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061011s2006    mdu067 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13028  a(OCoLC)84671844  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 3591 aSvendsen, Clive.10aCombining stem cell and gene therapy for neurological disorders /cClive Svendsen.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Nov. 3, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 6 min., 17 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jan. 30, 2006.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aParkinson Disease22aAmyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis22aGenetic Therapy22aGrowth Substances22aStem Cells 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13028  aAUTH01412cgm a22004094a 101268671DNLM20260227151138.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2003    mdu031 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:12413  a(OCoLC)147440896  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 45000aNational DNA Day 2003 :bDNA--the next generation /cNational Human Genome Research Ins