bv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aThe NIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture  aSpeaker, Kathryn V. Holmes.  aPresented Sept. 10, 2003.  aThe spike glycoprotein (S) of coronaviruses is a very large type 1 viral fusion protein that recognizes receptors on host cells and mediates membrane fusion and virus entry. The interactions of human and animal coronaviruses with their receptors are used as examples to consider how the SARS coronavirus may have emerged from an animal reservoir.  aAlso available online.  aVHS.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.5DNLM  aClosed-captioned.12aCoronaviridae22aReceptors, Virus.22aViral Fusion Proteins1 aHolmes, Kathryn V.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMedical Arts and Photography Branch. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series4 uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=2510  aAUTH01577cas a2200529 a 9423872DNLM20260227091020.0cr|cn#||||||||940331c19949999enkbr p       0    0eng    asn 93005650   a1071-5762l1029-2470  aFRARER  a(DNLM)SR0078899(s)  a(OCoLC)28679237  aNSDPcNSDPdDNLM  ansdp  9England00aW1bFR598410aFree Radic Res2dnlm 0aFree radical research00aFree radical research.  aYverdon, Switzerland :bHarwood Academic ;aNew York, NY :bdistributed by STBS Ltd.,cc1994-3 aLondon :bInforma Healthcare  av.bill.  aBimonthly,b2004-  aMonthly  aFour no. a year,b-2003  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 20, no. 1-  aTitle from cover.  aImprint varies.  aPrint issues ceased with v. 47, no. 12 (2013).1 aMEDLINEbv20n1,Jan. 1994-1 aPubMedbv20n1,Jan. 1994-1 aIndex medicus  aSix issues per volume.  aAlso issued online. 2aAntioxidants 2aFree Radicals 2aPeriodical0 x1029-247000tFree radical research communicationsx8755-0199w(DLC)   91655049w(OCoLC)112419774 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ifra20  aAUTH