 cross-disciplinary series, featuring both NHLBI staff and researchers throughout the scientific community, will enhance NHLBI listeners" understanding of the latest advances in this fast-moving research, especially as they relate to the NHLBI mission. For more information go to https://intranet.nhlbi.nih.gov/content/covid-19-insights-webinar-series.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 19, 2021).12aCOVID-1922aModels, Animal 2aWebcast 2aLecture1 aRowe, Steven,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNHLBI COVID-19 insights webinar series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=38872  aAUTH01861cas a2200505 a 101576715DNLM20260227090907.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||120110c20119999ne uu poo     0    0eng    a  2012250574  a2211-3207l2211-3207  a(OCoLC)772250336  aOH1bengcOH1dBUFdOCLCQdOCLCFdDNLM  apcc  9Netherlands 4aRC119b.I584710aW110aInt J Parasitol Drugs Drug Resist2dnlm00aInternational journal for parasitology.pDrugs and drug resistance.1 aDrugs and drug resistance1 aIJP-DDR  a[Amsterdam] :bElsevier,c2011-  a3 issues a year,b2014-  aAnnual,b2011-2013  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with vol. 1, issue 1 (Dec. 2011).1 aMEDLINEbv5n1, Apr. 2015--0 aPubMedbv1, Dec. 2011-0 aPMC  aSponsored by the Australian Society for Parasitology.  aPartner journal to the International journal for parasitology (IJP).  aDescription based on: Vol. 1, issue 1 (Dec. 2011); title from available issues screen (ScienceDirect, viewed Feb. 14, 2012).  aLatest issue consulted: 4 (2014) (viewed Jan. 22, 2014).12aParasitic Diseasesxdrug therapy22aDrug Resistance 2aPeriodical2 aAustralian Society for Parasitology.0 tInternational journal for parasitologyx0020-7519w(DLC)   2003233447w(OCoLC)017710444 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/jour