ity for scientists from the Center for Cancer Research, from other NCI divisions, and other NIH institutes, as well as from the extramural community (academia and the biotech industry), to gather and exchange information about the latest developments in research pertaining to the role of inflammation in the development and treatment of cancer.  This conference has been held every three years and has become one of the premier meetings in this field.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed Nov. 17, 2016).12aNeoplasmsxetiology22aImmunotherapy22aInflammationxcomplications22aInflammationxprevention & control22aNeoplasmsxprevention & control22aNeoplasmsxtherapy22aPhagocytesximmunology 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aCenter for Cancer Research (National Cancer Institute (U.S.)),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1990040uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19906  aAUTH01810cgm a2200469 i 101696077DNLM20260227155500.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u161102s2016    mdu060|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19938  a(OCoLC)971543728  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 2100aLeadership development in a neurosurgical residency /cKarin Muraszko.1 iTitle on PowerPoint:aChallenges of leadership development and mentoring in the age of restricted work hours 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 0 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds : contemporary clinical medicine : great teachers  aRecorded October 19, 2016.3 a(CIT): Contemporary Clinical Medicine: Great Teachers: Leadership Development in a Neurosurgical Residency.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (vi