formatics specialists to capitalize on the availability of human gene sequences and emerging techniques for the analyses of complex mixtures of proteins.  Symposium speakers will present varying perspectives on their proteome-based research from clinical medicine to bioinformatics via application of emerging technologies in protein chips, electrophoresis and mass spectrometry.   For more information, visit the  Proteomics Symposium Web Site.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aProteome 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bMass Spectrometry Interest Group40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10124  aAUTH03152cas a2200661   0253357DNLM20260227091040.0cr|cn#||||||||hd|bfa012baap700812c19449999vaumr p       0    0eng    amed47001541   a0022-3085l0022-3085  aJONSAC  a(OCoLC)01800316  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bJO795E10aJ Neurosurg2dnlm00aJournal of neurosurgery.3 aJournal of neurosurgery.pPediatricsf2004-20073 aJournal of neurosurgery.pSpinef1999-May 2004  aChicago [etc.]3 aCharlottesville, VA :bAmerican Association of Neurological Surgeons  av.billus., ports.  aMonthly,b2004-  aSixteen no. a year,b-2001  aEighteen no. a year,b2002-2003  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       Jan. 1944-  aPlace of publication varies.1 aMEDLINEbv23n1,July 1965-1 aPubMedbv23n1,July 1965-0 aOLDMEDLINE1 aAbridged index medicus1 aIndex medicus  aIssues for Feb.-May 2004 share pagination and are numbered in conjunction with issues of the journal's other supplement: Journal of neurosurgery. Spine.  aSuppl. to Vol. 90, no. 4 (Apr. 1999) misnumbered on inside of cover and contents p. as v. 90, no. 2.  aSupplements accompany some vols.  aSome vols. have supplement with title: Journal of 