ournals/?term=101687144  aAUTH02532cgm a2200565 i 9918592676406676DNLM20260227163410.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230429s2023    mdu999|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:33017  a(DNLM)CIT:33018  a(DNLM)CIT:33019  a(DNLM)CIT:33020  a(OCoLC)1457225357  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 2100aIntroduction to the principles and practice of clinical research :bNIH peer review process (parts 1-4) /cJasenka Borzan, Nicholas Gaiano, Serena Chu.1 aNIH peer review process (parts 1-4)1 aNational Institutes of Health peer review process (parts 1-4) 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2023]  a1 online resource (4 streaming video files (70 hrs., 4 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 1, 2023.3 a(CIT): The Introduction to the Principles and Practice of Clinical Research (IPPCR) is a course to train participants on how to effectively conduct clinical research. The course focuses on the spectrum of clinical research and the research process by highlighting epidemiologic methods, study design, protocol preparation, patient monitoring, quality assurance, and Food and Drug Administration (FDA) issues.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PowerPoint screen (viewed August 13, 2024).22aCenter for Scientific Review (National Institutes of Health)12aPeer Review, Researchxmethods12aBiomedical Researchxmethods22aEpidemiologic Research Design22aAcademies and Institutes22aResearch Support as Topic 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aBorzan, Jasenka,espeaker.1 aGaiano, Nicholas,espeaker.1 aChu, Serena,d1973-espeaker.2 aNational Institute of Mental Health (U.S.),eissuing body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4936240uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4936340uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4936440uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/