2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1 (2010).0 aPubMedbv11, 2020-0 aPMC  aArticles published as they become available and compiled into annual issues.  aArticles in English and Japanese; summaries in English and Japanese. Search interface available in English and Japanese.0 aVol. 1 (2010); title from PDF article header (publisher's website, viewed June 26, 2023).1 aVol. 14 (2023) (viewed June 26, 2023).12aRehabilitation12aPhysical Therapy Modalities 2aPeriodical2 aZenkoku Kaifukuki Rihabiritēshon Byōtō Renraku Kyōgikai,eissuing body.2 aKaifukuki Rihabiritēshon Byōtō Kyōkai,eissuing body.40uhttp://www.rehabili.jp/jjcrs/index%5Fe.html40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=9918556585006676  aAUTH02688nam a2200421 i 9918986608306676DNLM20260225080448.0210603t20222022fluac    b    001 0 eng    aGBC1A48942bnb  a9780367543129q(hbk.)  a0367543125  z9781000431490 (ePub ebook)  z9781000431476 (PDF ebook)  z9781003199373 (ebook)  a(OCoLC)1259549984  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCOdOCLCFdEEMdOCLCO  apcc  9United States 4aSF809.T6bD83 202200aWC 72504a636.08969362231 aDubey, J. P.,eauthor.10aToxoplasmosis of animals and man10aToxoplasmosis of animals and humans /cJ.P. Dubey.  aThird edition. 1aBoca Raton :bCRC Press,c2022. 4c©2022  axxi, 542 pages :billustrations (black and white, and colour), portrait ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"This is the only book to cover toxoplasmosis of animals and humans thoroughly in one single source. Found worldwide from Alaska to Australasia, Toxoplasma gondii is the cause of one of the most common parasitic infections in humans, livestock, companion animals, and wildlife, and is included on the list of potential bioterrorism microbes. Furthermore, T. gondii has been and continues to be used extensively as a model for the cell biology of apicomplexan parasites. In the decade since the second edition of this book was published, there has been an explosion of knowledge concerning the parasite Toxoplasma gondii and toxoplasmosis. This update provides unique information on all known host types for this parasite, with an additional chapter on history, substantial updates throughout, and a detailed focus on the biology of the parasite in Chapter 2. The third edition is compiled by author JP Dubey, an authority on T. gondii who has worked with virtually all hosts of the protozoan during the last 55 years, including humans, all livestock species, wildlife, and zoo animals. The book distills the voluminous and potentially confusing scientific literature, that has grown geometrically in the 30+ years since the publication of the first edition, into a comprehensive resource for all professionals, graduate students and researchers working in this field." --Publisher's description.12aToxoplasmosis22aToxoplasmosis, Animal22aToxoplasmaxparasitology  aAUTH01570cgm a22004574a 101322959DNLM20260227152216.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u071207s2007    mdu103 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14142  a(OCoLC)190751395  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWG 5001 aRoberts, David D.q(David Duncan),d1954-10aAngiogenesis and carcinogenesis /cRoberts and Yeh ; sponsored by the National Cancer Institute.1 iTitle on screen banner:aRedox biology.pAngiogenesis and carcinogenesis  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aRedox biology seminar series  aTitle from title screen (viewed Dec. 27, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 42 min., 45 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 13, 2007.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeovascularization, Pathologic22aAngiogenesis Inhibitors22aCell Transformation, Neoplastic22aOx