ICHD, this year's series offers advances that span the areas of molecular, cellular and organismal neuroscience.    For more information, visit the  NIH Neuroscience Seminar Series.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.12aHippocampus22aNeural Inhibition22aReceptor, Cannabinoid, CB122aSynaptic Transmission 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10864  aAUTH01867cgm a2200397 a 101578528DNLM20260227154059.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120215s2012    mdu077|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17097  a(OCoLC)783988622  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWM 475.71 aDrayna, Dennis.10aDemystifying medicine.pStuttering :ba medical disease? /cDennis Drayna, Penny Friedman, Donna Krasnewhich.1 aStuttering  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 17 min.) :bsd., col.)  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded Feb. 7, 2012.3 a(CIT): The course includes presentation of patients, pathology, diagnosis and therapy in the context of major disease problems and current research.  Primarily directed toward Ph.D. students, fellows, and staff, it is also of interest to medical students and clinicians.  The course is designed to help bridge the gap between advances in biology and their application to major human diseases.  Each session includes clinical and basic science components which are presented by NIH staff and outside invitees.For more information go to <a href='http://demystifyingmedicine.od.nih.gov/'>http://demystifyingmedicine.od.nih.gov/.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aStutteringxgenetics 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)