aPeriodical2 aMedico-Legal Society (Great Britain)0 x2042-183415tMedico-legal and criminological reviewx0302-1637w(DLC)   2001207907w(OCoLC)17149194 uhttps://journals.sagepub.com/home/mlj  aAUTH01259cas a2200433   0267442DNLM20260224111547.0cr|cn#||||||||701214c19709999sz br p       0    0eng    a0030-3747l0030-3747  aOPRSAQ  a(DNLM)O07840000(s)  a(OCoLC)01761331  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Switzerland00aW1bOP238P10aOphthalmic Res2dnlm00aOphthalmic research.30aJournal for research in experimental and clinical ophthalmology  aBasel, New York,bKarger.  av.billus.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       1970-  aPrint issues ceased with 2020.1 aMEDLINEbv14n1, 1982-1 aPubMedbv14n1, 1982-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso available online.  3Vol. 12, no. 1 (1980)c19920901fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aOphthalmology 2aResearch 2aPeriodical0 x1423-02594 uhttp://www.karger.com/Journal/Home/223858  aAUTH02528cgm a2200481 i 101676582DNLM20260227155258.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u160201s2016    mdu053|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19428  a(OCoLC)945025554  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 103.500aCultural neuroscience :bclosing the gap in population mental health disparities /cJoan Chiao.1 iSubtitle on PowerPoint:aClosing the gap in global mental health disparities 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2016]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (53 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBehavioral and social sciences research lecture series  aRecorded January 8, 2016.3 a(CIT): Behavioral and Social Sciences Research Lecture Series.  Mental health disorders pose a significant global financial burden in treatment annually.  A key challenge facing global mental health is to understand the etiology and treatment of mental health disparities, including the mechanisms of population disparities in mental health. Cultural neuroscience is a research field that examines the cultural, environmental and genetic factors that shape psychological and neural processes underlying behavior.  Recent advances in cultural neuroscience demonstrate the relevance of culture in modulating brain and behavior. This talk will provide an overview of advances in cultural neuroscience, with discussion of the implications of this research for closing the gap in population mental health disparities.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed March 16, 2016).12aMental Disordersxethnology12aNeuropsychology22aBrainxphysiology22aCultural Characteristics22aHealth Status Disparities22aMental Disordersxetiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aChiao, Joan Y.,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aBSSR lecture series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19428  aAUTH01141cam a2200301 i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032035002000073040003500093044001400128060003200142100003200174245006500206264007700271300003900348336002600387337002800413338002700441500004800468540013800516583003900654583007200693650001600765650001700781650003200798999000900830101187280DNLM20260224085826.0030805s1906    ag a          000 0 spa    a(OCoLC)52895715  aDNLMbengerdad20260219dDNLM  9Argentina00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 395 no.151 aFeinmann, Enrique,eauthor.10aOfidismo y seroterapia antivenenosa /cpor Enrique Feinmann. 1aBuenos Aires :bLa Semana Médica, Imp. de Obras de E. Spinelli,c1906.  a40 pages :billustrations ;c22 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"(De la Semana Médica, núm, 33, 1906)."  aNational Library of Medicine believes this item to be in 