ches. This workshop will focus on the development and use of animal models to understand the pathology, transmission, and immune responses to respiratory virus infection, with an emphasis on influenza and SARS-CoV-2.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed February 14, 2025).12aRespiratory Tract Infections12aVirus Diseases22aDisease Models, Animal22aAnimals, Laboratory 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aArnold, MIchelle,espeaker.2 aNational Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (U.S.),esponsoring body,ehost institution.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=5496540uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=54966  aAUTH01541cas a2200505 a 9815705DNLM20260227091038.0cr|cn#||||||||981016c19969999enk x p       0    0eng    asn 99039880   a1359-6535l1359-6535  zANTHF  a(DNLM)SR0091683(s)  a(OCoLC)42889502  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9England00aW1bAN869W10aAntivir Ther2dnlm00aAntiviral therapy.  aLondon :bInternational Medical Press31a[London] :bSAGE Publications  av. :bill.  aEight no. a year,b2005-  aFrequency varies,b1996-2004  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with v. 1 in 1996.  aDescription based on: Vol. 3, no. 4 (1998); title from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1,1996-1 aPubMedbv1n1,1996-1 aIndex medicus  aSupplements accompany some v.  aAlso issued online.  aOfficial publication of the International Society for Antiviral Research.12aAntiviral Agentsxtherapeutic use22aVirus Diseasesxtherapy22aVirusesxdrug effects 2aPeriodical2 aInternational Society for Antiviral Research.0 x2040-20584 uhttps://journals.sagepub.com/home/avt  aAUTH01326cas a2200445   0376442DNLM20260227090915.0cr|cn ||||||||731128c19589999paubr         0    0eng    asc 82001125 zsn 78005015  a0033-0620l0033-0620  aPCVDAN  a(DNLM)P47320000(s)  a(OCoLC)01624043  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  