times. It analyses the theories, practice, and research in health psychology from both Indian and western perspective. The volume brings together knowledge diversified across various narrow sub-fields. It expounds upon physiological psychology; chronic illnesses associated with physiological systems; and biopsychosocial approaches to treatment and management with therapeutic interventions integrated throughout the book. It further discusses health promotive and health risk behaviour with reference to health policies and data base at national and global levels. This book will be beneficial to the students, researchers, and teachers of psychology, applied psychology, public health, public policy, community health, medical and paramedical studies. It will also be indispensable to the policy makers and NGOs working in the field of public health"--cProvided by publisher.12aHealth Behavior22aBehavioral Medicinexmethods22aStress, Psychological22aResilience, Psychological  aAUTH01599cgm a2200469 a 101549178DNLM20260227153634.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u101208s2010    mdu079|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16167  a(OCoLC)698580017  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQZ 2661 aBarnes, Stephen.10aSoy and cancer :bwish you were young again /cStephen Barnes.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2010]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aStars in nutrition and cancer  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (1 hr., 19 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 4, 2010.3 a(CIT): This lecture will provide fundamental insights into the pleiotropic role of soy in modifying multiple processes associated with cancer risk and tumor behavior.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxdiet therapy22aIsoflavonesxpharmacology22aNutritive Value22aPrecancerous Conditionsxdiet therapy22aSoy Foods 2