erbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from title screen.  aStreaming video (1 hr., 6 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded May 12, 2010.3 a(CIT): The NCI's Office of Cancer Complementary and Alternative Medicine (OCCAM) invites you to view its monthly lecture series.  With the goal of informing the National Cancer Institute (NCI) community about the variety of ongoing research in cancer and complementary and alternative medicine (CAM), NCI's Office of Cancer Complementary and Alternative Medicine (OCCAM) has created a monthly lecture series on cancer CAM. These hour long lectures, occurring from 10 a.m. - 11 a.m. on the second Wednesday of each month, will feature a fifty minute presentation on a cancer CAM topic and allow ten minutes for questions.   For more information, visit  http://www.cancer.gov/cam/news_lectures.html.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aMultiple Myelomaxdrug therapy22aAntineoplastic Agentsxpharmacology22aAntineoplastic Agentsxtherapeutic use22aCurcuminxpharmacology22aCurcuminxtherapeutic use 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.).bOffice of Cancer Complementary and Alternative Medicine.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15894  aAUTH01683cas a2200493 a 101167473DNLM20260227090908.0cr|cn ||||||||030122c20029999ne  x p       0   a0eng    a  2003243084  a1567-133Xl1567-133X  a(OCoLC)51501349  aMDUcMDUdDNLM  alcdanlmcopyc  9Netherlands00aW1bBR116J10aGene Expr Patterns2dnlm00aGene expression patterns :bGEP.30aGEP  aAmsterdam ;aNew York :bElsevier,cc2002-  av. :bill. ;c28 cm.  aSix no. a year,b2003-  aQuarterly,b-2002  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 2, issues 1-2 (Nov. 2002)-  a"A section of Mechanisms of development."  aLast issue consulted: Vol. 2, issues 3-4 (Dec. 2002).1 aMEDLINEbv2n1/2, Nov. 2002-1 aPubMedbv2n1/2, Nov. 2002-1 aIndex medicu