d20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQU 5600aChromatin proteomics as new perspective to investigate the biology of exceptional longevity /cSimone Sidoli. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (59 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH protIG seminar  aRecorded December 12, 2024.3 a(CIT): Chromatin state and dynamics is modulated by chromatin interacting proteins, in particular histones and their post-translational modifications. We investigate the chromatin-bound proteome in aging to understand how DNA readout is misregulated. We focus on domains of reactivated heterochromatin, i.e. chromatin domains undergoing anomalous decondensation and decorated by histones co-modified with markers of condensed heterochromatin and active transcription. We optimize our mass spectrometry methods to investigate multiple dimensions of the chromatin proteome, including (i) its interactions with DNA and transcription factors, (ii) its post-translational modifications, and (iii) its cell-to-cell heterogeneity using single cell histone analysis.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed January 27, 2026).12aChromatinxmetabolism22aHistonesxmetabolism22aHistone Code22aChromatin Assembly and Disassembly22aProtein Processing, Post-Translational22aAgingxmetabolism22aProteomicsxmethods 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aSidoli, Simone,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bProteomics Interest Group,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNIH Proteomics Interest Group lecture40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=55457  aAUTH01790cgm a2200457 i 9918879456806676DNLM20260227164716.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u240802s2024    mdu125|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:34086  a(OCoLC)1482112828  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWB 5502 aArts for Health's Sake Workshopd(2024 :cOnline)jauthor.10aArts for health's sake /cKeith Mintzer. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (2 hr., 5 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 11, 2024.3 a(CIT): Arts for Health's Sake Workshop, held June 11, 2024, which is focused on supporting translational research into using arts therapy for the treatment of heart, lung, and blood diseases.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed December 4, 2024).12aArt Therapy22aTranslational Research, Biomedical22aResearch Support as Topic22aCardiovascular Diseasesxtherapy22aLung Diseasesxtherapy22aHematologic Diseasesxtherapy 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast1 aMintzer, Keith,espeaker,emoderator.2 aNational Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute,eorganizer,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=54855  aAUTH01447cgm a22004694a 101294464DNLM20260227151801.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061204s2006    mdu065|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13396  a(OCoLC)185042526  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aHQ 766.31 aBayley, Carol.10aContraception, Catholicism, and cancer research /cCarol Bayley.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Clinical Center grand rounds  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Dec. 14, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 5 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Oct. 4, 2006.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aContraceptionxethics22aBioethical Issues22aCatholicism22aNeoplasms