a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2001]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 16, 2008).  aStreaming video (18 hr., 31 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 26-28, 2001.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government. No copyright exists on this material. It may be disseminated freely.  aOpen-captioned.12aDental Cariesxdiagnosis12aDental Cariesxtherapy22aDental Cariesxetiology22aPrimary Prevention 2aConsensus Development Conference, NIH 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?995940uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?996040uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?9961  aAUTH01922cgm a22004454a 101493093DNLM20260227153026.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u090106s2008    mdu063 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14833  a(OCoLC)316419739  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 7051 aGelperin, Alan.12aA role for nitric oxide in olfactory information processing in the mouse /cAlan Gelperin.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2008]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH neuroscience seminar series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Feb. 27, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 2 min., 6 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 15, 2008.3 a(CIT): Nitric oxide is an important interneuronal signaling molecule that appears prominently in the olfactory systems of many species. Its synthetic enzyme neuronal nitric oxide synthase is concentrated within particular interneurons of the olfactory bulb, as are enzymes activated by nitric oxide that alter neuronal excitability. Using innovative new techniques, Dr. Gelperin's laboratory explores many aspects of information processing by the olfactory system, including roles of nitric oxide.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aOlfactory Perception22aNitric Oxidexphysiology22aOlfactory Bulbxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH neuroscience seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14833  aAUTH01539cgm a22004094a 101267526DNLM20260227145202.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s1999    mdu064 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:10172  a(OCoLC)276652260  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWD 1101 aSommer, Alfred,d1942-10aEpidemiology in the cause of vitamin A :bscience to practice /cAlfred Sommer.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c1999]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series. Robert S. Gordon, Jr. lecture  aTitle from screen banner (viewed June 25, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 4 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Jan. 27, 1999.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aCopyright: This is a work of the United States Government.  No copyright exists on this material.  It may be disseminated freely.12aVitamin A Deficiencyxepidemiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pRobert S. Gordon, Jr. lecture40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?10172  aAUTH04219nam a2200481 i 9918986583306676DNLM20260225070356.0200214t20212021nyua     b    001 0 eng    aGBC1986022bnb  a1259539031  a9781260143430q(paperback)  a1260143430q(paperback)  a(OCoLC)1140407125z(OCoLC)1259539031  aYDXbengerdacYDXdOCLCQdSMVdOCLCOdNTUdOCLCOdGRUdOCLCOdYDXdOCLCQdUKMGBdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCL  apcc  an-us---  9United States 4aRC963b.C87 202100aWA 44004a616.98032230 aCurrent occupational & environmental medicine10aCurrent diagnosis & treatment :boccupational & environmental medicine /ceditors, Joseph LaDou, Robert J. Harrison.1 aCurrent diagnosis and treatment :boccupational and environmental medicine  aSixth edition. 1aNew York :bMcGraw-Hill,c[2021] 4c©2021  axiv, 940 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aPreceded by Current occupational & environmental medicine. 5th edition. 2014.  a"A Lange medical book."  aIncludes bibliographical references and index0 aSection I: Occupational health practice. The practice of occupational medicine -- The occupational & environmental medical history -- Workers' compensation -- Ethics in occupational medicine -- Disability management & prevention -- Section II: Occupational injuries. Ergonomics & the prevention of occupational injuries -- Musculoskeletal injuries -- Shoulder, elbow, & hand injuries -- Back & lower extremity injuries -- The management of chronic pain -- Eye injuries -- Hearing loss -- Injuries caused by physical hazards -- Section III: Occupational illnesses. Medical toxicology -- Clinical immunology -- Occupational infections -- Occupational skin disorders -- Upper respiratory tract disorders -- Occupational lung diseases -- Cardiovascular toxicology -- Liver toxicology -- Renal toxicology -- Neurotoxicology -- Occupational hematology -- Occupational cancer -- Genetic toxicology -- Female reproductive toxicology -- Male reproductive toxicology -- Section IV: Occupational and environmental exposures. Metals -- Chemicals -- Solvents -- Gases & other airborne toxicants -- Pesticides -- Section V: Program management. The changing nature of work -- Total worker health -- Occupational mental health & substance use disorders -- Fatigue, shiftwork, & sleep disorders -- Workplace violence prevention -- Occupational safety -- Industrial (occupational) hygiene -- Disease surveillance -- Surveillance & screening in occupational health -- Biologic monitoring -- CBRNE preparedness -- Responder safety and health -- Section VI: Environmental health -- Principles of environmental health -- International occupational & environmental health -- Pediatric environmental health -- Climate change and worker health: implications for clinical practice -- Air pollution -- Water pollution -- Industrial emissions, accidental releases, & hazardous waste -- Building-related illness -- Multiple chemical sensitivity -- Health risk assessment -- Appendix. Biostatistics & epidemiology0 a"The book provides a complete guide to common occupational and environmental injuries and illnesses, their diagnosis and treatment, and preventive measures in the workplace and community. Our aim is to help health care professionals understand the complexities of occupational and environmental health issues and provide useful clinical information on common illnesses and injuries. The book contains many new chapters, expanding the coverage of occupational and environmental medicine well beyond that of the earlier editions"--Preface.12aOccupational Diseasesxprevention & control22aEnvironmental Health22aOccupational Health 2aUnited States1 aLaDou, Joseph,d1938-eeditor.1 aHarrison, Robert,d1954-eeditor.  aAUTH00866cam a22002531  450000100100000000300050001000500170001500800410003201000170007304000210009004400180011106000220012910000330015124500900018426000540027430000260032833600260035433700280038033800270040850400790043558300750051465000140058999900090060311820590RDNLM20260206133639.0810725s1926    xxu||||  |||| 00| 0|eng    a   26004443   aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aQX 50bC155b 19261 aCalkins, Gary Nathan,d1869-14aThe biology of the Protozoa,cby Gary N. Calkins ... illustrated with 238 engravings.  aPhiladelphia and New York,bLea & Febiger,c1926.  aix, [17]-623 p.bill.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aBibliography: p. [585]-598; "Special bibliography" at end of each chapter.  aWill not digitizec2026