M0 aengbdanbfinbnorbswe  9England00aW1bLO104510aLogoped Phoniatr Vocol2dnlm00aLogopedics, phoniatrics, vocology.  aOslo ;aBoston :bScandinavian University Press,cc1996-3 aLondon :bInforma Healthcare  av. :bill., ports.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 21, no. 1 (1996)-  aImprint varies.  aPrint issues ceased with v. 39, no. 4 (2009).1 aMEDLINEbv25n1, 2000-1 aPubMedbv25n1, 2000-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aIn English; summaries in English, Finnish and either Danish, Norwegian, or Swedish.  aOfficial journal of the Scandinavian Cooperation Council of Logopedics and Phoniatrics and of the British Voice Association.  aMerger of: Scandinavian journal of logopedics & phoniatrics, and: Voice (London, England).  3v. 21, no. 1 (1996)c20000831fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aLanguage Disorders 2aSpeech Disorders 2aVoice 2aVoice Disorders 2aPeriodical2 aNordisk samarbejdsråd for logopedi og foniatri.2 aBritish Voice Association.0 x1651-202214tScandinavian journal of logopedics & phoniatricsx0803-5032w(DLC)sn 95038079w(OCoLC)3182869714tVoice (London, England)x0966-789Xw(DLC)   93640756w(OCoLC)283828474 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ilog20  aAUTH02621cgm a2200421 a 101585239DNLM20260227154258.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u120525s2012    mdu049|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:17227  a(OCoLC)794961716  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWH 5401 aLandgren, Ola.10aMultiple myeloma and its precursor disease :bthe future is already here /cOla Landgren.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2012]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (49 min.) :bsd., col.).  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's seminar series  aRecorded Apr. 20, 2012.3 a(CIT): NIH Director's Seminar Series  Dr. Landgren received his M.D. in 1995 from the Karolinska Institute (Stockholm, Sweden). Following clinical training as a hematology/internal medicine specialist physician and receipt of a Ph.D. focusing on diagnostics and prognostics in Hodgkin lymphoma (2002) at Karolinska Institute in Sweden, he worked as an attending physician and conducted clinical research on lymphoproliferative malignancies and related precursors. In 2004, he came to the National Cancer Institute, Genetic Epidemiology Branch, DCEG, where he worked as an Investigator before he joined the Medicial Oncology Branch.    Dr. Landgren's major research interests are in the treatment, causation, diagnostics and prognostics, and natural history of multiple myeloma and its precursor condition, monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance (MGUS). He also studies related hematologic malignancies and their precursors states (including chronic lymphocytic leukemia and monoclonal B-cell lymphocytosis (MBL); Waldenstrom's macroglobulinemia and IgM MGUS), as well as myeloproliferative neoplasms. His research focuses on treatment-, host-, disease-, and immune-related factors in the pathway from precursor to full-blown malignancy, and their relation to outcome.  aClosed-captioned.  aTitle from title screen.12aMultiple Myeloma22aMonoclonal Gammopathy of Undetermined Significance 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH director's seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?17227  aAUTH01365cam a22003497a 101484083DNLM20260209161140.0080911s1911    mducf         000 0deng    a(OCoLC)261372096  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1201 no.1400aWF 7bK72c v.4 no.221 aKnopf, S. Adolphusq(Sigard Adolphus),d1857-1940.10aRobert Koch, (December 11, 1843-May 27, 1910.) :bthe father of the modern science of tuberculosis /cby S. Adolphus Knopf.  a[Baltimore? :bs.n.,c1911?]  a9 p., [1] le