00aWE 10300a152.3/34223/eng/202208171 aBeach, Pamela S.,d1977-eauthor.10aMotor learning and development /cPamela S. Beach, Melanie E. Perreault, Ali S. Brian, and Douglas H. Collier.  aThird edition. 1aChampaign, IL :bHuman Kinetics,c[2024]  axix, 499 pages :billustrations, portraits ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes online access.  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aPreface -- Letter to instructors -- Acknowledgments -- Theory and foundational concepts -- Perspectives in motor behavior -- Theoretical constructs in motor behavior -- Information-processing theory -- Understanding movement control -- Skill classification -- Stages of skill acquisition -- Assessing motor learning -- Infant motor development -- Locomotor and stability skills in childhood -- Object control skills in childhood -- Movement in adulthood -- Assessment of gross motor development -- Physical development -- Physical aging -- Knowledge and cognitive constraints -- Psychosocial and affective constraints -- Sociocultural constraints -- Developmental models for instruction -- Prepractice considerations -- Goal setting -- Practice -- Feedback -- Program design.  a"Motor Learning and Development, Third Edition, is an undergraduate text written for students and professionals pursuing careers in physical education, athletic training, early childhood education, gerontology, kinesiology, special education, adapted physical education, primary and secondary education, physical therapy, occupational therapy, and related fields. Motor Learning and Development has undergone a thorough revision since the second edition, including the addition of four new chapters and many new videos illustrating fundamental motor skills, motor milestones, and reflexes, several new ancillaries, increased PowerPoint slides and test bank questions, updated material based on the latest research throughout the textbook, and revised examples throughout the book"--cProvided by publisher.12aMotor Activity22aMotor Skills22aHuman Development22aAge Factors1 aPerreault, Melanie Elizabeth,d1983-eauthor.1 aBrian, Ali Sara,d1978-eauthor.1 aCollier, Douglas Holden,d1953-eauthor.  ihas work:aMotor learning and development (Text)4https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/ontology/hasWork  aAUTH01407cgm a22004454a 101289609DNLM20260227151450.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u061011s2006    mdu069  |||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13096  a(OCoLC)84671893  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWL 102.51 aBean, Bruce.10aIonic mechanisms of spontaneous activity in central neurons /cBruce Bean.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH neuroscience seminar series  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Oct. 31, 2006).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 8 min., 29 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Mar. 6, 2006.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeurons22aCentral Nervous System22aElectrophysiology22aIon Channelsxphysiology 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.) 0aNIH neuroscience seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13096  aAUTH01400cgm a22003974a 101268216DNLM20260227150155.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u060209s2003    mdu124 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:11532  a(OCoLC)1192548458  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWI 4201 aStrober, Warren.10aDemystifying medicine.pInflammatory bowel disease :bmechanisms /cWarren Strober and colleagues.30aInflammatory bowel disease  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2003]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 3, 2007).  aStreaming vide