flections on epi and pandemics and a focus on SARS-CoV-2 and innate immunity 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 49 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded January 25, 2022.3 a(CIT): Demystifying Medicine  Luba Vikhanski is a science writer at the Weizmann Institute of Science in Rehovot, Israel.  She is the author of "Immunity: How Elie Metchnikoff Changed the Course of Modern Medicine."  Vikhanski will discuss how the findings of Metchnikoff, known as the father of natural immunity, sparked an "immunity war" in the mid-19th century.  Robert Gallo is the Homer and Martha Gudelsky Distinguished Professor of Medicine and co-founder and director of the Institute of Human Virology at the University of Maryland School of Medicine in Baltimore.  A winner of two Lasker awards, Gallo is recognized internationally for his co-discovery of HIV as the cause of AIDS during his long tenure at the NIH.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed August 5, 2022).12aMetchnikoff, Elie,d1845-1916.12aImmunity, Innate22aCOVID-19ximmunology22aCOVID-19 Vaccinesximmunology22aPandemics. 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aVihkanski, Luba,espeaker.1 aGallo, Robert C.,espeaker.12aVihkanski, Luba.tDemystifying medicine.pInnate immunity12aGallo, Robert C.tDemystifying medicine.pReflections on SARS-CoV2 pandemic and innate immunity40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44347  aAUTH01605cas a2200493   0177346DNLM20260224111542.0cr|cn#||||||||690430c19699999enkbr p       0    0eng    a0021-9320l0021-9320  aJBSLAR  a(DNLM)J14660000(s)  a(OCoLC)01754471  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9England00aW1bJO56810aJ Biosoc Sci2dnlm00aJournal of biosocial science.30aBiosocial science  aCambridge, Eng. [etc.]bGalton Found