omes (Case study: Lung cancer) Bhadrasain Vikram, M.D., Chief, Clinical Radiation Oncology Branch, NCI Drugs developed as preventive in case of nuclear attack could be used to lessen side-effects from radiation therapy for cancer; comparative effectiveness studies  Richard Maughan, Ph.D., Director of Medical Physics, Penn Medicine High-Tech, Personalized Care: Behind the scenes with proton therapy technology    For more information, visit  http://www.cancer.gov/newscenter.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aNeoplasmsxdiagnostic imaging12aRadiography 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aVikram, Bhadrasain.2 aNational Cancer Institute (U.S.) 0aNCI/Penn Medicine science writers' seminar40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?15386  aAUTH01330cas a2200445   7505414DNLM20260227090917.0cr|cn#||||||||750626c19609999ja  x         0||| 0eng    asn 86009447   a0040-8891l0040-8891  aBTDCAV  a(DNLM)B56660000(s)  a(OCoLC)01606749  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Japan00aW1bBU898H10aBull Tokyo Dent Coll2dnlm04aThe Bulletin of Tokyo Dental College.  aTokyo.3 aTokyo :bTokyo Shika Daigaku  av.billus.  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-    Oct. 1960-1 aMEDLINEbv6n2,Jul. 1965-1 aPubMedbv6n2,Jul. 1965-1 aIndex to dental literaturex0019-3992bv6n2,Jul. 1965-v40n3,Aug. 19990 aOLDMEDLINE  aAlso issued online.  aSupersedes the Ronbun shu of Byorigaku Kyoshitsu, Tokyo Shika Daigaku. 2aDentistry 2aPeriodical2 aTōkyō Shika Daigaku.12tRonbun shuw(OCoLC)5036349740uhttps://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/browse/tdcpublication  aAUTH02799cgm a2200457 i 101673090DNLM20260227155200.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u151203s2015    mdu064|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:19295  a(OCoLC)932587870  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWM 2071 aZarate, Carlos A.,cJr.eauthor.10aRelief from severe depression and suicidal ideation within hours :bfrom synapses to symptoms /cCarlos Zarate. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2015]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 4 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Wednesday afternoon lecture, Astute clinician lecture series ;v18th  aRecorded November 4, 2015.3 a(CIT): Dr. Zarate's current research focus is on developing novel medications for treatment-resistant depression and bipolar disorder. His areas of expertise include biological and pharmacological aspects of mood disorders in adults. Dr. Zarate's group conducts proof-of-concept studies utilizing novel compounds and biomarkers (magnetoencephalography [MEG] and polysomnography [PSG], positron emission tomography, functional MRI and magnetic resonance spectroscopy [MRS]) to identify potentially relevant drug targets and biosignatures of treatment response. A multidisciplinary translational research team conducts the research in the ETPB. In addition, the Branch provides training to develop the next generation of clinical translational researchers. The Astute Clinician Lecture Series:The Astute Clinician Lecture was established through a gift from the late Dr. Robert W. Miller and his wife, Haruko. It honors a US clinician-scientist who has observed an unusual clinical occurrence, and by investigating it, has opened an important new avenue of research.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed December 16, 2015).12aMajor Depressive Disorderxdrug therapy22aAntidepressive Agentsxtherapeutic use22aDrug Discovery22aKetaminextherapeutic use22aSuicidal Ideation 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series.pNIH director's astute clinician lecture ;v18th.40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19295  aAUTH01297cas a22004214a 101157208DNLM20260227090912.0cr|cnu||||||||021017c20039999ts tr p       0    0eng    a  2003243392  a1570-1611l1570-1611  a(OCoLC)52852756  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9United Arab Emirates00aW1bCU822X10aCurr Vasc Pharmacol2dnlm00aCurrent vascular pharmacology.  aSharjah, U.A.E. ;aSan Francisco, CA :bBentham Science Publishers,cc2003-  av. :bill.  aSix no. a year,b2010-  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Mar. 2003)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Mar. 2003-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Mar. 2003-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.12aCardiovascular Diseasesxdrug therapy22aCardiovascular Agentsxpharmacology22aCardiovascular Systemxdrug effects 2aPeriodical0 x1875-62124 uhttp://www.eurekaselect.com/617/journal/current-vascular-pharmacology  aAUTH01683cas a2200517 a 101090552DNLM20260227090909.0m        d        cr|cnu---|||||990820c19999999ii || pos     0   a0eng    asn 99009153 0 a1526-3711l1526-371121  a(OCoLC)42200312  aNSDcNSDdDNLM  ansdpalcdanlmcopyc  9India10aW110a61721310aJ Contemp Dent Pract2dnlm0 aJ. contemp. dent. pract. 4aThe journal of contemporary dental practice04aThe journal of contemporary dental practice.  a[Cincinnati, OH] :bProcter & Gamble Co.,c[1999-2 32009-2010 :aCincinnati, OH :bSeer Pub.3 32011- :a[New Delhi] :bJaypee Brothers Medical Publishers  aSix no. a year,b2009-  aFrequency varies,b1999-2008  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (fall issue, 1999)-  aTitle from issue contents page (viewed Mar. 14, 2001).1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, fall 1999-0 aPubMedbv1n1, fall 1999-1 aIndex medicus  aHTML (electronic journal)  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 12, no. 3 (May/June 2011) (viewed Nov. 28, 2011).12aTooth