7    mdu074|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:22145  a(OCoLC)988587078  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWY 10500aLinking data & research to the bedside :bperspectives on patient acuity and nursing staffing /cCaitlin W. Brennan.1 aLinking data and research to the bedside1 iAt head of title:aWashington Regional Nursing Research Consortium (WRNRC) educaional offering 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2017]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 14 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded February 21, 2017.3 a(CIT): Washington Regional Nursing Research Consortium (WRNRC) Educaional Offering.  Much of the nurse staffing research conducted over the last 20 years focused mainly on large database analyses using hospital-level data, with less of a focus on unit-level context and patient-level demand for care.  In this presentation, the participant will hear the story of one researcher's journey from asking a clinical question at the bedside to conducting outcomes research on patient acuity, nurse assignment decisions, and quality and patient safety in oncology and palliative care populations.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed April 3, 2017).12aNursing Administration Research22aData Interpretation, Statistical22aPatient Acuity22aPersonnel Staffing and Scheduling 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aBrennan, Caitlin W.q(Caitlin Walsh),espeaker.2 aWashington Regional Nursing Research Consortium,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?22145  aAUTH01470cas a2200457 a 101156917DNLM20260204131659.0cr|cn#||||||||021001c20039999iaumr p       0   a0eng    a  20022151290 a1541-9576l1541-957621  a(OCoLC)50704650  aNSDcNSDdGUAd