b2013-  aQuarterly,b1988-  aBimonthly,b<2008> -2012  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (June 1988)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jun. 1988-0 aPubMedbv1n1, Jun. 1988-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  aJointly established by Chinese Center for Disease Control and Prevention (China CDC) and the Coulston International Corporation.  3Vol. 3, no. 1 (MAR 1990)c19900606fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paperxFurther review is required to determine exactly when acid-free paper was first used for this title 2aEnvironment 2aEnvironmental Exposure 2aEnvironmental Health 2aPeriodical2 aZhongguo ji bing yu fang kong zhi zhong xin.2 aCoulston International Corporation.0 x2214-01904 uhttp://www.besjournal.com4 uhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/biomedical-and-environmental-sciences/issues  aAUTH02592cgm a2200445 i 101710188DNLM20260227155728.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u170727s2017    mdu066|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:23381  a(OCoLC)1004447475  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQU 47000aFrom microbial immunity to genome editing /cFeng Zhang. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2017]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (1 hr., 6 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNIH Wednesday afternoon lecture  aRecorded June 28, 2017.3 a(CIT): NIH Director's Wednesday Afternoon Lecture Series  The microbial CRISPR-Cas adaptive immune systems provide archaea and bacteria with a programmable defense against invading nucleic acids. Several years ago, Dr. Zhang and others reported that the effector module from Streptococcus pyogenes CRISPR-Cas9 (SpCas9) could be harnessed for genome editing. Following this work, Zhang's lab has discovered, characterized, and engineered additional Cas enyzmes for use as molecular biology tools. These include a novel class of CRISPR-Cas systems that use RNA-guided RNases, such as Cas13a (C2c2) and Cas13b. Leveraging the natural properties of Cas13a, the lab developed a single-molecule nucleic acid sensing platform termed SHERLOCK, which can be used for rapid pathogen detection and genotyping. Zhang is continuing to explore microbial diversity to identify novel enzymes and systems that could serve as the basis for the development of additional molecular biology tools and applying these tools to tackle complex biological questions.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed September 8, 2017).12aClustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeatsximmunology22aDNA Breaks, Double-Stranded22aDNA-Binding Proteins22aGene Editing 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aZhang, Feng,d1982-espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?23381  aAUTH01708cgmaa22004334a 101267303DNLM20260227144748.0vf|cbahouvf|cjahoucr|cna||||||||060209s2006    mdu064 ||         vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:4259  a(OCoLC)65195193  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aQX 50500aChromatin organization, non-coding RNAs, and dosage compensation in drosophila /cOffice of Research Services, Medical Arts and Photography Branch.  aUnited States.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  a1 videocassette of 1 (Betacam SP) (1 hr., 3 min., 9 sec.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3duplication copy.  a1 videocassette of 1 (VHS) (1 hr., 3 min., 9 sec.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.3viewing copy.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aNIH director's Wednesday afternoon lecture series  aMitzi I. Kuroda.  aPresented Jan. 25, 2006.  aAlso available online.  aThe National Libra