Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2015]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (51 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aNCI's Center for Cancer Research grand rounds  aAccess restricted to HHS only.5DNLM  aRecorded December 4, 2015.3 a(CIT): NCI's Center for Cancer Research (CCR) Grand Rounds Donna L. Berry, PhD, RN, AOCN(r), FAAN is Director of the Phyllis F. Cantor Center for Research at the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute and an Associate Professor of Medicine at Harvard Medical School. Dr. Berry practiced as an oncology nurse specialist prior to receiving her PhD from the University of Washington in Seattle in 1992.  Dr. Berry leads several studies to improve the human experience of having a cancer diagnosis, ranging from making treatment decisions to managing cancer symptoms and side effects.  In 2011, Dr. Berry was the recipient of the Distinguished Researcher Award from the Oncology Nursing Society. The Association of Community Cancer Centers named her as the 2012 recipient of their Annual Clinical Researcher Award.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed Jan. 13, 2016).12aProstatic Neoplasmsxnursing22aPatient-Centered Care 2aLecture 2aWebcast1 aBerry, Donna L.q(Donna Lynn),d1956-espeaker.2 aCenter for Cancer Research (National Cancer Institute (U.S.)),esponsoring body. 0aCCR grand rounds40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?19362  aAUTH01957cgm a22004574a 101463147DNLM20260227152433.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u080102s2007    mdu074|||||||fs|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:14175  a(OCoLC)310072655  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWA 2951 aWilson, James M.,cDr.10aGlobal monitoring for disease outbreaks :bProject Argus /cJames Wilson.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aEmergency preparedness and biodefense seminar series  aTitle from title screen (viewed Feb. 6, 2009).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 14 min. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Nov. 29, 2007.3 a(CIT): Dr. Wilson is a faculty member in the departments of pediatrics, radiology, microbiology and immunology at Georgetown University Medical Center, where he directs Project Argus, a global detection and tracking system for the early detection of biological events.  His presentation will focus on how non-traditional data can be used to detect outbreaks of human, animal and plant diseases.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aBioterrorismxprevention & control22aCivil Defensexmethods22aDisease Outbreaksxprevention & control22aSecurity Measures 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bEmergency Preparedness and Biodefense Interest Group. 0aEmergency preparedness and biodefense seminar series40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?14175  aAUTH01560cas a2200457   7905114DNLM20260202141851.0cr||n|||||||||790607c19789999ug  x p       0    0eng    a0141-9536l0141-9536  a(DNLM)A16700000(s)  a(OCoLC)05199837  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Uganda00aW1bAF51310aAfr Health2dnlm 0aAfrica health00aAfrica health.  aSutton, Eng., :bIPC Middle East Pub. Co.2 aCambridge, UK :bFSG Communications31aKampala, Uganda :bAfrican Centre for Global Health and Social Transformation  av.bill., ports.  aSix no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-    Oct.? 1978-  aHas supplement: Diagnostics in Africa.0 aMEDLINEbSelected citations only0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aIssues for Vol. 24, no. 6 (Sept. 2002)-v. 31. no. 5 (July 2009) also published in Medical education resource Africa. 2aDelivery of Health Care 2aHe