o file (6 hr., 37 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded May 16, 2023.3 a(CIT): The Vivian W. Pinn Symposium honors the first full-time Director of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Office of Research on Women"s Health (ORWH), Dr. Vivian Pinn, and is held every year during National Women"s Health Week. This event serves as a critical forum for experts across sectors to communicate and collaborate for the advancement of women"s health. The title of this year"s symposium is "Menopause and Optimizing Midlife Health of Women." The symposium will discuss the menopausal transition, the accumulation of morbidity after menopause, menopause in special populations, the influence of social determinants of health on the experience of menopause, the use of menopausal hormonal therapy, and interventions to promote healthy aging.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed July 25, 2024).12aMenopause22aWomen's Health22aMiddle Agedxphysiology22aSocioeconomic Factors 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bOffice of Research on Women's Health,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=49307  aAUTH00774cam a22002297i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003500073044001000108060003300118245011700151250001400268264005300282300003000335336002600365337002800391338002700419650004100446710004800487999000900535101606593DNLM20260205121525.0130422s1972    cc a          000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdad20260205dDNLM  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 1768 no.1000aYi liao wei sheng zi liao.nDi 19 hao,pxian de fang zhi /cShanghai di 1 yi xue yuan Hua Shan yi yuan pi fu ke.  aDi 1 ban. 1aShanghai :bShanghai ren min chu ban she,c1972.  a28 pages :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolum