rcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCOVID-19 insights webinar  aAccess restricted to NIH only.  aRecorded October 21, 2020.3 a(CIT): We invite you to join a new biweekly NHLBI webinar series entitled COVID-19 Insights to learn about groundbreaking research focusing on the host response to SARS-CoV-2 infection. This exciting cross-disciplinary series, featuring both NHLBI staff and researchers throughout the scientific community, will enhance NHLBI listeners' understanding of the latest advances in this fast-moving research, especially as they relate to the NHLBI mission.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed November 20, 2020).12aCoronavirus Infectionsxcomplications22aCoronavirus Infectionsxblood22aPneumonia, Viralxcomplications22aPneumonia, Viralxblood22aBlood Coagulation22aThrombosisxcomplications 2aWebcast 2aLecture1 aMiddleton, Elizabeth,espeaker.2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body. 0aNHLBI COVID-19 insights webinar series40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=38869  aAUTH01566cgm a2200457 i 101773037DNLM20260227160331.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u201105s2020    mdu059|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:30337  a(OCoLC)1224228289  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 20.500aSex and gender-based research :byesterday's neglect, tomorrow's opportunity /cAlyson J. McGregor. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2020]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (59 min.)) :bcolor, sound.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aCC grand rounds  aRecorded October 14, 2020.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed November 23, 2020).12aBiomedical Research12aSex Factors22aGender Identity22aSexism22aPatient Selection22aResearch Design 2aLecture