Ebv1n1, Jan 2008-1 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan 2008-  aSubscription required for full-text online access.  aSubscription required for full-text online access.  a"Official journal of American Association of Neurological Surgeons, American Society of Pediatric Neurosurgeons, American Academy of Pediatrics Section on Neurological Surgery."  aFormerly published as a supplement to: Journal of neurosurgery.12aNeurosurgery12aNeurosurgical Procedures22aPediatrics 2aPeriodical2 aAmerican Association of Neurological Surgeons.2 aAmerican Society of Pediatric Neurosurgeons.2 aAmerican Academy of Pediatrics.bSection on Neurological Surgery.0 x1933-071511tJournal of neurosurgeryx0022-3085w(DLC)med47001541w(OCoLC)18003164 uhttps://thejns.org/pediatrics/view/journals/j-neurosurg-pediatr/j-neurosurg-pediatr-overview.xml  aAUTH02951cgm a2200469 i 9918384668706676DNLM20260227162154.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u220426s2022    mdu407|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32290  a(DNLM)CIT:32291  a(OCoLC)1347358809  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWL 704.62 aTackling Pain at NIH: Updates from the Bench, the Clinic, and the New NIH Pain Research Center (Symposium)d(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aTackling pain at NIH :bupdates from the bench, the clinic, and the new NIH Pain Research Center /cNCCIH, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c2022.  a1 online resource (2 streaming video files (6 hr., 47 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aAccess restricted to NIH only.  aRecorded March 31 and April 1, 2022.3 a(CIT): The National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH) Division of Intramural Research is convening a 2-day symposium to learn from and discuss with key stakeholders across NIH the current state and future directions of the intramural pain research program and to highlight current collaborations and discuss future research within the Pain Research Center (PRC). Attendees will hear from NIH IC leadership and clinical and basic researchers across the NIH and will learn about ongoing projects and collaborations that are underway in the PRC.The PRC, with support from the NIH Intramural Research Program (IRP) Director"s Challenge Award, various NIH Institutes and Centers, the Clinical Center, and other contributors and collaborators, serves as a hub for clinical pain research, creating and continuing to develop a pain phenotyping platform to better characterize and understand mechanisms of diverse pain states, and to further develop and test therapies to better manage or prevent the development of chronic pain and opioid abuse. View the agenda and a list of speakers: https://go.usa.gov/xzkrp  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed Oct. 6, 2022).22aNIH Pain Research Center.12aPain Managementxmethods22aChronic Painxtherapy22aBiomedical Research 2aWebcast 2aConference Proceedings2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.),eissuing body.2 aNational Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4501140uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=45013  aAUTH01468cas a2200433 i 101757339DNLM20260227090916.0m     o  d        cr||||||||||||171120c20179999enk|| poo     0    0eng    a  2020243065  a2398-631Xl2398-631X  a(OCoLC)1012398176  aQGQbengerdad20260227cQGQdOCLCFdOCLCQdOCLCAdDNLM  apcc  9England00aW110aBMJ Lead2dnlm00aBMJ leader. 1aLondon :bBMJ Publishing Group Ltd,c[2017]-  a1 online resource  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Vol. 1, issue 1 (April 2017)1 aMEDLINEbv6n1, Mar. 2022-0 aPubMedbv6n1, Mar. 2022-  aArticles are posted as they are ready for publication.  aSome issues have supplements.0 aVol. 1, issue 1 (April 2017); title from journal home page (publisher's website, viewed March 9, 2020).1 aVol. 3, issue 4 (December 2019) (viewed March 9, 2020).12aLeadership22aHealth Care Sectorxorganization & administration 2aPeriodical2 aFaculty of Medical Leadership and Management (Great Britain),eissuing body.40uhttp://bmjleader.bmj.com/  aAUTH01577cas a2200469 a 101154361DNLM20260226074731.0cr#mnu--------020307c20029999at mr p       0    0eng    a  2002262014  a1445-4408l1445-4416  a(OCoLC)48962624  aBUFcBUFdGUAdDNLM  alcanlmcopyc  9Australia00aW1bFU518310aFunct Plant Biol2dnlm00aFunctional plant biology :bFPB.13aFPB  aCollingwood, VIC, Australia :bCSIRO Pub.,cc2002-  aMonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 29, no. 1 (2002)-  aPrint issues ceased with v. 47, no. 12 (2020).  aTitle from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 35, no. 5 (2008).1 aMEDLINEbv46n1, Dec. 2018-0 aPubMedbv46n1, Dec. 2018-  aSome numbers issued in combined form.  aAlso issued online.  aIssued by: Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organization (Australia), in cooperation with the Australian Academy of Science.12aPlant Physiological Phenomena 2aPeriodical2 aCSIRO (Australia)2 aAustralian Academy of Science.0 x1445-441600tAustralian journal of plant physiologyx0310-7841w(DLC)   74645324w(OCoLC)9636444 uhttps://connectsci.au/fp  aAUTH02988cgm a2200397 i 9918230801006676DNLM20260227161346.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u210707s2021    mdu336|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:31788  a(OCoLC)1262796818  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aQW 7002 aExpanding the Scope of Infection and Inflammation Imaging: Past Lessons and Future Prospects (Symposium)d(2021 :cOnline)jauthor.10aExpanding the scope of infection and inflammation imaging :bpast lessons and future prospects /cCenter for Infectious Disease Imaging, Radiology and Imaging Sciences, Clinical Center, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2021]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 36 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded June 10, 2021.3 a(CIT): The purpose of the virtual conference is to bring together experts in the field of molecular imaging from all over the world to present their work and stimulate potential for new research opportunities, with a common overarching goal of better understanding the basic biology and pathogenesis of infection and inflammation in living subjects, using advanced molecular imaging technologies.  The symposium will focus on the potential of molecular imaging to provide earlier diagnosis of infectious pathologies thus improving patients" care and prognosis, as well as assess, non-invasively, the effectiveness of various therapies and preventative measures, such as vaccines. We will also discuss the potential use of immunoPET to target immune cell markers in infection and inflammation.  Featured speakers:      Matthias Miederer, Mainz University; Patrick A Hughes, The University of Adelaide; Dorian McGavern, NINDS, NIH; Carolyn Anderson, University of Missouri; Sanjay Jain, JHMI; David Wilson, UCSF; Xiankai Sun, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center; Yong Li, Stony Brook University; Andrei Iagaru, Stanford University; Milos Petrik, Palacky University Olomouc; Jan Maarten van Dijl, University Medical Center Groningen; Christopher R. Thornton, University of Exeter; Henry Vanbrocklin, UCSF; Dima Hammoud, NIH; Ian Crozier, IRF, NIAID; Camilo Ruiz-Bedoya, JHMI.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online resource; title from title screen (viewed August 2, 2021).12aInfectionsxdiagnostic imaging22aInflammationxdiagnostic imaging 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aCenter for Infectious Disease Imaging,eorganizer,esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=42018  aAUTH02418cgm a22004694a 101310932DNLM20260227152116.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070703s2007    mdu000 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13911  a(DNLM)CIT:13917  a(DNLM)CIT:13918  a(OCoLC)165047510  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 58.52 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.).bRecombinant DNA Advisory Committee.10aRecombinant DNA Advisory Committee (RAC) June 2007 /cOffice of Biotechnology Activities.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2007]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed July 13, 2007).  aStreaming video (20 hr., 44 min., 47 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded June 19-21, 2007.3 a(CIT): The RAC is a technical committee whose goal is to consider the current state of knowledge and technology regarding recombinant DNA.  This includes review of human gene transfer trials, and an assessment of the ability of DNA recombinants to survive in nature and the potential for transfer of genetic material to other organisms.  It also considers hypothetical hazards and methods for monitoring and minimizing risks. Approximately one-third of the 15 members do not have scientific expertise but represent public interests and attitudes. This balance is intended to provide a forum for open public debate of social and scientific issues attendant to recombinant DNA research.  The RAC has been overwhelmingly successful in achieving this goal.   For more information, visit the  Recombinant DNA Advisory Committee (RAC) Conference Web Site.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aDNA, Recombinant22aClinical Protocolsxstandards22aGene Transfer Techniques22aSafety Management 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1391140uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?1391740uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13918  aAUTH02890cgm a2200481 i 9918573266406676DNLM20260227162940.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u230302s2022    mdu501|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:32772  a(DNLM)CIT:32778  a(OCoLC)1428107170  aDNLMbengerdad20260227dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW 84.32 aAdvancing the Science of Community-Engaged Health Disparities Research (Workshop)d(2022 :cOnline)jauthor.10aAdvancing the science of community-engaged health disparities research (day 1 & 2) /cNHLBI, NIH. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2022]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (8 hr., 21 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded November 14 & 15, 2022.3 a(CIT): The NHLBI Center for Translational Research and Implementation Science (CTRIS) will host a two-day virtual workshop that focuses on advancing the science of community-engaged health disparities research. The workshop brings together researchers, healthcare providers, community partners, and government officials to discuss lessons learned from NIH-funded community-engaged research, new research methods, and the value of community partner relationships.  Participants will examine the principles, methodologies, and latest developments in community-engaged research. They also will explore how the application of this research can help reduce health disparities and promote health equity. Panel sessions will highlight:  Lessons learned from NIH-funded community engaged research efforts, such as the Community Engagement Alliance Against COVID-19 Disparities (CEAL) Novel methodologies and advancements that are shaping the future of community-engaged heath disparities research.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on online research; title from title screen (viewed March 11, 2024).12aCommunity-Based Participatory Researchxeconomics22aHealth Status Disparities22aSocioeconomic Disparities in Health22aTranslational Research, Biomedicalxeconomics22aCommunity-Institutional Relations22aHealth Equity 2aConference Proceedings 2aWebcast2 aCenter for Translation Research and Implementation Science,esponsoring body.2 aNational Institute on Minority Health and Health Disparities (U.S.),esponsoring body.40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=4650740uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=46509  aAUTH01267cas a2200445 a 8708558DNLM20260227091020.0cr|cn ||||||||870723c19879999enk x p       0    0eng    asn 87026331   a0268-960Xl0268-960X  aBLOREB  a(DNLM)SR0058216(s)  a(OCoLC)15800424  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9England00aW1bBL661L10aBlood Rev2dnlm00aBlood reviews.  a[Edinburgh ; New York] :bChurchill Livingstone,c[c1987-3 32001- :aLondon :bElsevier  av. :bill.  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Mar. 1987)-  aTitle from cover.  aImprint varies.1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, 1987-1 aPubMedbv1n1, 1987-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3(1988)c19890818fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aHematology 2aPeriodical0 x1532-16814 uhttp://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/0268960X  aAUTH01338cgm a2200409 a 101574453DNLM20260227154210.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u111208s2011    mdu049|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:16916  a(OCoLC)774949099  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aWH 2001 aLeavings, Megan.10aMolecular control of regulatory T cell function /cMegan Leavings.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2011]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (49 min.) :bsd., col.).  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aImmunology Interest Group semi