dnlm00aObere extremität.  aDarmstadt :bSteinkopff31aBerlin :bSpringer Medizin  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 2006.  aDescription based on: Bd. 2, Heft 2 (Juni 2007); title from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Bd. 2, Heft 4 (Dez. 2007).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aIn German; abstracts also in English.12aUpper Extremityxsurgery 2aPeriodical2 aDeutsche Vereinigung für Schulter- und Ellenbogenchirurgie.0 x1862-66024 uhttps://link.springer.com/journal/11678  aAUTH02191cgm a22004334a 101296483DNLM20260227151811.0m        z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u070103s2006    mdu066 ||||||fs   vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:13566  a(OCoLC)84729820  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States10aQU 58.51 aButte, Atul J.10aExploring genomic medicine using integrative biology /cAtul Butte.  a[Bethesda, Md. :bNational Institutes of Health,c2006]  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aTitle from screen banner (viewed Jan. 30, 2007).  aStreaming video (1 hr., 5 min., 49 sec. : sd., col.).  aRecorded Dec. 19, 2006.3 a(CIT): The past 10 years have led to a variety of measurements tools in molecular biology that are nearly-comprehensive in nature. For example, microarrays are one of at least 30 large-scale measurement or experimental modalities available to investigators in molecular biology. Instead of focusing on the cell, or the genotype, or on any single measurement modality, using integrative biology allows us to think holistically and horizontally. A disease like diabetes can lead to myocardial infarction, nephropathy, and neuropathy; to study diabetes in genomic medicine would require reasoning from a disease to all its various complications to the genome and back. To enable such research, we have been studying the process of intersecting genome-scale data sets in molecular biology, such as those from genetics, microarrays, knockout experiments, and many others.  aMode of access: World Wide Web.  aOpen-captioned.12aGenomics22aComputational Biologyxmethods22aMedicine22aMolecular Biologyxmethods 2aLecture 2aWebcast2 aNational Institutes of Health (U.S.)40uhttp://videocast.nih.gov/launch.asp?13566  aAUTH00761nam a2200253 i 45000010017000000030005000170050017000220080041000390400025000800420008001050440010001130600033001232450062001562500013002182640062002313000039002933360026003323370028003583380027003866500028004136500036004416500021004779990009004989919228723506676DNLM20260210085951.0251216s1952    cc a          000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5695 no.1300aMie shu yu fang shu /cDongbei yi xue tu shu chu ban she.  aChu ban. 1aShenyang Shi :bDongbei yi xue tu shu chu ban she,c1952.  a76 pages :billustrations ;c18 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier12aRodent Controlxmethods22aRodent Controlxinstrumentation22aHealth Education  aAUTH00809nam a2200253 i 45000010017000000030005000170050017000220080041000390400025000800420008001050440010001130600032001232450075001552640065002303000039002953360026003343370028003603380027003885000022004156500021004376500026004587100062004849990009005469919228723206676DNLM20260219104119.0251216s1960    cc a          000 0 chi    aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9China00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5695 no.600aEr zhen liao fa er xue ma zui /cHangzhou Shi hong shi zi hui yi yuan. 1a[Hangzhou] :b[Hangzhou Shi hong shi zi hui yi yuan],c1960.  a15 pages :billustrations ;c19 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aTitle from cover.12aAcupuncture, Ear22aAcupuncture Analgesia2 aZhejiang Sheng Zhong xi yi jie he yi yuan,eissuing body.  aAUTH00856nam a2200301 i 4500001001700000003000500