 B. A., and Rudolf Kottenhahn.  aBoston, New York [etc.]bD. C. Heath and companyc[1939]  axiv p., 1 l., 813, 687 p.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aOn cover: Heath's new German dictionary.  aFirst edition, compiled by Elizabeth Weir, published in 1888.  aPublished also by D. C. Heath & co. under title: Heath's German and English dictionary, and by Funk and Wagnalls company under title: Cassell's new German-English dictionary.  a"The present edition, 1939, is a new version of the dictionary, revised, enlarged, re-edited and reset, of which the two parts were issued separately in 1936 and 1939."  aEnglish language / dictionaries - German  aGerman language / dictionaries - English1 aWeir, Elizabeth.1 aLepper, John Herron,d1878-  a(DNLM)121243-nlmdb  aAUTHb19810622cREVd20260219  aWDN02022dgm a2200373 i 991897595960667620260212095053.0m     o  z f      cr|cna||||||||vz|czaz|u250104s2024    mdu348|||||||fo|||vleng    a(DNLM)CIT:35383  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM0 aeng  apcc  9United States00a2024 BRAIN neuroAI workshop /cOffice of the Brain Director, NINDS. 1a[Bethesda, Md.] :b[National Institutes of Health],c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 streaming video file (5 hr., 48 min.)) :bcolor, sound  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aRecorded November 13, 2024.3 a(CIT): NIH BRAIN NeuroAI Workshop to inform and coordinate future BRAIN research strategies and priority areas to build on recent scientific advances at the intersection of neuroscience and artificial intelligence, an emerging field known as "NeuroAI". This exciting research area is re-examining the fundamental principles of cognition, neural control, and intelligent behavior that may be shared by living organisms and AI systems. Convergent approaches in NeuroAI include data-driven modeling and representational analysis of neural systems; neuromorphic engineering of computing devices and neural interfaces; and new frameworks for understanding how modern AI systems learn and construct knowledge.<p></p><p>For more information visit&nbsp;https://n4solutionsllc.com/brainneuroai/</p>.  aClosed-captioned.  aDescription based on NIH CIT Videocast website; title from title screen (viewed [date] ). 2aWebcast40uhttps://videocast.nih.gov/watch=55262  pP2eEFa20250104  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  aCITRELb20250104  aWTC00914dam a22002775i 450000100100000000500170001000800410002704000250006804100080009304400180010106000330011910000310015224500910018326400550027430000210032933600260035033700280037633800270040450000770043193500240050899200210053299300250055399400250057899500250060399900080062810177238820260218114505.0201014r18811881scu           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLM0 aeng  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5500 no.191 aLegaré, Thomas,eauthor.10aObservations on epidemic of scarlet fever at Charleston, S. C., in the spring of 1881. 1aCharleston, S.C. :bEdward Perry, Printer,c[1881]  a8 pages ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aReprinted from American medical bi-weekly, New York, September 10, 1881.  a(DNLM)1772388-nlmdb  pH3eELa20201014  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  a[CAT ONLY]bYYYYMMDD  aWTC00788dam a22002533i 4500001001700000005001700017008004100034035002600075040002000101041000800121044001800129100004400147245002400191264005500215300002000270336002600290337002800316338002700344500005700371500006100428947001300489992002100502999001100523991907847160667620260130144119.0250813r18851885pau           000 0 eng    a(DNLM)IDX:11201881070  aDNLMbengcDNLM0 aeng  9United States1 aRichardson, Joseph Gibbons,d1836-1886.10aAddress in hygiene. 1aPhiladelphia :b[publisher not identified],c1885.  a23 pages ;c8vo